window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS=(window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1 | The Three Wives","paragraphs":["\"Life is never made unbearable by circumstances, but only by lack of meaning and purpose.\" — Victor Frankl","___","[10,000x Investment Multiplier System]","[Requirement for System Integration: Minimum of 0.1 Affection (1/3)]","The evening sky glowed orange as the sun set. Its rays reflecting off the roof of a small bungalow building in an urban neighborhood.","In front of this building was a limousine and five people.","\"Here is the house key deed, the key, and ten thousand dollars. The Ashford family will no longer have anything to do with you as of this moment. Do we understand each other?\"","Dexter opened his mouth.","The butler didn’t wait for Dexter to speak, nor did he offer a parting glance. He simply stepped back into the black limousine, leaving nothing behind but the faint smell of premium exhaust.","Dexter stood there, staring blankly.","He looked down at the key in his palm. It was faded and worn, as though a hundred people had used it.","Dexter was born into the wealthy Ashford Family by a slave mother who died during childbirth.","To make matters worse he was born with an F-rank mana affinity which he would never become a hero and was destined to be a nobody.","He was hidden away and abandoned, treated like a slave in the Ashford family where he was supposed to be royalty until today when he signed the condition for his freedom from the family.","He didn’t know what it was but he was desperate to escape the family’s influence, so he signed the contract.","But how could he have known that the condition was getting married to the three famous cripples in the entire city.","He turned around and behind him were three women dressed in white wedding gowns.","When he married them thirty minutes ago, it still felt like he was living in a nightmare.","Escaping one family only to be involved with three other families?","’ Did I jump from frying pan straight into fire?’","He hated this situation. He had been helpless all his life. Finally escaping only to be tied down once more... it was hell.","He turned around to finally take a look at his three ’wives’.","The lady who was in a wheelchair, in the middle of the others is called: Mira Calloway.","From the wealthy Calloway family, she’s permanently paralyzed from the neck down.","She has flaming red hair, crimson eyes and a tiny mole beneath her nose.","She looked like the picture perfect painting of a sun goddess as she sat there with a blank expression on her face.","Three Years ago, she was called the Crimson-Valkyrie.","Born with an S rank mana affinity and an A rank Crimson Flame-heart talent. She battled monsters through countless dungeons, becoming one of the youngest B-rank heroes in the city.","However, tragedy struck when three families joined forces to explore a wild S-Rank dungeon under the Ashford Family’s jurisdiction.","Due to a grave miscalculation by the Ashford family, the dungeon was classified as S-Rank when it was, in fact, an SSS-Rank dungeon.","The expedition ended in catastrophe, leaving her crippled and her meridians completely shattered.","To Mira’s left, stood a tall, slender woman with dark hair cascading past her shoulders.","The second wife, Lyra Vance of the influential Vance family, was once a prodigy in her own right.","Born with B-rank mana affinity, she had awakened an A-rank ability known as Shadow World and rose rapidly to become one of the fastest individuals to attain C-rank hero status.","Since it was a joint family expendition, it included her family. She had been present in the dungeon alongside Mira when the incident occurred.","Since then, her vocal cords had been ruptured and her eardrums destroyed, leaving her unable to speak or hear.","In her prime, she was known as Aurelyx: The Shadow Saintess .","It was rumored that she has two faces. She could be smiling at you and then next second wish to kill you just like that.","At this moment, she currently stared at Dexter with an unreadable expression, just as one would stare at a strange painting.","To Mira’s right stood the third lady, Selene Frost from the prestigious Frost noble family.","Born with an A rank mana affinity and S rank Eternal Ice Winter ability. She became an A-rank hero and also was in the same SSS rank dungeon when she became blind and chronically ill.","Selene’s skin was pale, almost translucent and she wore a thin cardigan over her wedding dress that did nothing to hide how much she was shaking.","’ They must be freezing.’","That was his first thought.","He walked to the rusty iron gate, fumbled with the key and finally got it open. He went to the women.","He moved behind Mira’s wheelchair first. Then he reached out and gently caught the hem of Selene’s sleeve.","\"It’s cold out here. Let’s head inside.\"","His voice came out rougher than he intended. He cleared his throat.","The moment his fingers touched her sleeve, Selene flinched as she yanked her arm away.","Dexter’s jaw tightened and he frowned.","’ What the hell?’","He could feel the evening cold through his suit which meant she had to be freezing.","Out of the corner of his eye, he saw a curtain twitch in the house across the street which meant that the neighbors were already watching. If someone took a photo of them and posted it on the internet, this place would turn into something else.","’ Since I can’t touch her, maybe Lyra would .’ He said in thought and then brought out his phone, opened the notes app, and typed in a big font.","[Take her hand. Let’s head inside. It’s too cold.]","He held the screen in front of Lyra’s face. Her dark eyes focused on the text, then looked up at Dexter.","She stared at him for what seemed to be a minute and then slowly nodded.","Then she stepped toward Selene. Her hand hovered near Selene’s arm for a moment. Selene seemed to have noticed it. She brought her arm forward and Lyra’s fingers settled around Selene’s wrist.","Dexter sighed and then gripped the handles of Mira’s wheelchair.","He wheeled her up the path, while Lyra guided Selene behind them in silence. The front door got stuck, making Dexter put his shoulder into it to open.","The smell of dust and old wood escaped the house. He tapped at the wall with his fingers and found the switch, lighting up the entire house.","The bungalow was small but structurally sound. A previous owner had left behind three sagging sofas, an old television, a wooden dining table with five chairs, and a shelf of dusty paperbacks.","The wallpaper was also peeling at the corners.","He left the three women in the living room and went to check the bedrooms.","It was two rooms. One was slightly larger than the other. Each contained a bed frame with a bed, a nightstand, and a window with iron bars and dirty curtains.","’ Two rooms and four people .’ Dexter thought.","It would be logical for two people to sleep in one room but nothing about this night was logical.","’I can only use the small room, merge the two beds together for the three of them to sleep.’","The beds were large enough for two people to sleep on so two combined beds should be more than enough to house the three women.","He found some extra blankets in a closet that smelled like mothballs and spread them out to cover the gap between the mattresses.","His own room was now empty. Luckily, he found a hand-crank air mattress in a storage closet, pumped it up, and threw a blanket over it.","’This should be alright for tonight. Tomorrow, I will make other arrangements.’ Dexter muttered to himself.","When he returned to the living room, the girls were exactly where he’d left them. No one had moved an inch just like barbie dolls.","\"I set up the beds,\" he said, leaning against the doorframe. \"You guys can head in and get some sleep.\"","Dexter was about to leave when he saw no one answered him","He frowned in frustration ’Why aren’t they—’","And then it hit him.","One couldn’t hear him, the other couldn’t see and the third couldn’t move.","Dexter gritted his teeth and without a word, he turned and walked back to his bedroom.","He needed five minutes. Just five minutes to sit in silence and not think about the fact that he had been disowned, married to three strangers, and left in a crumbling house with ten thousand dollars and no plan.","---","About an hour later, he came back.","He had washed his face with cold water from the kitchen tap and had calmed down a bit.","He typed a new note on his phone:","[Let’s go to bed. Bring Selene with you. I’ll handle Mira.]","He held it in front of Lyra. Her eyes focused once more. Then she looked at him, making Dexter a bit uncomfortable, but she eventually nodded her head.","She went to Selene and guided her toward the bedroom, one hand on Selene’s elbow, the other on the small of her back.","Dexter walked over to Mira.","She was still in her wheelchair. She hadn’t looked at him once since the wedding.","He crouched in front of her. \"I’m going to pick you up now.\"","Her eyes trembled but she said nothing as Dexter lifted her up.","She was really light as though she hadn’t been eating.","He carried her through the doorway and into the bedroom. Lyra had already settled Selene on the far side of the bed. He lowered Mira on the empty side of the bed.","Mira’s head suddenly turned as she looked directly at him for the first ever. Her ember eyes were extremely dull.","\"You know,\" she suddenly spoke. Her voice was like a thousand sirens singing \"It’s our wedding night.\"","Dexter was at first stunned. Not because of her voice but because one of them was finally willing to speak to him.","He glanced at her and said nothing","She continued. \"You can do whatever you want to me. I’m completely paralyzed and won’t be able to resist you at all.","Dexter was stunned.","’I still don’t know whether to be happy now that I’ve finally escaped my family or be sad that I’ve gotten entangled with three.’","Right now, he was feeling something but it was definitely not lust.","But now that she mentioned it...","Dexter felt heat crawl up the back of his neck. But he kept his face still.","Mira of course she saw it. Her lips curled into a cold smile.","\"Or... did you want all three of us? Don’t worry. One is blind and won’t know if you’re small. And the other can see everything, but she can’t tell a soul.\" Mira chuckled coldly.","\"Convenient, isn’t it?\"","On the far side of the bed, Selene reached into her sleeve to pull out a slightly bruised apple","and began to munch on it gently.","Dexter rolled his eyes.","\"Save the reverse psychology,\" he said flatly. \"I wasn’t planning on anything. Even if I wanted to do it, it certainly won’t be with someone who can’t move.\"","The room suddenly went silent and a flicker of amusement flashed in Mira’s eyes.","Selene had stopped chewing as she froze there on the bed.","Dexter exhaled through his nose and rubbed the back of his neck.","\"I don’t plan to do anything to you guys either. I like my women taking the initiative so just... sleep. We’ll figure the rest out tomorrow.\"","He didn’t wait for a response. He hit the light switch, plunging the room into darkness and closed the door.","Dexter rested in his room massaging his forehead","’How the hell am I supposed to take care of three people when I can barely take care of myself?’"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2 | Life With Three Ex-Heroines","paragraphs":["\" When fate hands you three lemons, make three cups of lemonade.\" — Dale Carnegie","—-","Dexter tried sleeping but it refused to claim him just like his father...","Eventually, he ended up cultivating through the night. The Starlight Meditation Technique extracts mana from the sun and the stars to increases one’s cultivation level.","Hero levels are graded: Awakened Hero also called Meta Heroes (1 to 12), Super Hero (1 to 12), Ultra Hero (1 to 12), Transcendent (Initial, Mid, Advance, Peak), Supreme (Initial, Mid, Advance, Peak), and Legend.","But Dexter possesses the lowest mana affinity: F rank, even comparable to an ordinary human. Absorbing mana to him is like trying to catch a fish with greasy hands, mana slips away.","But the meditation itself had another benefit, it clears one’s mind. By the time it was morning, he felt relaxed, calm and refreshed.","He stood up and stretched.","\"Pop!\"","His spine popped, then he went to the bathroom.","The hot water thankfully worked. He turned the tap and let it run until steam curled up from the basin, fogging the mirror.","He brushed, showered quickly, dressed in a grey t-shirt and dark joggers then padded to the kitchen on bare feet.","The kitchen was small and outdated, but functional. He opened the cupboards, found rice, a few eggs, some dried mushrooms, and a bottle of soy sauce.","Then he remembered the wedding gift boxes still out in the entrance. Luckily they had a gate.","He dragged them into the kitchen and started unpacking.","Most of it was useless jewelry, he found practical items though: bags of dried grains, canned soups, instant noodles, tea, and a small container of brown sugar.","He cooked. Rice porridge with dried mushrooms and soft-boiled egg on the side.","While it simmered, he set the small dining table. Four bowls, four spoons, four cups of hot tea.","Then he went to the master bedroom.","The door was open and Mira was already in her wheelchair, parked near the window, staring at nothing.","Her hair was tangled around her face, and her wedding dress was wrinkled.","Selene was still in bed, lying on her back, her eyes open and fixed on the ceiling, looking like she hadn’t moved all night.","Lyra was sitting upright at the edge of the mattress, with her hands folded neatly in her lap.","Dexter typed on his phone and held it out to Lyra:","[Breakfast is ready. Can you help Selene to the table?]","Lyra read the message. But instead of nodding, she hesitated. She raised one hand and pointed a slender finger at her own mouth.","Dexter blinked in confusion. \"What?\"","She pointed again.","\"Oh! Sorry!\"","They hadn’t brushed their teeth, washed their faces or bathed yet.","He pressed his lips together and typed:","[Hold on. Two minutes.]","Going back to the gift boxes and dug through them. Toothbrushes—still in packaging. Toothpaste. Two bars of soap. A bottle of lotion. A comb. He gathered everything up, carried it to the bedroom, and set it on the nightstand.","He unpackaged an electric toothbrush, applied toothpaste, and held it out to Lyra. She took it. Their fingers briefly brushed and it was ice cold making Dexter raise an eyebrow.","Gave Selene another and then turned to Mira.","\"Open your mouth.\"","Mira’s eyes narrowed. \"Excuse me?\"","\"Open. Your mouth.\"","\"You can’t just—\"","Mid sentence, Dexter slid the toothbrush between her teeth and flicked it on.","Mira’s eyes went wide, then narrowed into a glare so sharp it could have cut diamond. She sat there with indignation as toothpaste foam was gathering at the corner of her lips.","Dexter felt happy for shutting her up and grinned.","He held up a small basin. \"Spit.\"","She spat hard, making a bit of foam splash and land on his wrist.","\"I thought you might prefer your women to swallow,\" Mira said with disdain. \"Guess I was wrong.\"","Dexter was stunned. ’ This girl is crazier than I thought!’ He shook his head and brought a bottle of water to her mouth.","\"Rinse.\"","She smirked but opened her mouth to drink the water and rinsed then spat it out.","He took the toiletries to the bathroom, washed his hands, and came back. He stood in front of her wheelchair and asked.","\"Do you need help with the restroom, or do you want to bathe first?\"","Mira didn’t look at him. She stared at the wall beside her. \"I’m paralyzed, in case you hadn’t noticed. Or do you see a pair of working legs I don’t know about?\"","Dexter chuckled. \"Will tell Lyra to assist you.\"","Dexter was about to leave when he heard a small voice. \"D-don’t.\"","Dexter stopped dead in his tracks and frowned.","’ What does she mean by ’don’t?’ Does she actually want me to do it myself? Hell no.’","She had practically called him a pervert last night, if he did this, he would be a true pervert in her eyes.","He was about to reject but as he saw her sitting unmoving, face down and looking all sad.","’ Ah! Fuck me!’","He cursed in his mind and inhaled sharply, unlocked Mira’s wheelchair and pushed her through the hallway.","The bathroom was small with a toilet, a sink, and an old cast-iron bathtub with clawed feet. He’d scrubbed it earlier that morning while the water was heating.","\"Toilet or bathtub first?\"","She replied in a quiet voice. \"Toilet,\"","She was still wearing the wedding dress. Dexter knelt in front of her, wrapped one arm around her waist, and lifted. Her body pressed against his chest and it was warm. He could feel breasts and even count her ribs through the cloth.","Dexter’s expression didn’t change and with his free hand, he found the zipper at the back of her dress and pulled it down.","Underneath, she wore a plain sports bra and cotton briefs. Her skin was pale, milky and ungodly smooth.","\"Do you like what you see?\" Her voice cracked slightly.","Dexter scoffed. \"I’ve seen thousands of beautiful women on Cornhub. What makes you think yours is special?\"","\"Y-you!\"","Mira’s face flushed red in anger but Dexter suddenly removed her panties and placed her securely on the toilet so she wouldn’t fall.","\"I’m going to step out now just call me when you’re done.\"","He pulled the door halfway shut and left to pick up underwear and a dress for her. He saw a flowery gown and smiled. \"Perfect.\"","---","About fifteen minutes later, Mira spoke in a quiet voice. \"I’m done.\"","Dexter entered. He wouldn’t let his gaze linger anywhere it shouldn’t and pressed the button on the smart toilet. The water hissed and Mira stared strangely at it but she said nothing.","When she was clean, Dexter lifted her again and suddenly unclasped her sports bra, keeping his gaze fixed firmly on the tile above her head, and gently lowered her into the warm water.","He washed her hands first, her arms, her shoulders and her legs, lathering shampoo into her scalp, rinsing it with a cup. She sat in the tub with her eyes closed, her face turned away, her ears burning red.","He lifted her out, wrapped her in a towel, and patted her dry. Then he picked up the flowery sundress he’d found in her luggage.","\"I hate this dress,\" Mira said. Her voice was tight.","Dexter smirked. \"I know. That’s why I picked it.\"","Mira instantly glared daggers at him. But she couldn’t stop him and could only watch as he put it on her.","He helped her back into the wheelchair and pushed her to the kitchen table.","Meanwhile, Lyra had successfully helped Selene wash up in the other bathroom,","and the two of them were already seated.","Dexter ladled the hot porridge into four bowls.","Lyra gently took Selene’s hand, guiding her fingers to the handle of the spoon until Selene was able to eat on her own.","Mira took a small bite, chewed slowly, and looked up. \"It doesn’t actually taste half bad.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"Was that... a compliment?\"","\"Don’t push your luck.\" She retorted drily and went back to eating.","They ate in silence but it was too late when Dexter realized Lyra had consumed more than four people’s worth of porridge.","’ How’s this possible? Her body is so thin. Where did all that food go?’","He was stunned.","Lyra noticed him staring and she glanced with her causal expression. But a flush crept up her neck. She was embarrassed but didn’t want to show.","’ That was supposed to be our lunch.’","He shook his head, and grabbed his phone, typing.","[It was supposed to be lunch but it’s alright. I will cook more now.]","He held the screen out to her. She read it and looked up at him then hesitantly nodded.","After breakfast, Dexter cleared the table and started washing dishes.","\"The great heir of the Ashford family, washing dishes.\" Mira’s voice sounded out as she mocked.","Dexter rinsed a bowl and set it on the rack. \"I’m sure you and your family were quite shocked when you realized I was the one you married and not the legitimate heir. Can’t believe the three great families got scammed. Haha.\"","Mira eyes twitched and she was suddenly speechless.","Of course Dexter knew the families had been scammed. According to the contract, the three families were promised marriage to the first born of Ashford family, but ended up getting scammed as the bastard son is the first born.","The three families thought it would be easy to form ties with the Ashford family, not knowing it was a trap all along.","Suddenly, a sharp gasp sounded out.","Dexter turned around, Selene was trembling violently on the sofa. The temperature in the room started dropping fast as frost spread across the floorboards, climbing the walls, creeping across the coffee table.","’I read in the file that she’s chronically ill. I didn’t expect it to be this bad.’","’ Fuck! Where did I place the medicine her family dropped?’","He panicked and he ran to the hallway where they’d stacked the medical supplies. Quickly unlocked a box with two syringes in it. He took one.","The air around Selene was so cold his fingers went numb the moment he crossed into the frost radius. Ice crystals formed on his eyelashes but he pushed through it, bent down and quickly stabbed the syringe into her.","Nothing happened at first, then the frost stopped spreading as the ice finally cooled.","Dexter grabbed every blanket he could find and wrapped them around her as the tremor slowly faded.","From the doorway, he saw Mira and Lyra.","However, neither of them spoke.","Selene drifted into an exhausted sleep. Her face was ghost-pale, her lips still faintly blue.","---","A few hours after the morning crises, Dexter was lost in thought.","And went to the kitchen, the porridge was gone, the eggs were finished and the dried grains nearly gone. With Lyra’s appetite, they’d burn through what little remained by dinner.","He found Mira in the living room and crouched in front of her wheelchair.","\"I need to go to the market. I’ll be back within an hour. Don’t open the door for anyone.\"","Mira raised an eyebrow. \"Yes, master. Shall I have dinner ready when you return, master?\"","\"Very funny. Don’t open the door.\"","He told Lyra the same thing via text, made sure Selene was still sleeping comfortably, and left.","---","The corner store was three blocks away. Dexter kept his head down as he moved. He needed rice, vegetables, cooking oil, salt, maybe some meat if it was available.","The shopkeeper stared at him for a while.","\"You’re quite popular but I can’t seem to remember where I know you from.\"","The man’s eyes lit up. \"Yeah! From the news. They mention you as the hidden son of the Ashford family.\"","Then the old man frowned and glanced at Dexter. \"Come to think of it, it wasn’t hidden son, it was bastard son. You’re the one that scammed three girls to get married to you hmm?\"","The shopkeeper sneered in disgust.","’ How did the news get out so fast?’","Dexter frowned and simply greeted the shopkeeper.","\"Morning,\" Dexter said. He started gathering items. \"Rice. Two kilos. Cabbage. Carrots. Cooking oil. Salt. And whatever pork you have that’s—\"","\"We’re low on pork,\" the shopkeeper interrupted, leaning against the counter. \"Prices have gone up.\"","Dexter paused, his eyes narrowed at the shopkeeper.","\"How much?\"","\"10 dollars per pound.\"","Dexter’s face turned black.","\"That’s twice the market price,\"","\"Inflation.\" The shopkeeper shrugged. \"Take it or leave it.\"","Dexter stared at him for a long moment. The man didn’t blink. He knew he had Dexter cornered. Everyone in this neighborhood probably knew by now and might even be worse.","Dexter paid. He counted out the bills, placed them on the counter, and left immediately with his things.","On his way back, he saw a medicine store.","Dexter hesitated but eventually entered the store. He purchased Selene’s suppression medicine which cost 500 dollars per syringe, he bought a week’s worth."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3 | System Awakening!","paragraphs":["\"The afterglow of a battle is always sweeter than the victory itself.\" — Oscar Wilde","Dexter got home within the hour.","When he opened the door, he saw his wives in the living room, Lyra and Mira were staring into space as usual and Selene was still asleep on the old couch.","Their eyes didn’t even move to him when he entered as they remained in their own world.","’ Can’t imagine what they must be feeling.’","Afterall, they were previously at the peak of their lives but now, the had all been tossed to a useless person.","Dexter shook his head and calculated how much he had left and it was about 5000 dollars.","At this rate, they’d be broke in two weeks. Maybe less.","He dropped the pen and rubbed his face.","---","That evening, Dexter sat alone in the small backyard. The sky was dark and the neighborhood hummed with distant sounds of televisions, arguments, a baby crying.","He crossed his legs, closed his eyes, and cultivated.","The meditation technique drew ambient mana into his body but he couldn’t absorb it. Like a bucket fetching water from a well.","His thought began to wander and landed on money. He needed money if he wanted to make it through this month.","He needed a job. But with F-rank ability, no formal combat training, and the stink of the Ashford disgrace, no legitimate guild or company would touch him. The only work available was low-level Dungeon Porters and Scouts.","Even that required a basic hero license. And a hero license required clearing at least one dungeon.","Dexter opened his eyes and stared at the sky. A single star poked through the haze.","’ Tomorrow ,’ he thought. ’ I’ll figure it out tomorrow.’","---","The next morning, Dexter prepared a simple breakfast, rice porridge again, with pickled vegetables and tea. He was setting the table when three heavy knocks rattled the front gate.","’Are the neighbors finally getting friendly?’","Dexter set down the teapot. He looked at his three wives and spoke.","\"Stay here.\"","He walked out the door and opened the gate.","The moment he opened the door, a huge man burst through the door and entered the gate.","The one in front was a tall dude built like a door with a white beard. He wore a leather jacket.","Seeing him, Dexter felt his mana wave.","’Awakened Hero level 3.’","The others were level 2 and 1.","Behind him, three smaller men fanned out, hands in pockets, trying to look casual.","\"Morning,\" the big man said. His grin widened, revealing his gold tooth.","\"Well, well. The bastard prince of the Ashfords. Look at this, boys, this is the closest you can ever get to royalty.\"","He shoved past Dexter without waiting for an invitation and directly entered the house. The three thugs followed, their boots tracking mud across the living room floor.","\"My name’s Kreg,\" the big man said, scanning the living room like a generational thief. \"This territory belongs to us, the Red Fang Crew. Since you’re new here, I’ll explain how things work. You pay us protection fee, monthly and we will protect you from monsters invasions.\"","Dexter’s expression didn’t change.","’ He’s at the Awakened Hero rank level 3 stage. There’s no way I can be his match. surrender is not a sign of defeat. ’","He inhaled and asked. \"How much is the protection fee?\"","Kreg smiled. \"I like smart people a lot.\"","Then he came before Dexter, a head taller than him as he looked down at Dexter as he grinned. \"How about 5,000 dollars for starters.\"","Dexter’s face changed slightly. \"That’s impossible. I don’t have 5,000 dollars to give.\"","Kreg laughed out loud, his voice booming through the walls.","\"Oh, I think you do.\" He stopped in the middle of the living room. His eyes moved slowly around the room and then landed on the three women.","Mira sat in her wheelchair near the sofa. She met Kreg’s gaze with indifference, as though he were a stain on the wall she couldn’t be bothered to clean. Lyra sat beside Selene, the same indifference while Selene simply stared elsewhere.","\"Word is,\" Kreg said, stepping closer to Dexter, \"the Ashfords gave you a nice little parting gift. Ten grand, right? Cash?\" He cracked his knuckles. \"Protection fee is five thousand. For the first month. After that, we negotiate.\"","Dexter’s fists clenched hard. ’What to do? That cash is all we have. If I give them, we won’t survive for long but if I don’t, these men might do something worse.","\"Take the money and leave,\" Dexter said, pulling the remaining cash envelope","from his pocket. \"It’s all I have.\"","At that moment, Kreg’s men started drifting moving towards the women. One of them licked their lips.","\"Boss, these girls are high-quality. Look at them. We could use them for a while, then sell them to some wealthy clients. Nobles pay top credit for.\"","\"Hahaha. You’re right. Even if they’re broken, we could get a massive price for","them from some of the underground collectors...\"","One of the thugs grabbed Lyra by the jaw, examining her face like checking a dog.","Kreg’s eyes flashed with a sudden, ugly greed as he looked at the three women.","\"They would fetch a pretty penny...\" Kreg murmured, ignoring Dexter.","A surge of white-hot anger hit Dexter. Usually, he was thoughtful and calculating but right now, his sanity vanished.","Before Kreg could finish his sentence, Dexter moved.","He punched the first thug square in the jaw. Turned, kicked the second in the balls and tackled the third one directly to the ground punching his face in!","He had no formal combat training, but he caught them completely off guard.","But the physical disparity was too wide. Dexter was only a level 1 bronze warrior, the lowest level here is level 2.","Before Dexter could land the third punch, the men recovered faster than he had thought","Two of them grabbed him from behind, wrenching his arms behind his back. The third one stood up and immediately punched him in the ribs.","\"Ugh!\"","Kreg stepped forward. His gold tooth gleamed.","\"That was stupid,\" he said, and hit Dexter across the face.","The blow sent blood spilling in the air, staining the floor.","Kreg leaned in. \"What did you think would happen?\"","Dexter looked up at him. Blood trickled from his split lip down his chin. \"Take the money and get out.\"","Kreg sneered and ignored him as he turned toward the women again. \"Why would I leave when there are precious cargo to be secured?\"","Dexter chuckled. \"Do you really think our families will let common thugs touch their daughters without consequences?\"","Kreg’s grin faltered but he recovered it quickly. \"You’ve all been abandoned. They don’t care about you.\"","\"They don’t care about us,\" Dexter nodded in agreement. \"You’re right. They don’t care about us. However, they care about their reputation. If word gets out that some low-life street thugs laid hands on the daughters of the Frost, Vance, and Calloway families, what do you think would happen? \"","\"The only way they could save face would be to make an example. Just wiping your entire crew completely won’t be enough to pacify them. Your families won’t be spared either. Even the bastards.\"","Kreg’s face immediately went pale. He was just a regular thug, nowhere near enough to compete with those massive families.","Suddenly, Kreg drove a fist directly into Dexter’s stomach.","Dexter doubled over as he coughed up blood.","His knees buckled. The men holding him let go, and he dropped to the floor.","Kreg snatched the envelope from Dexter’s pocket.","\"Even if I can’t do anything to the girls, I can still do so many things to you.\"","Kreg muttered and patted Dexter’s face.","\"We’ll be back next month. You better have more money by then.\" He glanced at the women one more time. \"Or we’ll find other ways to collect.\"","\"Let’s go.\"","The thugs laughed and mocked him as they left the house.","---","Dexter lay on the floor for a long moment. Stars speckled his vision and his ribs ached as he breathed.","The girls stared at him with strange expressions on their faces. But Dexter ignored it as he heard a sound.","[Ding!]","Dexter flinched. He looked around. But nothing nearby made that sound.","Suddenly, golden text materialized in the air before his eyes.","’ Could it be?’","’[Requirements have been met.]","[Conditions: Minimum Affection of 0.1 (4/3)]","[Initializing system integration]","[Progress: 0%... 25%... 50%...]","[Progress: 75%... 90%... 100%]","’[Integration Complete. Welcome, Host, to the Ten-Thousandfold Investment Multiplier System.]’","Dexter couldn’t believe it. Ever since the incident when he was 9, the system had been a part of his life.","However, the requirement for activating the system was gaining a miniscule 0.1 affection of at least 3 people. For 10 years, he only managed to gain the affection of a single person.","Now that he’s 19, he had completely given up and had completely forgotten about the system. But now, it the requirement was reached? How?","╔═══════════════════════════════╗","10,000x INVESTMENT MULTIPLIER SYSTEM","╚═══════════════════════════════╝","[Investment Target(s)]: Mira Calloway (Wife), Lyra Vance (Wife), Selene Frost (Wife), Jasmine Constance (Ex-Girlfriend)","[Name]: Dexter Ashford","[Race]: Human","[Talent]: Not Awakened","[Mana Affinity]: F-Rank (Low Grade)","[Rank]: Awakened Hero/ Meta Hero","[Level]: 1","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Attributes]","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","Strength: 25 (Basic human stat is 10)","Agility: 25 (Basic human stat is 10)","Physique: 25 (Basic human stat is 10)","Mana: 20 (Basic human stat is 10)","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Meditation Technique]","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","★ Starlight Meditation Technique [Mortal Grade]","• Increases Mana Absorption","• Improves Mana Recovery","• Accelerates Cultivation Speed","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[System Notice]","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","’[System Note: Invest in your wives. Protect them. Provide for them. Every act of investment; financial, emotional, physical, strategic will yield returns multiplied by your current tier.","Higher investment significance yields greater rewards.","Requirement to upgrade to 100x Multiplier: Kill 10 beings.]","’[System Note: Rewards given directly by the system cannot be reused to trigger a direct investment return. For example, using the 50,000 credits to directly hand over as cash will not trigger a return. However, if you use those credits to purchase items, food, medicine, or assets for your wives, the investment return will trigger.]’","•••","’[Scanning investment...]’","’[Investment detected: Subject sacrificed 100% of liquid assets (5,000 Credits) to neutralize an immediate physical threat to all three investment targets. Accepted physical violence to create a protective barrier. Prioritized target safety over personal welfare.]","Dexter was still stunned when another set of notifications came in.","’[Analyzing target responses...]’","’[Mira Calloway: Emotional disturbance detected — dormant emotional seed planted.]’","’[Lyra Vance: Physiological response detected — cortisol decrease of 12% — a minuscule sense of madness restored for the first time in 6 months.]’","’[Selene Frost: Core temperature elevation of 0.3°C during protective action — frost generation suppressed voluntarily for 3.2 seconds — longest conscious suppression on record.]’","’[Current Multiplier: 10x — Base Tier]’","’[Calculating Returns...]’","’[Calculation Complete.]’","’[Returns Granted:]’","’1. 50,000 Credits — Direct Financial Return (10x original investment of 5,000 Credits).’","’2. Mana Affinity Upgrade: F-Rank → E-Rank.’","’3. Talent Awakening: Enhanced Hearing (E-Rank) (200-meter radius + sound differentiation).’","’4. Cultivation Boost: 10 Months of compressed mana refinement applied.’","’5. Flame Demon Bloodline (Royal Grade).’","[Do you wish to accept Rewards? Y/N]"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4 | Returns: 50,000 Dollars, Talent Awakening &Flame Demon Bloodline","paragraphs":["\"You gave them everything,\" Mira’s flat voice snapped Dexter out of his shock.","He managed to steady himself, leaning his shoulder against the peeling wallpaper of the entryway.","He wiped his mouth with the back of his hand, leaving a dark red smear across his face as he chuckled bitterly.","\"I had no other choice.\"","Mira’s lips curled into a sharp sneer. \"You’re too weak.\"","Dexter’s eyes flashed with irritation and he retorted. \"Pot calling the kettle black.\"","As though she hadn’t heard him, Mira closed her eyes and sunk into her own world.","As for Lyra, she stared at him for a brief moment as though trying to figure something out but then she eventually gave up, turned to stare at the window.","On the other side of the sofa, Selene hadn’t moved a single bit even when the thugs came, it was as though she hadn’t heard anything and remained closed off in her world.","Dexter sighed but didn’t say anything else. While he felt they were disappointed in him, his system told him something else.","Dragging his feet, Dexter made it to his small bedroom and sat cross legged on his airbed.","He closed his eyes and breathed out. The glowing golden text of the system still hovered in his vision, bright and steady in the darkness of his closed eyelids.","```","[Returns Granted:]","1. 50,000 Credits — Direct Financial Return (10x original investment of 5,000 Credits).","2. Mana Affinity Upgrade: F-Rank → E-Rank.","3. Talent Awakening: Enhanced Hearing (E-Rank) (200-meter radius + sound differentiation).","4. Cultivation Boost: 10 Months of compressed mana refinement applied.","5. Flame Demon Bloodline (Royal Grade).","[Do you wish to accept Rewards? Y/N]","```","Dexter stared at the prompt with shivering hands.","He had spent his entire life believing he would always be a useless, unawakened nobody. But these girls he thought were burdens turned out to be the ones to unlock his system.","\"Accept.\"","***","In that instant, a notification rang out on his phone. Dexter took out his Samsung Galaxy 9 out and saw 50,000 dollars had been deposited into his bank account.","\"It’s actually real!?\"","Just as this shock rippled through his mind, an invisible shockwave exploded outward from his chest.","\"BOOM!\"","A violent shockwaves exploded from his body as something within him snapped like massive chains clacking and unlocking all at once.","Dexter’s eyes flew wide open as his body trembled uncontrollably as his heart began to beat with a force of a piston in an engine.","\"Thump! Thump! Thump!\"","The force of the heartbeat was so strong that it sent vibrations down the bed and to the ground.","Every single pore on his skin suddenly opened wide and in that instant, started to suck in the mana in the surroundings like a vacuum.","Gradually, an invisible vortex of mana formed around him as his body rapidly absorbed it like sponge.","The raw energy rushed toward him like a vacuum as mana forced its way into his skin, filling his empty, dry meridians with mana. Just like a dress well finally producing water.","\"Kra-ka-ka!\"","His bones popped, from his toes to his skull. It sounded like a string of firecrackers going off inside his skeleton. Dexter gasped as his muscles began to tighten, and hardening under the sudden influx of raw power.","He felt so light and incredible free. All his life he hadn’t notice just how sluggish and heavy he was.","`[System Notification: Cultivation boost applied. 10 months of compressed mana refinement integrated.]`","`[Host has leveled up: Awakened Hero Level 1 → Level 2!]`","The pain in his ribs began to fade, replaced by a warm, solid pressure.","But before the happiness could fully settle, a sudden, terrifying heat bloomed erupted from within him.","***","The heat grew rapidly and it felt like someone had poured liquid fire directly down his throat.","His eyes widened as steam began to rise from his skin. The blood inside his veins felt as though it had turned into molten lava, bubbling and boiling as it rushed through his newly widened pathways.","’ Damn it! What is this! ?’ Dexter thought, his teeth slamming shut.","He bit his tongue hard, as he fought not to scream in pain.","Sweat poured from his forehead, sizzling as it dripped onto the dusty wood. The pain was intense, consuming every single nerve ending in his body. It felt as though his very cells were being torn apart and rebuilt.","Deep within his chest, his cellular structure was changing. A dark, powerful demonic essence was weaved itself into his human DNA, fusing with his flesh and bone.","Then, just as the heat came, it vanished back and faded into nothing.","A soft wave of hot air burst outward from his body, carrying a faint scent of sulfur and ash, before dissipating into the corners of the room.","\"Huff!\" \"Huff!\" \"Huff!\"","Dexter slumped on his bed and panted heavily. But his eyes shine brilliantly.","```","[System Notification: Flame Demon Bloodline (Royal Grade) successfully integrated.]","[All basic attributes have received a permanent +2 bonus.]","[Bloodline Profile: Flame Demon Bloodline]","Grade: Royal","Passive Skills:","1) Fire Resistance (20%): Host can resist 20% of all damage caused by fire-based attacks.","2) Flame Will: Host can conjure and control basic flames using personal mana.","Active Skills:","1) Scorching Fury: Increase overall physical strength by 50% for 3 minutes.","- Cost: 20 Mana per minute","- Cooldown: 24 hours","2) Flame Demon Transformation: Awaken the innate bloodline to temporarily gain 1% of a true Flame Demon’s power. (Locked: Requires higher cultivation level).","3) Flame Slash: Release a destructive blade strike composed of concentrated fire. 200% attack power and speed.","- Cost: 20 Mana per strike","- Cooldown: 24 hours","4) Flame Burst Step: Gain a sudden burst of speed, increasing movement velocity by 300% for 1 second.","- Cost: 30 Mana per burst","- Cooldown: 10 seconds","```"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5 | Flame Demon Bloodline","paragraphs":["Dexter slowly raised his hands, staring at them in the dim light of the bedroom. They still looked the same but he felt raw power coursing through his muscles.","He hadn’t expected the bloodline to be so powerful.","With his current strength and skills, he felt like he could handle the three thugs and even Kreg easily now.","He was currently a Tier 2 Awakened Hero and while it wasn’t impressive, to a man who had spent his life at the bottom, this was like learning to breathe after years of drowning.","The moment his mana affinity shifted from F-rank to E-rank, he felt his meridians changing slowly widening by a few millimeters at most.","At this rate, mana easily flowed through his system with less resistance.","```","[Talent: Enhanced Hearing]","Type: Auxiliary","Rank: E","Ability: Hear sounds within a 200-meter radius under normal conditions, and up to 1 kilometer in a straight line when focusing. Permits sound differentiation and heart-rate tracking.","```","Nor just increasing his affinity, gaining bloodline and strength, he also awakened talent too!","Dexter closed his eyes, focusing his mind on his ears.","Instantly, the world exploded with sound. He could hear the slow, rhythmic dripping of the leaky faucet in the kitchen three walls away. He could hear the rustle of dry leaves scraping against the backyard fence.","More than that, he could hear the distinct, separate heartbeats of the three women in the living room.","Mira’s heartbeat was slow, steady, and heavy, carrying a deep, sluggish rhythm. Lyra’s heart beat with a rapid, light pattern, like a bird trapped in a cage. And Selene’s heart was weak and erratic.","Satisfied, Dexter stood up. The movement was incredibly smooth, his joints no longer making sounds. He walked to the bathroom, stripped off his sweat-soaked clothes, and stepped into the shower.","As the hot water washed over him, he looked at his reflection in the small, fogged-up mirror. The purple bruise on his jaw was gone. The sharp, deep pain in his ribs had completely vanished, leaving only a faint red scratch on his side. His body looked more fit, the muscles more defined and tight.","He dried himself off, dressed in a clean black t-shirt and grey joggers, and walked out into the hallway.","***","Dexter decided to check on the girls if they needed anything.","The moment he entered, Mira, Lyra, and Selene all turned their heads toward the hallway at the exact same instant.","Their eyes locked onto him, their expressions filled with a strange, sudden intensity.","Dexter paused, feeling a bit self-conscious under their combined stare. ’Why are they looking at me like they’ve seen a ghost?’ he thought, blinking.","Lyra’s dark eyes narrowed slightly, her gaze moving from his face down to his shoulders, then to his hands. Even though she could not hear, she was still connected to mana and could feel the sudden, dramatic shift in his presence.","Selene’s head remained tilted toward him, her sightless eyes wide.","The two of them stared for only a 2 seconds before turning their heads away, returning to their quiet states.","But Mira continued to look at him with her crimson eyes.","\"Is... something wrong?\" Dexter frowned as he asked, clearing his throat.","\"You’ve awakened,\" Mira said. Her voice was quiet, but there was an unusual weight behind it.","As a former Super Hero, even with her meridians blocked, her she could still perceive mana due to her high affinity.","Dexter hesitated for a moment, then gave a slow, honest nod. \"Something happened while I was resting. After the fight with Kreg’s men... it felt like a barrier inside me broke.\"","Mira gazed at him for half a second and gave a simply, quiet hum then closed her eyes and returned to darkness.","Dexter was about to leave but he suddenly thought if something.","He expanded his system interface then focused on Mira’s name under the investment targets, and the screen expanded into a detailed panel of golden text.","```","[Name]: Mira Calloway","[Age]: 22","[Relationship]: Wife","[Cultivation]","Former Rank: A-Rank Hero","Former Level: Super Hero (7th Tier)","Current Level: Awakened (4th Tier)","Current Mana: 12% (Sealed)","[Body Condition]","Meridian Damage: 89%","Neck-Down Paralysis","• Paralysis from the neck down","• Chronic nerve pain","• Muscle atrophy","• Core instability","[Mental State]","• Depressed","• Suicidal","• Angry","• Hateful","• In Pain","• Slightly Amused","```","Dexter felt a sudden, deep ache in his chest as he read the description. A level six out of ten chronic nerve pain, constantly firing through her body while she sat there, unable to move a single finger to soothe it. No wonder her voice was always so bitter and cold.","\"I can feel your eyes on me,\" Mira said suddenly. \"See something you like, husband?\"","Before Dexter could find a response, a sharp, choked gasp shattered the silence."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6 | Another Episode","paragraphs":["[Name]: Mira Calloway","[Age]: 22","[Relationship]: Wife","[Cultivation]","Former Rank: A-Rank Hero","Former Level: Super Hero (7th Tier)","Current Level: Awakened (4th Tier)","Current Mana: 12% (Sealed)","[Body Condition]","Meridian Damage: 89%","Neck-Down Paralysis","• Paralysis from the neck down","• Chronic nerve pain","• Muscle atrophy","• Core instability","[Mental State]","• Depressed","• Suicidal","• Angry","• Hateful","• In Pain","• Slightly Amused","```","Dexter felt a sudden, deep ache in his chest as he read the description. A level six out of ten chronic nerve pain, constantly firing through her body while she sat there, unable to move a single finger to soothe it. No wonder her voice was always so bitter and cold.","\"I can feel your eyes on me,\" Mira said suddenly. \"See something you like, husband?\"","Before Dexter could find a response, a sharp, choked gasp shattered the silence.","***","Selene Frost, who had been sitting quietly on the far edge of the old sofa, suddenly stiffened.","Her breath hitched in her throat, a soft, wheezing sound escaping her lips. Dexter’s head snapped toward her. He recognized the signs instantly—another icy seizure was beginning.","\"Selene!\" he called out.","The temperature in the small living room plummeted instantly. The air grew so cold that Dexter’s breath turned into thick, white plumes. Frost began to bloom rapidly across Selene’s pale skin, turning the ends of her dark hair a stark, icy white. Thin, delicate sheets of ice began to crawl across the fabric of the sofa, spreading down the wooden legs and onto the floorboards.","She was sitting right at the very edge of the cushions. As her body began to convulse, her balance wavered. She began to tilt forward, her sightless eyes wide with silent panic.","If she fell, her head would slam directly into the sharp edge of the low wooden coffee table. With her frail, weakened body, such an impact could easily result in a fatal head injury or a fractured skull.","Dexter did not hesitate.","\"Flame Burst Step!\"","His body moved before his mind could even register the command. 5 points of mana vanished from his core, and a soft, low thud of heat exploded beneath his feet. In an instant, his speed tripled. He blurred across the short distance, his hand reaching out to catch her just as her shoulders cleared the edge of the seat.","He wrapped his arms around her shivering frame, pulling her back against his chest.","The moment his skin made contact with her shoulders, a biting, intense cold surged through his arms. The frost on her cardigan transferred to his sleeves, turning the fabric stiff and white. It felt as though a hundred tiny needles of ice were driving deep into his flesh, trying to freeze the blood in his hands.","But Dexter held on. He gritted his teeth and immediately activated Flame Will.","A burst of heat surged from his hands as he tried to contain the frost but it was like a candle in a hurricane","With his right hand, he reached into his pocket and pulled out one of the emergency syringes he had purchased from the pharmacy earlier. He removed the cap with his teeth, lined up the needle against her shoulder, and pressed the plunger, injecting the warm, thick serum directly into her system.","The seizure lasted for thirty seconds.","To Dexter, it felt like hours.","Gradually, the violent tremors in her limbs began to slow, and the rapid spread of frost on the floorboards halted, the thin layers of ice slowly melting into small pools of water.","When the episode finally passed, Selene slumped forward against his shoulder, completely unconscious. Her skin was still damp and pale, but her breathing had returned to a slow, even rhythm.","Throughout the entire ordeal, neither Lyra nor Mira glanced at their direction. They seemed to have gotten used to Selene’s condition.","Dexter’s gently lifted her, carrying her small, fragile body into the bedroom, and laid her down on the large, combined mattress. He pulled three thick blankets over her, tucking her in tightly to ensure she would stay warm then turned on the radiator.","’The sickness seem to be acting up faster than usual.’","Dexter wiped the remaining frost from his hands, thinking about the time intervals when a clear, familiar sound echoed in his mind.","’Ding!’","```","[System Notification: Investment detected — Physical protection and medical intervention during an episode.]","[10x Multiplier activated.]","[Target: Selene Frost (Wife)]","[Calculating Returns...]","[Calculation Complete. Returns Granted:]","1. Frost Resistance (Minor): Host can now tolerate low temperatures and ice-based energy attacks 15% more effectively.","2. Frost Sense: Host’s body is now sensitive to the unique mana fluctuations of frost. You can now sense and predict Selene’s seizures 10 to 15 seconds before they physically begin.","```","Dexter was pleasantly surprised. With this system, maybe he would eventually find a cure for her.","He closed his eyes and accepted the rewards."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7 | Food Smith: Novice Peak","paragraphs":["The sun slowly came as night fell over the quiet neighborhood.","Inside, the atmosphere was completely different from the cold despair of the previous day.","For the first time in years, Dexter felt a deep, genuine happiness.","He hummed a soft tune as he moved around the kitchen. Earlier, he had searched the internet on his phone, looking for healthy, nourishing recipes that could help restore physical strength and gently soothe damaged meridians.","He had settled on a recipe for a slow-simmered chicken and wild herb broth. He carefully chopped fresh ginger, dry ginseng roots he had found in the family gift boxes, and fresh green onions. He washed a cup of pearl rice he bought earlier, letting it boil slowly in a clay pot until the grains softened and broke down, releasing a thick, comforting aroma then he added sliced mushrooms and soft, shredded meat.","It was a simple meal, but to a body that had been starved of nourishment, it was medicine.","’I wonder what rewards I will get this time.’","Dexter thought happily as he set four bowls and spoons on the wooden dining table. He walked to the living room, where the three girls sat in their usual silence.","\" Dinner’s ready,\" he called out.","No one moved.","’Right. I keet forgetting.’","He pulled out his phone and typed: [Food is ready. Come to the kitchen.]","He held the screen in front of Lyra who read it, nodded. She stood up, her movements were graceful despite her thin frame as she walked to Selene’s side and touched her elbow.","Selene tilted her head, recognizing the touch, and allowed Lyra guide her toward the kitchen.","They’d only been here two days, but they were already learning each other’s rhythms.","Dexter then turned to Mira.","Shes still had her eyes closed. The evening light caught her red hair and made it glow like embers.","He walked behind her wheelchair and gripped the handles.","\"I’m taking you to the kitchen.\"","Mira didn’t respond nor did she open her eyes.","Dexter didn’t mind, he wasn’t looking for response the first place. He unlocked the wheelchair and pushed her through the doorway, and into the kitchen.","The four sat together in the small kitchen. Only the hum of the refrigerator and the clinking of spoons could be heard. Lyra guided Selene’s hand to her spoon, helping her find the bowl and she began to eat on her own.","Dexter sat beside Mira. He picked up her spoon, scooped a small portion of the warm food and blew on it then held the spoon to her lips.","Mira stared at him, her crimson eyes flickering with a mixture of annoyance and reluctance. But the rich, savory smell of the food was too enticing to ignore making her stomach let out a quiet, embarrassing growl.","She opened her mouth, letting him feed her.","The moment the warm porridge touched her tongue, her crimson eyes widened slightly. The savory flavor of the chicken broth, balanced by the earthy sweetness of the ginseng and ginger, seemed to burst across her taste buds.","Moreover, she felt a faint warmth ease the sharp, persistent nerve pain in her neck and shoulders slightly.","Even Lyra and Selene paused when they tasted the food.","Mira swallowed and looked at Dexter. \"Did you actually cook this?\"","\"I did,\" Dexter said, smiling as he gathered another spoonful. \"Is it to your liking?\"","\"It is acceptable,\" she replied indifferently, though she quickly opened her mouth for the next bite.","Dexter smiled at her reaction and fed her until her bowl was completely empty. He then finished his own portion and was satisfied as the other two finished their meal.","---","After dinner, Dexter cleaned the dishes while the women sat in their various spot. Lyra by the window, Selene by the couch and Mira, anywhere Levi placed her.","He was drying the last bowl when the notification appeared.","```","[Ding!]","[Investment detected: Subject prepared and provided meal with beneficial mana properties to all three investment targets. Physical nourishment provided. Emotional labor performed (feeding assistance).]","[Current Multiplier: 10x — Base Tier]","[Calculating Returns...]","[Calculation Complete.]","[Returns Granted:]","1.Five Body Nourishing Meals Recipe (Complete Set) (Grade 2)","— A collection of five recipes specifically designed for heroes with damaged meridians. Each meal targets different aspects of physical and energetic recovery.","2.Cultivation Boost: 2 Days of Compressed Mana Refinement Applied.","3.Peak Novice Food-smith","[Do you wish to accept Rewards? Y/N]","```","Dexter was stunned by the rewards. Just cooking for them casually gave this much rewards. What if he unlocked the 10,000 multiplier system, wouldn’t he become godlike?","’I actually got a graded technique?’","’And it’s actually a cooking type technique!’","’Woah! It actually also made me a Foodsmith","In this world, there are Geneticists who concoct serums that provide special attributes like increasing strength, speed and even advancing cultivation levels. And also, there are those who apply the same techniques to food.","These people are called Food-Smiths! They use special techniques to nourish their food, making it have effects that is beneficial to the body and now, he was at the peak of novice rank without having a single knowledge about being a Foodsmith.","He accepted immediately.","In that moment, mana rushed into his body in a ways and his bones cracked and popped as his strength increased by a bit.","At the same time memories flooded his brain rapidly. Various cooking techniques flooded his mind in a flash and just like that he was a Peak Novice, Food-Smith!","That’s not all, the information about the recipe and also various ingredients needed flooded into his mind like they had been part of his memories.","Five Nourishment Meal:","Meal 1: Meridian-Soothing Broth — A golden liquid made with various ingredients but two main ingredients with two main ingredients Sun-moon fruit, Juiper root Sun-moon fruit and Juniper bark root. Soothes inflamed meridians and promotes gradual repair of minor damage.","Meal 2: Marrow-Fortifying Stew — Thick, hearty stew containing Ground Dragon Bone and Blood Rice. Strengthens the skeletal structure and improves mana circulation through the bones.","Meal 3: Nerve-Calming Congee — A rice porridge infused with Serenity Willow Bark and Moonlight Dew. Reduces chronic nerve pain and calms the nervous system.","Meal 4: Qi-Replenishing Soup — A clear soup made with Starlight Mushroom and Essence Spring Water. Directly replenishes depleted mana reserves and accelerates natural mana regeneration.","Meal 5: Body-Harmonizing Rice Bowl — A balanced meal combining elements of the previous four recipes with additional herbs. Brings the body’s systems into alignment and promotes overall healing."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8 | Spoiling The Girls","paragraphs":["Dexter’s hands were trembling slightly as he finished drying the bowl.","Half of the ingredients listed in his memories, he hadn’t seen them. And half he recognized but they were to expensive.","He pulled out his phone and began searching for the price of the ingredients.","It took Dexter half an hour to find what he needed.","There was a commercial district nearby called the Merchant Quarter. Most of the shops there are equipment stores, potion suppliers and other stuffs.","Tucked between a weapon smith and a potion brewery was a small shop called \"Heaven’s Taste: Cultivation Cuisine Supplies.\"","Dexter scanned their online catalog and found everything he needed.","Spirit Ginseng: 400 credits per root","Phoenix Feather Root: 300 credits per bundle","Ground Dragon Bone: 500 credits per packet","Serenity Willow Bark: 200 credits per portion","Starlight Mushroom: 350 credits per batch","Moonlight Dew: 250 credits per vial","Essence Spring Water: 150 credits per bottle","Blood Rice: 100 credits per bag","For Meal 1 — the Meridian-Soothing Broth — the daily cost was approximately 1,100 credits for three servings.","For all five meals rotated throughout the week, the daily cost averaged around 2,000 credits.","It was astonishingly expensive. A regular family could eat for a month on what Dexter would spend in a day.","Dexter’s eyes flickered and he wondered if it was going to be worth it spending so much money on food. But he quickly shook the thought of. With the system, he didn’t need to be worried.","Dexter did the math in his head.","If he spent 2,000 credits per day on ingredients, that was 14,000 credits per week. Over a month, that was roughly 56,000 credits.","If he maximized the \"significance\" of each investment, the returns could far outweigh the costs.","•••","The next morning, Dexter woke up early, showered and dressed in a simple black hoodie and sweatpants, pulling the hood low over his face.","The walk to the Merchant Quarter took forty minutes.","He reached the Merchant Quarter and it was quite less crowdy as people were still preparing for work.","Delivery trucks were unloading crates and the shop owners were setting up displays.","Heaven’s Taste was a narrow storefront with a green awning and a hand-painted sign. The windows displayed jars of dried herbs, bundles of roots, and packets of powder.","Dexter pushed open the door.","\"Morning,\" Dexter said, keeping his voice low. \"I need a week’s supply of specialized ingredients. Sun-moon fruit, Juniper bark root, Dry Dragon-Leaf, and premium spiritual pearl rice.\"","An elderly man with thick glasses was behind the counter. The man gave a warm smile and replied. \"How much quantity do you want to purchase?\"","Dexter calculated for a bit and replied.","The merchant nodded his head.\"Two thousand dollars for a single day’s supply of genuine Sun-moon fruit and Juniper bark root. For a week, that will be fourteen thousand dollars.\"","Dexter did not hesitate. He tapped his phone against the payment terminal, confirming the transfer. \"I’ll take them. Please pack them securely.\"","The old man smile widened.","’What a nice customer. He didn’t even haggle’","Then he replied. \"Please wait while I prepare them do you.\"","He then left the counter and headed deeper into the shop.","After the transaction was done, Dexter bought more things, two large bags of premium organic rice, fresh vegetables, lean chicken breast, and high-quality beef from the organic section, spending another five hundred dollars.","While walking on the street , he used his phone to browse a reputable local security agency online.","The bungalow’s wooden doors and thin window frames were far too easy to breach, as Kreg had proven. He selected a high-grade home defense package that included reinforced steel deadbolts, heavy iron security bars for all ground-floor windows, and a basic motion-sensor alarm system.","He paid five thousand dollars upfront for an express, same-day installation. The agency promised to send a team of technicians that same morning.","...","While walking through the district, he stopped in front of an Relic shop. Relic are tools with special effects to increase one’s damage power, speed and even mana.","The higher the type of Relic the stronger they are.","The Relic shop was called \"Essence Emporium\".","The interior was larger than Heaven’s Taste, with glass display cases arranged in a grid pattern.","Each case held jewellery, weapons, accessories and all of them faintly glowing with stored mana.","Type 1 Relics were the lowest tier of enchanted items, but even they were expensive.","A young man in a neat uniform stood behind the counter. \"Welcome to Essence Emporium. How can I help you today?\"","\"I need equipments with Pain reduction and Calming effects. Do you have anything like that?\"","The clerk’s expression became professionally interested. \"We have several options. For pain reduction, I’d recommend the Serenity Bangle. \"","The youth to a display case of silver bracelets — \"Type 1, reduces pain signals by up to 10% and takes the edge off chronic conditions.\"","\"How much?\"","\"Eight thousand credits.\"","Dexter’s eyes twitched. That was more than he’d expected. He sighed and replied.","\"I’ll take one.\"","The clerk retrieved the bracelet and placed it on the counter. It was plain thin silver band with a small blue gem set in the center. But there was actual beauty in its simplicity.","\"For calming effects,\" the clerk continued, \"we have the Tranquility Band. Type 1, reduces anxiety and stabilizes emotional fluctuations. It’s often prescribed for heroes with PTSD or anxiety disorders.\"","\"Does it help with seizures?\"","The clerk hesitated. \"It’s not designed for that specifically. But if the seizures are triggered by emotional instability or stress, it might reduce their frequency. I can’t make any guarantees.\"","Dexter thought of Selene and replied.","\"I’ll take two,\" he said.","\"Two Tranquility Bands?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"That’s five thousand each, so ten thousand total.\"","Dexter’s remaining balance was shrinking rapidly.","But the system would reward him. He had to trust that.","He paid and took the three bracelets — one Serenity Bangle for Mira, two Tranquility Bands for Selene and Lyra.","After confirming the payment, Dexter took the three small jade boxes and slipped them into his backpack.","His also stopped at a licensed medical supply pharmacy. He purchased a few bandages, painkillers and other things. While standing at the counter, he hesitated, his face turning slightly red as his eyes fell on the hygiene section. He realized that three young women living in an old house would eventually need basic personal supplies.","Embarrassed but resolute, he grabbed several packs of premium tampons and personal hygiene wipes, placing them on the counter.","\"Is that everything, sir?\" the pharmacist asked, hiding a small smile.","\"Yes,\" Dexter said, clearing his throat. \"That’s everything.\"","On his way back to the bungalow, as he passed a high-tech electronics store, a display in the window caught his eye.","It was a pair of sleek AI smart glasses. The advertisement claimed the glasses could translate spoken words into real-time text projected onto the lenses, or translate it to other languages so one can speak across several languages.","Dexter paused as an idea formulated in his mind.","He entered the store and purchased two pairs of the smart glasses for twenty thousand dollars.","By the time he finished his shopping spree, his bank account had been reduced from 150,000 thousand credits to exactly 6000.","He had spent forty-four thousand dollars in a single morning. But he did not feel a single shred of regret."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9 | Smart Glass For Selene","paragraphs":["Dexter arrived back at the bungalow at eight-thirty.","At exactly nine o’clock, a white van pulled up outside the gate. Three professional security technicians stepped out, carrying heavy toolboxes and metal bars. Dexter greeted them quietly, guiding them through the house. For the next two hours, the sound of drilling and metal clanging echoed through the bungalow.","By ten o’clock, the work was finished. Every window on the ground floor was now reinforced with thick, black iron security bars, and the front and back doors had been fitted with heavy, grade-1 steel deadbolts and a digital keypad lock.","A small, subtle alarm panel was installed beside the entrance. It wasn’t enough but at least it could inform the police if there was another break in attempt.","With the house secure, Dexter walked into the lady’s room. Mira was already awake, strangely sitting in her wheelchair. Dexter guessed Lyra might have helped her there.","While Lyra sat quietly on the sofa and Selene laying in the bed with her eyes opened.","Dexter reached into his backpack and pulled out the first pair of AI smart glasses. He walked over to Lyra, crouching down so he was at eye level with her.","As he reached out, Lyra flinched slightly, her shoulders tensing as she pulled back. Dexter stopped his movement, keeping his hands open and visible. He pulled out his notepad and wrote in large, clear letters:","`[These are smart glasses. They will translate my voice into text on the screen so you can see what I am saying. Please try them.]`","He held the note in front of her. Lyra read the words, her dark eyes moving from the paper to the sleek, white glasses in his hand.","But her expression didn’t change in the slightest.","He held them out to her.","Lyra didn’t reach for them.","Dexter waited. Then he typed another message.","[Please try them. I think they’ll help.]","She stared at the text for a long moment. Then, slowly, she raised her hand and took the glasses.","Her fingers were cold, she turned the glasses over in her hands, examining them.","Then she put them on.","The lenses flickered as the AI activated. The clerk had alredy calibrated it in advance so he didn’t need to touch anything.","Dexter nervously cleared his throat and spoke. \"Can you see the text?\"","The glasses translated his voice into words that appeared on Lyra’s lenses in real time.","[Can you see the text?]","Lyra’s eyes moved slightly, reading. Then she looked at Dexter.","Her expression changed.","It was so subtle that anyone without enhanced perception might have missed it. But Dexter caught it.","’That means it’s working.’","Dexter grinned and spoken again.","\"If you want to speak back to me,\" Dexter said, pointing to the small button on the frame of the glasses, \"you can type a message on your phone, and the glasses will read the text out loud using a text-to-speech feature. We can communicate now.\"","Lyra remained silent, completely rooted in place, staring at him through the glasses.","\"Hey,\" Dexter said softly, leaning closer. \"Are you alright?\"","She did not respond. She looked down at her lap, her hands clenching into tight fists. Dexter sighed quietly, thinking he might have pushed her too fast or made her uncomfortable. He stood up, turning his attention to Selene.","Dexter walked over to Selene, holding the second pair of smart glasses. He carefully sat beside her, keeping his voice low so as not to startle her.","\"Selene, I bought something for you too. These glasses have an active AI assistant. I’ve installed the house schematic to the glasses.\"","\"Also, it constantly scans the surroundings and through the bone conducting sound, it will speak to you and inform you where you want to go or how many steps to the kitchen, and where the doors are. It will help you move around the house safely.\"","Selene did not respond. She laid there as still as a statue, her pale skin looking almost translucent in the morning light.","Dexter waited for a moment, then gently set the white glasses on the sofa cushion right beside her hand. \"I’ll leave them here for you. You can try them whenever you feel ready.\"","...","Dexter walked back into the kitchen, and started making the \"Five Body Nourishing Meals\" he knew by heart this time.","According to the text, this broth was a rare, low-grade Enchanted Meal designed specifically to slowly coat damaged meridians, easing the constant nerve pain caused by severed pathways and restoring a tiny fraction of active mana circulation.","Dexter carefully pulled the expensive ingredients from the insulated bags. He sliced the thick, pale root of the Sun-moon fruit into thin, even discs. The root released a sharp, medicinal scent that cleared his sinuses. He then took the Juniper bark root and ground it into a fine powder using a small mortar and pestle.","As the hours passed, the kitchen filled with an incredible, rich aroma. The scent was entirely different from the simple porridge he had made the night before; it was sweet, heavy, and complex, smelling of fresh mountain air, wild honey, and warm herbs.","By one o’clock, the broth had boiled down into a thick, shimmering liquid that looked like liquid gold.","[Ding! You have succeeded in making a Grade 1 making Enchanted Meal]","[Name: Enchanted Meal]","[Type: Food]","[Grade: 1]","[Effect: Nourish the body, moisturize meridians, heal injuries and calm the mind]","Dexter ladled the hot, golden broth into three small bowls then carried them to the dining table, where his three wives were already seated.","Interestingly, none of them were wearing the smart glasses he had purchased. Lyra had left hers on the living room table, and Selene’s still sat untouched on the sofa cushion. Dexter’s brow furrowed slightly in disappointment, but he did not comment. He set the bowls down in front of them.","He sat beside her wheelchair with the bowl in one hand and the spoon in the other.","\"Open,\" he said.","Mira turned her head to look at him. Her crimson eyes moved from his face to the bowl to the spoon. Her eyes squinted as though she recognized what it was but couldn’t believe it.","\"What is this?\" she asked.","\"Meridian-Soothing Broth,\" Dexter said. \"First of the Five Body Nourishing Meals.\"","Mira’s eyes widened slightly as she knew it was actually a Grade 1 Enchanted Meal the moment she saw it.","But if it was really a Grade 1 Enchanted Meal and Dexter made it, that would mean that Dexter was at least a Novice Food-Smith!"]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10 | REWARDS!!!","paragraphs":["’Truly full of surprises.’ She thought in her mind as she glanced at him.","Dexter fed her and she opened her mouth slightly, letting the warm spoon enter.","The moment the broth touched her throat, a , soothing warmth exploded within her chest.","A wave of pure, refined mana rushed along her severed meridians. The constant, burning nerve pain in her neck and shoulders, suddenly dulled, dropping significantly for the first time in three years.","She stared at Dexter and spoke.","\"Didn’t you give all your money to the filth yesterday?\"","\"Don’t worry about the money,\" Dexter replied with a small, relaxed chuckle, holding up another spoonful.","Mira stared at him, her eyes searching his face but she eventually gave up and muttered. \"Stubborn.\"","As he fed her, Mira glanced at the empty space on the table beside her, then looked at Dexter. \"Where is mine?\"","Dexter paused, his spoon hovering in the air. \"Your what?\"","She narrowed her crimson eyes at him. \"My smart glasses. Or do you think I don’t need them just because I’m paralyzed?\"","Dexter snorted softly, a trace of amusement in his eyes. \"Don’t you usually like closing your eyes and ignoring me? What do you need them for?\"","Mira glared at him. \"If I don’t wear them, good luck getting those two to wear theirs.\"","Dexter’s face twitched. He looked from Mira to Lyra and Selene, who were sitting silently at the table. He realized Mira might be right; the other two were watching her, taking cues from her behavior.","\"Alright,\" Dexter said, sighing as he smiled. \"I give up. If you can get them to wear the glasses, I will buy the latest, most expensive model for you tomorrow.\"","Mira let out a short, quiet huff of satisfaction, swallowing the last of her broth.","\"Did you sell your kidney?\"","Dexter smiled gently as he reached into his backpack, pulling out three small, velvet-lined jade boxes. \"Would it have mattered if I did?\"","Mira rolled her eyes, but said. Nothing more.","\"Oh, before I forget.\"","Dexter set the three jade boxes on the table. He opened the first box, revealing the bronze-tinted metallic Pain-Reducing Bracelet. He leaned closer to Mira, carefully lifting her limp right hand and sliding the band over her wrist.","\"It’s really ugly,\" Mira muttered, looking at the simple bronze band.","But the moment the metal made contact with her skin, a soft, high-frequency hum vibrated through her wrist. A mild, soothing electric pulse traveled up her arm, gently blocking the chronic pain signals in her spine. The constant pain in her neck and shoulders dropped by another ten percent.","Mira froze. Her crimson eyes widened as she felt the sudden, blessed relief wash over her body. She looked from her wrist to Dexter’s face, her voice dropping to a whisper. \"You... you bought me a Type 1 artifact?\"","\"Yes,\" Dexter said, nodding his head. \"It’s a pain-reduction artifact. It should help make sitting in that chair a bit more comfortable.\"","He stood up, picked up the other two jade boxes, and handed them to Lyra. He pulled out his phone, typed a quick note, and showed it to her:","`[These are Calming Bracelets. They are low-grade artifacts that will help calm your mind and reduce Selene’s seizure frequency. Please keep them.]`","Lyra read the text, her dark eyes looking at the beautiful, blue jade bracelets inside the boxes. She looked up at Dexter, her expression soft and silent, and slowly nodded. She took one of the bracelets and slid it onto her own wrist, then reached out to slide the second one onto Selene’s arm.","Selene sat quietly, drinking her golden broth in silence. But when she finished her bowl, she slowly tilted her head toward Dexter.","Her lips parted, and she spoke in a voice so soft and quiet that Dexter almost missed it:","\"...Warm.\"","It was the very first word she had spoken to him since they met.","At that exact moment, a flood of bright, golden notifications materialized in Dexter’s vision, accompanied by a rapid succession of soft tones in his mind.","[Ding!]","[Investment Detected: Physical, Mental, Emotional, Security]","[Current Multiplier: 10x]","[Calculating Returns...]","[Calculation Complete.]","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Returns Granted]","[Skill Upgrade]","[Cooking: Novice (Peak) → (Early) Rank 1 Master Food Smith]","• Improved Enchanted Meal Success Rate","• Reduced Ingredient Waste","• Enhanced Flavor Extraction","• Additional Meal Effects","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Recipe Acquired]","[Grade 2 Recipe: Body Accelerating Healing Broth]","• Accelerates recovery and healing","• Double the effect of the Five Body Nourishing Meals when taken together.","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Cultivation Reward]","[2 Months of Compressed Mana Refinement]","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Item Upgrades]","[Serenity Bangle] x2","Type 1 Relic → Type 2 Relic","• Pain Reduction: 10% → 20%","[Tranquility Band]","Type 1 Relic → Type 2 Relic","• Calms the Mind","• Stimulates Brain Activity","[AI Smart Glasses] (Type 1) x3","→ Uses body heat to charge","→ Doesn’t need internet to translate","→ 100x speed in transcribing and translating (Type 2)","• Real-Time Speech Translation","• Multi-Language Translation","• Detects Mana Signatures","• Detects Aura Fluctuations","[Medical Supplies]","→ Grade 1 Painkiller","• Eliminates Pain for 2 Hours","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Security Upgrade]","[Smart Security System]","• Right reinforced Steel Deadbolts","• Iron Window Bars","• Motion Detection Alarm","• Mana-Sensitive Perimeter Ward","• Silent Alert Linked to Security Guild","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Do you wish to accept Rewards? Y/N]"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11 | Step-Mother’s Visit","paragraphs":["Dexter almost burst out in happiness right there and then. All his investments actually came back to him! Well, not the cash but even then, these returns were terrifying.","Just cooking for a few hours and he gained 2 months worth of cultivation. If he did this everyday, wouldn’t he break through to Super hero stage in less than a month?","It was too terrifying to even think about!","Dexter accepted without hesitation.","The knowledge flooded into his mind — new techniques, new recipes, new understanding of how food and cultivation intersected. His hands tingled as the cooking skill upgraded, muscle memory forming for movements he’d never made.","Two more months of cultivation. Added to the ten months he’d already received, that was a full year of compressed mana refinement in less than forty-eight hours.","He was still weak. Still at the bottom of the power hierarchy. But he was climbing.","...","Dexter’s smile vanished instantly. His E-rank Enhanced Hearing activated and he picked up the sound of a heavy, idling engine outside the gate.","He walked cautiously to the front door, unlocked the heavy new deadbolt, and stepped onto the porch.","Standing outside the gate was a massive, clean-cut bodyguard wearing a tailored black suit and dark sunglasses. He stood with his hands folded in front of him.","Behind him, a long black Rolls-Royce sat parked against the curb. The rear door of the luxury car opened, and another bodyguard, holding a large black umbrella, helped a woman step out onto the cracked asphalt.","The woman walked elegantly up the concrete path toward the gate.","She looked to be in her late thirties, but her smooth, pale skin and flawless features made her look no older than nineteen. She had long, raven-black hair streaked with elegant silver at the temples, sharp, aristocratic cheekbones, and eyes the color of winter ice. She wore a dark designer dress that likely cost more than Dexter’s entire house, and her every movement oozed a cold, effortless authority.","\"Stepmother,\" Dexter said, his voice going completely flat.","Valentina Ashford.","She was the primary wife of Aldric Ashford, the current leader of the family. She was the woman who had orchestrated Dexter’s suffering and isolation since he was a child.","Valentina had never laid a hand on him herself—she was far too intelligent for physical violence.","Instead, she had simply reduced him to a life of slavery, suffering and pain. She had spent ten years trying to make him invisible, to erase his very existence. And even killed a few of the servants for pitying him. Those who show him affection either ends up dead or maimed.","\"Dexter, darling,\" Valentina said, her perfect smile not reaching her cold, winter-blue eyes. \"May I come in?\"","Without waiting for his invitation, the lead bodyguard opened the gate, and Valentina walked past Dexter, stepping into the small bungalow.","She surveyed the small living room with barely concealed disdain, her ice-blue eyes lingering on the worn sofas and old tv.","\"How... cozy,\" Valentina murmured, her gaze moving slowly around the room. \"I see you’ve made yourselves at home.\"","\"What do you want, Valentina?\" Dexter growled.","Valentina’s smile sharpened. \"Can’t a mother check on her dear son?\"","\"My mother died when I was born.\"","\"True, a truly mysterious death.\" Valentina glanced at him and chuckled then smoothly, walked slowly around the room.","She paused near the dining table, her cold gaze falling on the three women.","\"The Crimson Valkyrie, Shadow Saintess and the illustrious Eternal Ice Princess Tempest.\" She let out a soft, mocking tutting sound. \"Such a waste. Three brilliant heroes, reduced to... this. And married to a useless, bastard.\"","She turned to Dexter, her head tilting like a curious bird. \"Your father was quite generous, don’t you think? He could have ignired the plea of the three families. Instead, he let you marry the three useless and famous cripple. .\"","Dexter’s eyes narrowed. \"I am asking again. What do you want, Valentina? Since I no longer have ties to the Ashford family, I can have you arrested for trespassing.\"","Valentina’s smile slowly vanished, and for a brief second, her mask of high-class elegance slipped, revealing a cold, ruthless expression.","\"Very well,\" she said quietly.","\"Your father is concerned about the safety of your three wives. We heard of the attack from the thugs and ask me to deliver a warning.\"","\"If anything happens to these three girls under your roof, the Ashford family will hand you over to the Calloway, Vance, and Frost families as a sacrifice to appease their anger.\"","Dexter let out a cold, sharp laugh. \"Banish me to this run-down house and then threaten me? You’ve already thrown me away, Valentina. Your threats mean nothing to me.\"","\"Get the fuck out of my house, and tell Aldric I’ve severed ties with the family as per the contract. The safety of my wives are my concern alone. I and the Ashford family have nothing to do with each other. So leave.\"","Valentina’s expression did not change, but her gaze hardened. \"Brave words for a useless kid.\"","She turned to leave, pausing as she reached the heavy front door. She looked back over her shoulder, her lips curving into a terrible, beautiful smile.","\"Oh, Dexter? One more thing before I go.\"","\"What?\"","\"The official investigation into the SSS-rank gate incident has finally been closed,\" she whispered, her voice carrying a chilling trace of amusement. \"It turns out the gate was not misclassified by accident. Someone intentionally altered the records to trap those three girls inside that dungeon permanently.\"","She let out a soft, mocking chuckle. \"If they wanted them dead back then, you might want to ask yourself... will they want to finish the job now?\""]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12 | Cute Neighbor","paragraphs":["\"It turns out the gate was not misclassified by accident. Someone intentionally altered the records to trap those three girls inside that dungeon permanently.\"","She let out a soft, mocking chuckle. \"If they wanted them dead back then, you might want to ask yourself... will they want to finish the job now?\"","Without waiting for his response, she stepped out of the house, her bodyguards closing the heavy door behind her.","Dexter stood frozen in the middle of the living room.","From the table, Mira let out a cold, sharp snort. \"If you hadn’t realized that already, ’husband’, then you are even dumber than I thought.\"","From the start to the finish, she hadn’t once glanced at lady Ashford. Her eyes closed as though she was sleeping in the wheelchair.","Dexter stood in the kitchen for a long time, staring at the closed front door.","Valentina’s words had confirmed his worst fears. The SSS-rank gate disaster was not as simple what they said. It was a targeted, assassination attempt to wipe out the talents of the three families all at once. And now that the three girls were living together in a defenseless, run-down bungalow, it would be even simpler to kill then.","He needed to grow stronger, fast.","With his newly awakened E-rank mana affinity and the Flame Demon bloodline, he had a solid foundation. But he had no formal combat techniques, and he could not afford to purchase expensive monster nexus cores to accelerate his cultivation without a hero license.","To get a license, he would have to register with the local Hero Guild, undergo a physical test, and successfully clear a trial dungeon.","But the fastest way to build his power was still through the system. He needed to take care of his wives, provide for them, and earn more investments.","The next three days passed in a quiet, steady rhythm.","Dexter woke at 4:30 AM every day. He showered, dressed, and began cooking breakfast. The meals were simple — rice porridge, eggs, vegetables — but he added a thread of mana to each one, just like he had with the first nourishing meal.","At 6:00 AM, he woke the women.","Mira was the easiest. She was always awake before he came for her, sitting in her wheelchair by the window, staring at nothing. He’d push her to the bathroom, help her with her morning routine, and then wheel her to the kitchen.","Lyra required text messages. He’d type [Wake up] on his phone and hold it in front of her face until she opened her eyes. Then he’d give hwr the glasses. Afterwhich everything else name easy.","Selene was the hardest. She didn’t wish to wear the glasses and thought it might be humiliating but he convinced her tht the other two girls are wearing she reluctantly wore it on the third day.","Breakfast was eaten in silence. Dexter fed Mira. Lyra fed herself, though she ate enough for three people and he was constantly having to cook more. Selene required guidance Lyra assisted with that.","---","Mid-Morning.","After breakfast, Dexter prepared the Five Body Nourishing Meal for the day. Each meal took between two and four hours to cook, depending on the recipe.","Dexter rotated through the meals, one per day, following the recipe manual’s recommended schedule.","He fed each meal to the women and watched for changes.","Mira’s pain levels decreased gradually. The Serenity Bangle helped, but the meals were making a difference too. After three days, he saw in the system that her chronic nerve pain had dropped from 6/10 to about 5.2/10 — not a huge change, but noticeable.","Lyra’s appetite remained enormous, but her mood seemed slightly more stable.","Selene’s seizures didn’t stop, but the Frost Sense Dexter had acquired let him anticipate them and adjusted the serum in advance reducing the seizure by a lot.","---","Afternoon.","After the nourishing meal, Dexter worked with Mira on physical therapy.","Her muscles were atrophying and if he didn’t act, she’d lose what little function she had left. He didn’t know if the meals would eventually repair her meridians enough for her to move again, but he wasn’t going to wait and find out.","Mira hated it.","\"This is useless and humiliating,\" she said through gritted teeth as he bent her left arm at the elbow. \"Unhand me you pervert.\"","\"Yes. I’m a pervert.\"","Dexter replied.","\"What’s the use when we’re going to die in a few days?\"","\"This is for when you will be able to walk again. \"","She glared at him, even the nunber one geneticist in the city couldn’t do anything, what’s makes you think you can?","’The system.’ Of course Levi wasn’t stupid enough to blurt it out.","While he worked with Mira, Lyra sat nearby and watched.","---","Late Afternoon.","Dexter trained in the backyard.","The space was small but it was enough for basic practice. He’d cleared away the debris and set up a makeshift training area with a punching bag he’d bought from a secondhand store.","He practiced basic punches. Jabs. Crosses. Hooks. Uppercuts. The movements were crude as he had no formal combat training, but he was learning.","He practiced kicks too. His legs were stronger than his arms as the Flame Demon bloodline seemed to favor lower body power.","Then he tried to use his abilities.","Flame Burst Step was the easiest. He activated it, and the world blurred and he appeared at another location in a split second. The speed was disorienting, but he was getting better at controlling it. He could now choose a specific destination instead of just launching himself forward blindly.","Flame Slash was harder.","---","Evening.","Dinner, more simple food, more silence.","Then bedtime.","Dexter helped each woman to the bedroom — Mira in her wheelchair, Lyra guiding Selene. He helped Mira into bed, arranged the blankets around Selene, and made sure Lyra was comfortable.","Then he retreated to his own room and cultivated until sleep claimed him.","---","This happened for three days and the rewards he got were astronomical. He broke through to Tier 3 Awakened Hero stage the next morning.","Dexter headed to the backyard, practicing his punches, when he heard something.","His enhanced hearing picked it up immediately.","He turned just as a girl climbed over the low fence that separated his backyard from the neighbor’s.","She was about sixteen, with messy brown hair and a face full of freckles.","\"You’re the guy from the news,\" she said. \"The one who married the three cripple.\""]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13 | Mysterious Tessa","paragraphs":["The afternoon sun beat down on the neighborhood, making the air shimmer with heat.","A dog barked from across the street as a car passed.","\"Bang!\" \"Bang!\" \"Bang!\"","Rhythmic punching noises sounded out from the backyard of a small bungalow.","The punching swayed as a young man relentlessly punched at the bag with two jabs, a cross and a hook.","He was wearing a grey wife-beater that was soaked through with sweat.","He raised his fists again. Jab. Cross. Hook.","That young man is Dexter.","After two hours of grilling, he felt he was setting a hang of the whole punching thing.","He wiped the sweat off his forehead and drank an enormous water.","\"You’re doing it wrong.\"","Dexter almost chocked in surprise. He lowered the water and glanced up at the fence line.","A girl was sitting on top of the wooden fence that separated his backyard from the neighbor’s property. She looked completely comfortable, as if sitting on a narrow wooden fence was the most natural thing in the world.","She looked sixteen, maybe seventeen. Red messy hair, tied back with a strip of cloth. Freckles scattered across her nose and cheeks like someone had flicked paint at her face. Green eyes that shone like a cat’s eye.","She wore a simple blue dress with a white apron. Which meant she’s either baking at home right now or works at one.","\"Excuse me?\" Dexter said.","\"The punch.\" She pointed at the punching bag. \"You’re leading with your shoulder. That’s why you keep losing your balance slightly after the hook.\"","Dexter stared at her. \"How long have you been watching?\"","\"For 10 minutes give or take.\" She casually said. \"You were very loud. I can hear you grunting from my kitchen.\"","Dexter felt heat crawl up his neck. He hadn’t realized anyone could hear him.","The girl swung her legs and dropped from the fence, and landed on the ground with a soft thud.","She was shorter than him by a few inches, but she carried herself with a confidence that made her seem bigger.","\"I’m Tessa. Tessa Wren. I live next door.\" She jerked her thumb over her shoulder. \"My dad owns the bakery on the corner.\"","\"Oh.\" Dexter wiped sweat from his forehead with the back of his hand. \"I’m Dexter.\"","\"I know.\" She said it blandly, without excitement or judgment. \"Everyone knows.\"","Her mouth was quite sharp and faster than her brain.","\"The bastard prince with crippled wives.\" She tilted her head, studying him. \"That’s what everyone in the neighborhood is calling you.\"","Dexter’s face hardened slightly. \"Is that so.\"","\"It is.\" Tessa walked past him to the punching bag and gave it a light tap with her knuckles. It barely moved. \"The old ladies at the market think you’re a scandal. The men think you’re either crazy or brilliant.","\"And what do kids like you think?\" Dexter asked.","\"The kids think you’re interesting.\" She looked back at him. \"And I think you’re bad at punching.\"","Dexter suddenly chuckled.","\"I guess I owe you a thanks then.\"","\"You’re welcome.\" Tessa turned around and touched the fence.","All of a sudden, she leapt up and landed on the narrow top wood like a cat.","The fence wasnt even two inches wide but she stood on it as if it were solid ground.","\"Here is how you punch,\" Her voice suddenly turned serious as she clenched her fists then started shadow boxing.","\"Power comes from the ground and the waist,\" she said. \"Not the arm. The arm is just the delivery system. The real punch starts in your feet.\"","She gestured at the bag. \"Try it.\"","Dexter looked at her for a moment. Then he turned to the punching bag, set his feet, and threw a hook.","This time, he led with his hip. He rotated his waist, transferred his weight, and let his fist follow the momentum.","\"Bang!\"","It sounded like a sharp crack as his fist struck the punching bag.","Dexter raised an eyebrow in surprise.","\"You’re a fast learner,\" Tessa smiled.","Dexter clenched and then three another hook, then another. Each one landed with that same sharp crack, sending bag swinging harder and harder.","The difference was quite incredible.","He turned to Tessa. \"Where did you learn that?\"","She shrugged. \"You learn a thing or two in this neighborhood. People here aren’t as simple as they seem.\"","Dexter squinted. He focused on her, trying to read her energy waves. Everyone who absorb mana emit an energy wave that others can feel to determine their power level. Just like how you look at someone to determine if he’s insane or not.","Well, unless they’re hiding it that is.","But Tessa was like a calm lake with no ripple.","Dexter frowned. He couldn’t get a reading on her at all. Which either meant she’s a normal human or she’s a whole realm higher then him.","But he was certain of one thing: she was a hero.","\"You’re a hero,\" he said.","Tessa’s expression didn’t change. \"Am I?\"","\"Awakened Or Super?\"","\"I’m just an ordinary girl with no energy to read.\" She shrugged.","\"Ordinary girls can’t stand on a two-inch fence rail without falling.\"","Tessa smiled an astonishing smile. \"Maybe I just have good balance.\"","Dexter stared at her for a long moment. Then he shook his head. She wasn’t going to tell him. Fine. He had bigger problems.","\"You’re training to become a hero, aren’t you?\" Tessa suddenly asked.","\"Something like that.\" Dexter turned back to the punching bag and resumed his fisting but this time, he reduced his striking force.","She tilted her head again. \"You’ll probably die in your first dungeon.\"","\"Probably.\"","\"But you’re still going anyway.\"","\"I have to.\" Dexter glanced at the house. Through the kitchen window, he could see the faint outline of someone sitting at the table — Lyra, probably.","Tessa was quiet for a moment. The sound of traffic, dog barking and Dexter’s punch filled the silence.","\"My mother was a hero,\" Her voice lowered softly."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14 | Not Enough","paragraphs":["\"My mother was a hero,\" Tessa’s voice lowered softly.","\"She died in a D-rank Cyclops dungeon when I was ten.\"","Dexter paused and he looked at her.","\"She was a B-rank hero.\" Tessa’s green eyes were fixed on the ground. \"Strong enough to clear D-rank dungeons in her sleep, everyone said. But dungeons don’t care about ranks. One wrong step, and she never came home.\"","\"I’m sorry.\"","\"Don’t be.\" Tessa looked up, and her eyes were dry. \"Heroing isn’t as glorious as the Hero Association makes it out to be. It’s ugly and dangerous and most people who try it end up dead or worse. The ones who survive are either lucky, talented, or both.\" She studied him. \"You’re neither.\"","\"Thanks.\"","Tessa guffawed at his reply.","\"Come by the bakery tomorrow morning. We’re preparing our special — honey buns with secret glaze. They’re good for recovery.\" She paused, looking back at him.","Before Dexter could respond, she dropped down on the other side of the fence and disappeared into the neighbor’s yard.","Dexter stood in his backyard, staring at the empty fence.","The girl was definitely not simple.","But she’d helped him. And she hadn’t asked for anything in return.","He shook his head and turned back to the punching bag. He spent the next hour throwing hooks using the method she’d shown him.","---","By the time he went back inside, the sun was setting and Dexter was sweaty and exhausted but not felt really good.","Mira was sitting at the kitchen table with her eyes closed.","\"Not even married for a month and you’re already talking to pretty young girls.\"","Dexter paused in the doorway, a drop of sweat falling from his chin to the floor. And he grinned.","Mira’s expression was flat. Her voice was even flatter. But there seem to be somythythat resembled amusement.","\"Should I be jealous, husband?\"","Dexter chuckled and walked to the sink, turning on the tap to wash his hands. \"She’s sixteen, Mira.\"","\"And I’m crippled, not blind.\" Lyra’s eyes followed him as he moved. \"She was looking at you like you’re a lost puppy she wants to adopt.\"","Dexter dried his hands on a towel and leaned against the counter. \"She’s just a neighbor.\"","\"Just a neighbor who happens to know how to throw a perfect punch and stand on a fence rail without falling.\"","Mira remained silent but then spoke. \"Be careful who you trust, Dexter. Everyone has an angle, even you.\"","Dexter froze where he stood.","The last three words ringing in his hears.","She was telling him she knew that he had an ulterior motive but she might have misunderstood.","\"What do you think is my motive?\"","Mira sneered. \"What is everyman’s motive?\"","Dexter stared at her then he bursted out laughing much to the surprise of Mira.","He laughed for a good 2 minutes before he finally recovered. \"You can’t begin to imagine how wrong you are.\"","\"Remember to call me when you want to use the bathroom. I heard it causes sickness if you hold your pee for long.\"","Then he left to the shower","---","He washed up and changed into clean clothes. Then he sat on his air mattress and pulled up his system interface.","---","[10,000x INVESTMENT MULTIPLIER SYSTEM]","[10 kills to upgrade to 100x Multiplier]","[Investment Target(s)]","- Mira Calloway (Wife)","- Lyra Vance (Wife)","- Selene Frost (Wife)","- Jasmine Constance (Ex-Girlfriend)","════════════════════","[Name]: Dexter Ashford","[Talent]: Enhanced Hearing (E-Rank)","[Occupation]: Rank 1 Master Food-Smith (Peak)","[Bloodline]: Flame Demon (Royal Grade)","[Mana Affinity]: C-Rank","[Rank]: Awakened Hero / Meta Hero","[Level]: 3","════════════════════","[Attributes]","Strength: 75","Agility: 85 [+10 Hidden Needle]","Physique: 75","Mana: 75","════════════════════","[Meditation Technique]","- Starlight Meditation Technique (Mortal Grade)","════════════════════","[Bloodline Skills]","- Scorching Fury","- Flame Demon Transformation","- Flame Slash","- Flame Burst Step","════════════════════","[Relics]","- Serenity Bangles ×2 (Type 2 Relic)","- Tranquility Bangle (Type 2 Relic)","- Self-Recharging AI Smart Glasses (Type 1 Relic)","- Hidden Splinter Needle Hairpin ×3 (Type 2 Relic)","---","[Hidden Splinter Needle Hairpin]","[Grade]: Type 2 Relic","[Category]: Hidden Weapon","[Durability]: 100/100","════════════════════","[Attributes]","↳ Agility +10","════════════════════","[Passive Effects]","↳ Silent Flight","• Produces no sound and conceals its aura while in flight.","↳ Aimlock Accuracy.","• Auto correct throw path when targeting close to a fatal point.","════════════════════","[Active Skill]","↳ Ghost Needle","• Cooldown: 30 Seconds","• Throws the hairpin at tremendous speed.","• Ignores 40% of the target’s Physical Defense.","• Deals greatly increased damage when striking a vital point.","• Automatically returns to the user after the attack.","════════════════════","He had bought seen an hairpin as one of their wedding gifts and gave it to the girls.","The system actually produced a Type 2 Relic as investment returns to him.","Right now, his mana affinity has increased to C-rank which meant his cultivation speed will increase as he can now easily absorb mana.","And his strength was seven and a half times higher than a normal human. being. However, this is the base strength for a Tier 3 awakened.","For each Tier broken through, one gains 25 extra attributes across all the stats. For Tier one their strength, agility, physique, and mana increases from 10 to 25, tier 2 is another 25 stats making 50 attribute points across all stats and Tier 3 making 75 attribute points across.","Three days ago, he was an F-Rank, nobody with stats of 25 across his board.","Now, his growth was terrifying and he had advanced to Level 3. If anyone in the Hero Association saw his progress rate, they’d either call it a miracle or assume he had some sort of secret.","But this speed still wasn’t enough."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15 | Upgrading The Girls","paragraphs":["Dexter closed the interface and sat quietly, his thoughts drifting back to Valentina’s warning.","Those Assassins. Someone had tried to kill the three women in that dungeon. They’d failed and the women had survived. But the people behind it wouldn’t just give up. They’d try again.","And Dexter was the only thing standing between them","He was only a Tier 3 Awakened Hero. Any assassin worth their money would be at Tier 9, maybe even early Super Hero rank. In a direct fight, Dexter wouldn’t last ten seconds.","He needed to advance further and even more, he needed a weapon.","Not the decorative broad sword that had come as a wedding gift but a real relic weapon that can channel his mana and amplify his combat ability.","But real relic weapons cost real money. And more importantly, to buy a weapon from any legitimate shop, you needed a Hero License.","The Hero Association regulated all relic weapons to prevent them from falling into the wrong hands.","To get a Hero License, you had to register with the Association, enter one of their virtual dungeons, and clear it. Your performance inside determined the rank of license you received, which in turn determined what grade of equipment you could buy.","Originally, Dexter had planned to wait until he reached at least Level 5 before taking the exam since a higher level would mean a better evaluation, a better license, and access to better weapons.","But he didn’t have time anymore.","\"I actually almost forgot.\"","The thought came suddenly. He’d been so focused on the assassination threat and leveling up that he’d nearly overlooked something important.","When the system had rewarded him for the massive investment of buying all those items for his wives, it had returned the upgraded versions to him.","He reached into the drawer beside his bed and pulled out three beautiful bracelets.","The moment he touched it, a refreshing sensation flowed through his body, like stepping into a cool stream on a hot day. His mind cleared. The ache in his muscles from training faded to nothing.","’These are the real deal,’ Dexter thought.","A genuine Type 2 Serenity Bracelet was worth at least twenty thousand dollars on the open market.","He could sell them. Use the money to hire guards, buy black-market weapons, set up defenses.","But after only a brief moment of consideration, he shook his head and stood up, holding the three bracelets as he walked toward the living room.","---","Mira was seated in her wheelchair in front of the television. The TV was off but she sat there anyway, staring at the blank screen. She was wearing the AI smart glasses, but her eyes were closed behind the lenses, and her brows were furrowed in pain.","Even with the Type 1 bracelet, the pain was still there.","She seemed to notice him approaching as her neck tilted slightly but she didn’t open her eyes.","Dexter stopped beside her and held out one of the new bracelets.","\"Mira,\" he said softly. \"I brought you another bracelet. It does the same thing as the one you’re wearing, only it’s much more effective. Give me your wrist.\"","Mira slowly opened her eyes.","Her gaze first landed on his face. Then it shifted to the bracelet in his hand.","Her eyebrows knitted together.","\"...That’s a Type 2 bracelet.\"","She stared at him with suspicion. Dexter had learned over the past few days that Mira knew more about artefacts and cultivation resources than he did — she’d been an A-rank hero, after all. She could identify equipment grades by sight.","\"She spoke in a Flat tone. \"First, you bought a Type 1 bracelet, and now you’ve brought home a Type 2 relic. don’t tell me you actually sold your kidney to buy this.\"","Dexter glared at her. \"Do you want it or not?\"","Mira snorted softly. \"As though I can stop you? Do what you want.\"","Dexter nodded. He reached for her wrist and unclasped the old Type 1 bracelet then quickly fastened the new Type 2 bracelet in its place.","The instant the clasp clicked shut, Mira’s body trembled as a cool, soothing energy spread from the bracelet up her arm. From her shoulder, down her spine, and out into her limbs.","It was really nice, making Mira release a soft sigh.","The relentless pain that had tormented her every waking moment for three years diminished by twenty percent.","Twenty percent didn’t sound like much but for someone who had lived with constant, unbearable pain, it was a massive difference.","Compared to the Type 1 bracelet, which had only reduced her pain by about 10 percent, this was on an entirely different level.","For the first time in a long while, Mira’s tightly knitted brows slowly relaxed.","She sat there for a moment, clearly feeling the difference, her expression something Dexter had never seen on her face before.","It was relief.","Mira’s eyes narrowed slightly as she watched him lower her hand back onto the armrest. Then, without asking, he reached up and removed the bulky AI glasses from her face.","\"Hey—\"","\"Relax.\" He replaced them with a thinner, lighter pair. \"Advanced AI glasses. They have an eye-tracking system. You can use your eyes to browse the internet, navigate apps, read messages — everything. It’s connected to the network.\"","Mira blinked as the new lenses adjusted around her vision. The display was sharper, the text clearer, the interface more intuitive than the clunky Type 1 glasses.","She tested it — moving her eyes left, right, up, down — and the cursor on the display followed. A small smile tugged at the corner of her mouth before she suppressed it.","\"The internet,\" she said, her voice dry. \"Nothing but feeble people with opinions that change every split second.\"","Dexter said nothing. But he knew what she meant.","Not long ago, she had been the Flame-Heart Princess. An S-rank hero. One of the youngest B-rank heroes in the city. The internet had loved her, praised her, celebrated her, then the dungeon happened.","And the same internet that had worshiped her turned on her overnight. She went from hero to zero in the eyes of the world.","Mira closed her eyes behind the new glasses and said nothing more.","---","Lyra was standing at the window of the living room.","She always seemed to be standing or sitting near a window. Dexter wondered if it was because she couldn’t hear the world so she watched it instead.","Or maybe it was just the only place where she could feel like she was connected to something beyond these four walls.","He crossed the room and stopped beside her.","\"I bought advanced versions,\" he said, holding up the items. \"New AI smart glasses, thinner than the ones you’re wearing. And a Type 2 Serenity Bracelet to replace the Type 1.\"","The text appeared in her glasses, translating his spoken words in real time.","Lyra’s slender neck turned. Her dark eyes dropped to the bracelet in his left hand, then to the new glasses in his right. She studied them for a moment, her expression unreadable as always, then reached up and removed her old glasses.","She exchanged them for the new ones. The thinner frames settled on her face, and her eyes moved as the display calibrated. Then she unclasped her old bracelet and handed it to him. She fastened the new Type 2 bracelet around her wrist.","For a moment, she was her eyelid trembled.","The Serenity Band’s calming effect was subtle, not as dramatic as the pain relief Mira experienced, but he thought he saw her shoulders drop slightly.","\"Is it working?\" he asked.","This new glasses traslated the words quickly and even had two automated reply below the words.","[Yes. It’s working.] [No. It’s not working]","She glanced at the [Yes. It’s working] Option and a robotic voice rang out from the frame of the glasses.","\"Yes. It’s working.\"","Dexter smiled.","He handed her a second set of glasses and a second Type 2 bracelet. \"These are for Selene. She flinches when I touch her, so can you help me give them to her?\"","Lyra looked at the items in his hands. Then she looked at him and nodded.","Took both items, then she turned and walked to the bedroom.","Two minutes later, she returned, carrying the old AI glasses and the old Type 1 bracelet. She handed them to Dexter without a word.","He took them and placed everything into a small storage case. He could sell them to a secondhand relic dealer and use the money to hire a guard at the Hero Association for a day, giving him ample time to enter a controlled dungeon and earn his license.","It wasn’t much of a plan. But it was what he had.","He was halfway to the door when the loud sound cut through the entire neighborhood."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16 | Monster Outbreak!","paragraphs":["The sound was very faint, but Dexter’s Enhanced Hearing caught it from five blocks away.","A long, wailing tone like that of a siren.","Dexter’s confused face immediately changed as he realized what it was.","A monster outbreak siren.","Every city in the country had them — warning sirens designed to alert the population when a dungeon breach occurred.","Dungeons were supposed to be contained, sealed behind gates that the Hero Association monitored. But sometimes, a gate destabilized, a new dungeon pops up or monsters broke through their cages. It was always unexpected and always cause death or injury.","Andrew groaned softly, he had been expecting assassins, didn’t think there would be an actual monster outbreak.","He closed his eyes, as he activated his ability.","Suddenly, every sound within a 200 meter radius flowed through his ears.","\"BOOM!\" \"HOOOWL!\" \"Bang!\" \"Bang!\" \"Bang!\" \"H-help me! It’s—\" \"Squelch!\"","Andrew’s face paled slightly and the last sound he heard was of a skull cracking and exploding like watermelon squeezed too tight.","The siren was coming from the east — from the direction of the Merchant Quarter and it was getting louder, which meant the breach was spreading.","’I hope it doesn’t reach here.’ Andrew thought nervously. From what he heard, the monsters were likely wolves but he wasn’t too sure.","Most breaches were contained quickly by the Hero Association had response teams that could be deployed within minutes. So the sirens were more of a precaution instead.","But \"most\" wasn’t \"all.\"","Dexter had live long enough to know not to depend on his luck.","He immediately started to move as he locked the back door, then ran to the the front door and locked it. Then started with the windows locking every single windows in the house. Just in case. He moved the fridge to the front door and barricaded the back door with the dining chair.","Then he checked the locked doors once more to ensure no mistakes.","Mira’s quiet time was ruined by him running around the house. She opened her eyes and glared at him as he passed her wheelchair for the seventh time.","Her brows furrowed in irritation as she asked. \"What are you doing?\"","Dexter didn’t stop moving. \"It’s hopefully nothing, but I’m hearing the outbreak siren in the distance. It’s better to be safe than sorry.\"","He went to Lyra, who was watching him from the kitchen doorway with a calm expression.","\"There might be a monster outbreak nearby,\" he said, speaking clearly so the glasses could translate. \"I need you to go to the bedroom. Just in case.\"","Lyra suddenly reached for something. It was her phone. Her fingers moved as a robotic voice spoke from the frame of her glasses.","\"We are already dead. The monsters would be doing us a favour.\"","Dexter stared at her, stunned.","The idea that death would be a mercy made him sympathetic.","She’d been trapped in silence and darkness for three years, unable to hear, unable to speak, unable to do anything but exist. Of course she’d had thoughts like that.","Dexter didn’t know what to say. So he said nothing.","Lyra looked at him for a moment longer. Then she turned and walked to the bedroom without another word.","Dexter exhaled and went to Mira.","\"Come on,\" he said, gripping the handles of her wheelchair.","\"Did I tell you I wanted to move?\" Mira’s voice was irritated.","\"Did I ask your permission?\"","Mira’s lips curled. \"You know, you’re becoming quite abusive.\"","\"I heard you like abusive men.\" Dexter replied without thinking.","The words left his mouth before his brain could stop them.","The moment they were out, Dexter wished he could take them back.","Mira’s face changed. The mocking irritation on her face changed as her expression turned blank and then chilling cold.","A raging fire replaced them as the crismon eyes locked in Dexter.","Mira’s father was rumored to be abusive. Dexter didn’t know the full story and was simply said to have been a senseless rumor that came out after the news of her being a cripple came out.","He thought it was just a rumor but from Mira’s reaction, it was most likely true.","He opened his mouth to apologize—","But then he heard something.","From two blocks away, the siren’s wail was suddenly drowned out by other sounds. Gunshots, screams and explosions then a very loud and sharp howl.","It was the sound of a monster.","And it was very close.","Dexter’s face changed. He grabbed Mira’s wheelchair and pushed her fast towards the bedroom.","\"Lyra!\" he called out as he reached the door. \"Lock the door from behind!\"","He wheeled Mira inside, positioned her chair against the far wall, and stepped back into the hallway. Then closed the door shut and locked it from the outside.","He waited but there was no sound of a lock clicking from inside.","Dexter’s eye twitched.","’Are these girls courting death!?’","He wanted to roar in anger. He’d just told them there was a monster outbreak. He’d just told them to lock the door. And they couldn’t even manage that one simple task?","He forced himself to calm down. Getting angry wouldn’t help. He needed to focus.","’Fine, it doesn’t really matter.’","He turned and ran to the kitchen.","Part of their wedding gift — the pile of boxes that had come from the three families — had contained a decorative broadsword.","It was a ceremonial blade with intricate design made to look beautiful however it wasn’t meant for battle.","Dexter had never bothered to move it and it had been leaning against the wall in the kitchen since the first night.","He grabbed it and frowned.","The metal was cheap, the balance was terrible, and the edge couldn’t even cut through bread.","But it was solid steel, and right now, solid steel was better than bare hands.","He also grabbed two kitchen knives from the drawer and tucked one into his waistband at his back and held the other in his left hand, the broadsword in his right.","Then he stood at the hall way and listened carefully, suddenly his face changed as the kitchen window shattered..."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17| Dark Hounds Attack","paragraphs":["With his Enhanced Hearing, the world seem to become a map of sound.","He could hear the outbreak in detail now. People fighting, the sounds of gunfire, the roar of hero abilities activating, the crash of bodies hitting walls and vehicles.","But mixed in with the human sounds were the monster sounds.","’Dark Hounds.’","Dexter’s body stiffened as he recognized where he recognized the monster howls.","These are ordinary mutated beast with strength ranging from 3-stars to 7-Stars. But that wasn’t the most terrifying thing about them, the most frightening thing about them was that they came in packs, dozens of them. Sometimes hundreds.","The fast and aggressive pack hunters could tear through civilian neighborhoods like paper and they were getting closer.","\"Awooooooo!\"","Dexter’s grip tightened on the broadsword and cold sweat dripped down his forehead and ran along his jaw as his heart pounded rapidly.","He inhaled slowly, using the breathing method from the Starlight Meditation Technique to clear his mind and regulate his heart beat.","Then his ears trembled.","Dexter suddenly ran to the kitchen window and positioned himself beside it.","As though in cue,","\"Bang!\"","A claw tore through the reinforced iron bars on the kitchen window.","The metal screeched as three thick, black claws easily ripped through the bars like they were made of tin and a massive head popped inside.","It was a Dark Hound.","The beast looked like a mutated simple version of a dog. It was about 1.5 meters tall and larger than a lion with thick black fur and yellow eyes.","There was 4 star like patterns on its forehead signifying it was a 4-star Mutated Beast.","Droll escape its massive jaws and its teeth were long and curved like hunting knives.","Dexter eyes turned cold holding his breathe, he stabbed forward with his entire strength.","\"Chi!\"","Hot, foul smelling blood spilled out in all directions, spattering out there on the kitchen floor and wall.","\"Squelch!\"","The Hound thrashed, its claws scraping against the window frame. Dexter twisted the blade and pulled it free, and the creature’s body immediately went limp, half-in and half-out of the window.","[Requirement for System Activation Completed]","[Requirement: Kill 3 Humans or 3 Mutated Beast (3/3)]","[System Initialization Completed.","[Congratulations on activating the Slaughter Extraction System]","[Slaughter Extraction System: Extracted +3 strength, +2 Mana, ]","He didn’t have time to read the notification or ponder why his strength had suddenly increased as another sound entered his ears.","Dexter dropped the bloody broadsword and picked up the second kitchen knife from his waistband. One knife in each hand.","He hurried to the front door and his face changed as he rolled to the side.","In a split second, the door exploded inward as a massive Dark Hound burst through the ruined doorframe, letting the wood splinter.","\"Hooooooowl—\"","The howl shook the walls and rattled the window.","Dexter stomped his feet on the wall, using its momentum, he pivoted, as he stabbed the knife into its throat from underneath. The blade punched through the soft tissue of the neck and into the brain.","The Hound instantly collapsed and immediately died.","[SES: Extracted +3 strength, +2 Mana ]","Dexter yanked the knife free and rolled to the side as two more Hounds came through the destroyed door.","They were both level 5 Mutated Beast!","They immediately spread out as they charged at him from two different direction. One going left and one going right, trying to flank him with astonishing speed!","Dexter’s face changed as this two beasts were even faster than he could keep up with.","He activated his Enhanced Hearing to the fullest as a blur flashes to his left.","Dexter heard the wind shift and he instantly dodged left, letting the claw swipe through empty air.","As the claw missed him by a centimeter, he suddenly moved as he sliced the underside of its front leg but the blade wasn’t sharp enough to fully slice through it and only causing a deep wound, deep enough to make it bleed. The Dark Hound yelped and stumbled.","At that moment the Dark Hound on the left came immediately after.","Dexter instantly dropped low, as the claw sliced some of his hair.","His other knife moved as he slashed at the Hound’s belly as it passed. The knife cut through fur and skin, and the Hound snarled in pain, blood dripping from the wound.","But they weren’t dead. And more were coming.","Dexter suddenly heard another sound from behind him.","Another Dark Hound had actually crawled through the kitchen window!","His face changed as he quickly turned to the back.","But it was too late.","\"Bang!\"","The Dark Hound’s claw slammed into his back.","The impact was like getting hit by a car.","Pain exploded across his shoulder blades, and Dexter was sent flying across the hallway, slamming heavily in the wall as he slid to the floor.","His grip loosened and both knives clattered out of his hands.","For a moment, the world spun and his vision blurred as his back screamed with agony.","He gritted his teeth and forced himself to push thought the pain. He raised his head and then saw the hound that hit him wasn’t attacking again. He saw its forehead and he saw 6 star like pattern on its head.","6-Star Mutated Beast.","Dexter’s face paled and he knew today he might not survive.","’Should I escape?’","With [Flame Burst] bloodline skill and his Enhance Hearing ability, he was certain he could escape unscathed.","But the women...","His face kept changing as his brain fired up rapidly. His brain told him that his only chance at survival was to escape. There’s no way a Tier 3 Awakened Hero can kill a 6-Star Mutated beast!","Every level provides at least 25 stats which meant the 6-Star mutated beast has at least 150 stats in strength alone.","Dexter only has a pitiful 75 stats in strength; the gap was almost double!","If he runs now, he could survive but his wives..."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18 | Second System Awakening, Level Up","paragraphs":["Dexter only has a pitiful 75 stats in strength; the gap was almost double!","If he runs now, he could survive but the girls, his wives, would definitely die.","He had only known them for almost a week but he didn’t even know what they liked. Therefore they were basically strangers.","Not to mention Lyra’s appetite. She could eat a family of three daily meal in one sitting.","Despite taking his time to cook extra portions for her, she never thanked him.","Selene basically treats him like he was filth from the dirtiest slum and flinches when he gets close to her.","Mira is the worst of them all.","Despite taking care of her every needs, she insults and undermine his ego every chance she got even when he bathes and wash her every single day.","The three women never once expressed their thanks and treats him like nothing.","Therefore it would be unreasonably, incredibly and ridiculously stupid to risk him life for them when they are basically strangers and log weight.","However, as he saw the beast moving toward the bedroom door. Toward Mira, Lyra and Selene, time seem to slow down and every sound seem to fade in the background as he heard breathing of the three women.","He recognized Mira’s taking in a deep breathe of air as though it was her last and then exhaled.","He recognized Lyra’s footsteps as she walked towards the door, impatiently awaiting what’s to come.","He recognized Selene’s slow beating heart suddenly picking up as she whispered her longest words.","\"It’s finally hear.\"","The three had actually accepted their death and was fully embracing it.","Dexter’s face flushed in sadness but his heart lit up in inexplicable rage!","Rage that the girls had given up after this small amount of set back!","How could they be so selfish!?","Do they know how many people were born deaf and mute?","Do they know how many was born crippled or how many was born blind or how many was born with chronic pain?","And yet, those people managed to live life to the fullest, finding meaning and happiness in this world and even managed to find love.","Yet, these three selfish princesses got to live with their senses intact for so many years.","Not only that, the three were born talented and had everything served to them on silver platter but when they suffered this set back, they actually want to take their own lives?","\"How can you be so selfish!?\"","Dexter roared in anger and fury!","The rage burned so hot it burned away the pain.","\"Scorching Fury!\"","\"BOOM!\"","A surge of energy struck him like a thunderbolt.","His blood literally ignited as his magma like blood flooded through every fiber of his body.","His muscles trembled and swelled as his strength increased by 50%!","His eyes seem to burn with flame, with his irises flickering with actual fire as his hair floated upward.","The Dark Hound struck at the bedroom door and its claw easily pierced a hole in the door. One more strike and it would break through.","Dexter suddenly appeared beside the massive hound and thrust its two blade right through its neck.","\"Ding!\"","The Hound actually turned around so fast it slashed and parried the blade attack.","Dexter felt his arm trembled and he gritted his teeth.","The beast possess 150 agility stats and despite Dexter activating [Scorching Fury] his strength and agility capped at 112.5. There was still a vast difference between the two of them!","Before he could react, the Dark Hound’s mouth opened so wide it could fit a watermelon blurred as it flashed towards him.","If he doesn’t move, his head will be chopped off! But even with Scorching Fury his speed was still too slow to react to his head being bitten off.","Dexter’s eyes widened into a panic as he watched the maws of the Dark Hound Wrap around his head.","\"Flame Burst!\"","30 points of mana burned and Dexter’s feet released a blast of heat wave as Dexter’s agility increased by 300% for 1 second.","\"Bang!\"","Dexter watched as the massive mouth of the Dark hound slow down incredibly.","Dexter didn’t retreat, instead he turned towards the side of the beast. Its mouth was still wide open but its eyes actually reacted to Dexter’s incredibly fast movement.","Dexter raised the knives and stabbed them directly through the eyes of the Dark hound with all his strength.","The beast could track Dexter’s movement but just like the previous Dexter, it couldn’t react and could only watch as the blade stabbed into its left eye and straight to its skull.","[SES: Extracted +6 strength, +5 physique, + 3 Mana]","The beast froze and then collapsed in an instant.","\"Ding!\"","The notification barely registered but Dexter was already moving.","The two wounded Hounds from before already stood up. One was limping while the other was circling around him, snarling and circling, looking for an opening.","\"Awooooo!\"","\"Awooooo!\"","The two beasts actually let loose a loud howl. Dexter’s face couldn’t be more blacker.","He moved with incredible speed, slashing the throat of the first Dark Hound and using his momentum, he stabbed his blade through the skull of the second Dark Hound, pinning it to the wall like a decoration.","Hearing the howl, Dark Hounds began converging rapidly around the house.","Two level 6 burst through the kitchen window but before they could land, two emerald and almost invisible needle pin tore through the air like a bullet, heading for the nose of the first Dark hound and the second needle pin heading for the cheek of the second.","If hit, it will probably be non fatal. It was truly a bad throw.","But strangely, the needles changed trajectory in mid air and stabbed into the eyes of the Dark Hounds.","\"Chi!\" \"Chi!\"","[SES: Extracted +10 strength, +15 physique, + 3 Mana, +8 agility]","...","[Hidden Splinter Needle Hairpin]","[Grade]: Type 2 Relic","[Category]: Hidden Weapon","[Durability]: 100/100","════════════════════","[Attributes]","↳ Agility +10","════════════════════","[Passive Effects]","↳ Silent Flight","• Produces no sound and conceals its aura while in flight.","↳ Aimlock Accuracy.","• Auto correct throw path when targeting close to a fatal point.","════════════════════","[Active Skill]","↳ Ghost Needle","• Cooldown: 30 Seconds","• Throws the hairpin at tremendous speed.","• Ignores 40% of the target’s Physical Defense.","• Deals greatly increased damage when striking a vital point.","• Automatically returns to the user after the attack.","The two 6-Star beast collapsed on the kitchen floor, sliding forward due to the momentum of their lunge.","[Ding! You’ve leveled up to Tier 4]","Dexter didn’t care about the notification as another Dark Hound burst through the kitchen doorway. Then another at the destroyed front door.","He pulled the knife from the dead Hound’s neck and gripped it in his left hand, then picked up the broadsword beneath his feet.","The first Hound lunged.","Dexter didn’t try to dodge this time. He parried the claw strike with the broadsword as the impact sent vibrations up his arm, but Scorching Fury gave him the strength to hold his ground, then activated Flame Burst Step.","\"Whoosh.\"","He vanished like a puff of smoke. One moment he was in front of the Hound, the next he was beside it, appearing so fast that the creature’s eyes couldn’t track him.","He slashed its head off clean.","The body dropped. The head rolled.","The second Hound came from behind. Dexter heard it and spun, bringing the broadsword around in a wide arc. The blade caught the Hound across the chest, cutting deep into its ribs. It yelped and stumbled back.","The third Hound attacked from the kitchen doorway. Dexter Flame Burst Stepped again, appearing to its left, and drove the knife into its eye. The creature shrieked and collapsed.","The fourth Hound hesitated but Dexter didn’t, in his anger, he lunged forward and attacked, his speed was fast and his momentum oppressive that the Mutated beast actually turned tail and ran but Dexter caught up with it, killing it in a two strikes.","The Dark Hound kept converging and Dexter was like a mad babarian, using everything in his asernal to kill. The more he kills the stringer he becomes!","By the time Hero’s from the Hero Association, Dark Hound corpses filled the entire house, both inside and outside of it."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19 | MASSIVE Rewards & 100x Upgrade!","paragraphs":["Dexter stood in front of his gate.","Dark Hound corpses covered the ground around his house. A few still twitching in their final moments of death.","As the smell of blood filled the air with a faint small of sulfur coming from Dexter’s body.","Righr now, Dexter’s shirt was torn, revealing deep claw marks the 6-Star Hound had left on his back.","Blood was caked under his fingernails and his arms were streaked red from wrist to elbow.","In his left hand, was a steel rod he used to kill the last beast after the knife snapped inside a 5-Star’s skull.","From far away, the wail of emergency sirens cutting through the night, getting closer.","Heroes in proper combat gear were already engaging beasts in the streets and he could hear the crack of abilities activating, the crash of bodies hitting vehicles, the sharp reports of gunfire from the Association’s armed response units.","Dexter exhaled slowly. He let himself lean against the gate post a she breathed in.","He looked around the neighborhood. The fighting was concentrated on the eastern side of the street.","But here, on his side of the block, something didn’t add up.","Directly to his left, a blue house with a cracked driveway was untouched and also to his right, a cream-colored two-story with a garden fence was also untouched. Across the street, two more houses, the same thing.","Then he looked at Tessa’s house, the same thing to.","Dexter frowned as he stared at the four houses.","The Dark Hounds had swarmed this neighborhood like a flood.","But those four houses? The surrounded his bungalow were not affected.","’What is this situation?’","It was like the beasts didn’t dare go near them.","---","They arrived 30 seconds later.","The Silver-rank response team moved through the neighborhood quickly dispatching the monsters around.","The team slowed as they approached Dexter’s yard. The house was almost thoroughly destroyed. With beast corpses in the kitchen, the yard and the living room.","There was blood everywhere, claw marks in the wall and the kitchen window destroyed.","And in the center of it all, was a young man, covered head to toe in blood.","The Silver-rank team leader was a tall woman in polished silver armor. Her eyes went from the corpses to Dexter. He was clearly a Tier 4 awakened. How had he killed a 6 star beast?","One of her team members leaned in and whispered something. The woman’s eyes widened slightly as she recognized who he was.","The bastard who married the cripple.","That guy did ’this’?","\"You...did this?\" she asked.","Dexter met her eyes. He was tired. His body was failing. But his voice came out flat and clear.","\"Yes.\"","She stared at him for a long moment.","Then she brought her fist to her chest and saluted a hero’s salute that’s not meant for civilians.","Dexter blinked. He hadn’t expected that.","\"Name?\" she asked. \"For the report.\"","\"Dexter Ashford, awakened Hero. Tier 4.\"","\"Get the medic over here,\" she called over her shoulder. \"This man has a dozen open wounds.\"","The team medic rushed forward, already pulling supplies from his kit and started working on Dexter","---","The Hero Association secured the neighborhood within 20 minutes. The remaining Dark Hounds were either killed or driven back toward the breach zone, where higher-rank heroes were working to seal the Gate instability.","Dexter was escorted to a medical tent set up at the edge of the evacuation zone.","Finally alone, he opened his system notifications.","They’d been piling up for the last hour. He’d been too focused on survival, but now, in the silence of the tent, he let them flood in.","[Investment Multiplier System Activated]","[Investment Detected: Physical, Mental, Emotional, Security]","[Current Multiplier: 100x]","[Calculating Returns...]","━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━","[Return 1: Compressed Cultivation — One Year]","A wave of energy slammed into his chest. Dexter grunted in pain and pleasure as he grabbed the edge of the cot as mana flooded through his body.","His mana core expanded, his meridians widened, and he broke through to Tier 5, Tier 6, Tier 7 before the wave finally subsided.","[Return 2: Mana Affinity Upgraded — C-Rank → A-Rank]","Instantly started to flowed through him like water through an open pipe. The difference was staggering. He could feel mana in the air now without the need to concentrate and meditate.","It was everywhere, and for the first time, it was actually his to use.","[Return 3: Talent Upgraded — E-Rank → D-Rank (Enhanced Hearing)]","The range of his Enhanced Hearing doubled, and the clarity improved in ways he couldn’t quantify yet.","[Return 4: Bloodline Upgraded — Royal Grade → ORIGIN GRADE]","[New Bloodline: Berserk Flame Demon Bloodline (Origin Grade)]","Dexter’s eyes widened.","Top 100,000 bloodlines — Mutated Grade. Common people have this grade of bloodlines.","Top 10,000 — Royal Grade. It’s typically rare and Wealthy and powerful families built legacies on these.","Top 1,000 — Origin Grade. Had never been found.","And his had just jumped from Royal to Origin.","[Berserk Flame Demon Bloodline — Origin Grade]","[Passive: Fire Resistance increased to 50%. Flame Will now generates ambient heat that weakens nearby enemies.]","[Active: Scorching Fury — Strength increase upgraded from 50% to 80%. Duration extended to 5 minutes.]","[Active: Flame Burst Step — Speed increase upgraded from 300% to 500%. Duration extended to 2 seconds.]","[Active: NEW — Berserk Form — When health drops below 20%, enter a controlled rage state. All stats increase by 100%. Pain receptors shut down. Duration: 10 minutes. Cooldown: 48 hours.]","[Active: NEW — Flame Demon’s Wrath — Unleash a concentrated blast of demonic fire in a 15-meter radius. Damage scales with missing health. The less health you have, the more devastating the attack.]","[LOCKED: Flame Demon Transformation — Requires higher cultivation level to unlock.]","Dexter’s hands were trembling in pure happiness.","But that wasn’t all.","[Return 5: Culinary Rank Advanced — Rank 1 Master Chef → Rank 2 Grandmaster Chef (Early)]","[Effect: All meals prepared by host now contain strong special effects. Enchanted Meals will be significantly more potent. Meals can now actively accelerate healing, boost cultivation, and purify toxins.]","[Return 6: Martial Art Acquired — \"Extreme Slaughtering Demon Body\" (Tier 3)]","[Description: Transform mana into slaughter energy to temper the body. Progressively strengthens muscle fiber, bone density, and skin toughness through combat. Upon perfection, body becomes impervious to all weapons. Physique doubles. Power of any weapon used is doubled.]","[Return 7: Grade 3 Restoration Pill ×1]","[Effect: Randomly heals a single injury in the body. Can restore damaged nerves, fractured bones, or severed meridians. One-time use.]","Dexter’s heart stopped. \"Restore damaged nerves.\" His mind immediately went to his three wives. But he only had one pill.","[Return 8: Type 3 Macro-Splicing Saber","═════ Macro-Splicing Saber ═════","Relic Grade: Type 3","Category: Saber","Durability: 300/300","Attributes","+35 Strength","+25 Agility","+20 Vitality","Special Effects","• Macro-Splice","Slices through large targets with unnatural precision. Greatly increases damage against armored enemies, fortifications, and colossal monsters.","• Spatial Cleave","The blade releases a compressed crescent slash that travels up to 25 meters before dissipating.","• Structural Severance","Attacks identify and exploit structural weak points, reducing an enemy’s defense by 30% for 5 seconds.","• Edge of Ruin","Each consecutive strike increases blade sharpness and damage by 8%, stacking up to 5 times.","• Relic Rend","Deals 40% bonus damage against relic armor, magical barriers, and summoned constructs.","Ultimate Skill","◆ Macro Dissection","Consumes a large amount of mana to unleash a single overwhelming slash. Everything within a 50-meter line is cut apart on the molecular and magical level, ignoring 60% of physical defense and destroying weaker barriers instantly.","Passive","• Unbreaking Edge","The saber never dulls and automatically repairs minor damage over time.","A real weapon. A Type 3 weapon. The kind of relic that Silver and Gold-rank heroes spent fortunes to acquire.","[Return 9: Type 3 Protective Amulet]","[Effect: Wearer receivesa passive barrier that absorbs damage up to Peak Super Hero Regenerates over 24 hours after breaking.]","[Return 10: Type 3 House Protection Talisman]","[Effect: When placed on a dwelling, creates a barrier that repels all entities below Superhero Rank at will. Monsters and hostile individuals below this threshold cannot invade the protected area. Duration: Permanent until destroyed.]","Dexter stared at that last one. A permanent house barrier. The kind of protection that would have stopped the Dark Hounds from ever reaching his door.","If only he’d had it a week ago.","[Return 11: D-Rank Talent Card — \"Echo-Location\"]","[Effect: Emits high-frequency sound pulses that create a three-dimensional map of the surrounding environment. The user can perceive terrain, walls, obstacles, moving targets, and hidden objects even in complete darkness or through smoke, fog, and similar visual obstructions.","[Return 12: D-Rank Talent Card — \"Mana Arms\"]","[Effect: Construct up to 4 additional arms using solidified mana. Each arm has 10% of user’s physical strength. Duration scales with mana reserves.]","[Return 13: D-Rank Talent Card — \"Telepathy\"]","[Effect: Speak directly into the minds of others. Can also read the surface thoughts of individuals whose cultivation level is below the user’s.]","Four extra arms. Telepathy. Ground-based sonar. These ar the things that could assist his wives!","[Return 14: Type 3 Chain Pain Ring]","[Effect: Temporarily transfer any ill effect, status condition, or debuff from the user to a target. Can also be used in reverse]","[10,000x Investment Multiplier System— Upgrade Notification]","[Confirmed Kills: 16/100]","[Threshold reached: 10 kills]","[Multiplier Tier UP: 10x → 100x]","[All future Investment returns will now be calculated at 100x multiplier.]","[Kills remaining until next upgrade (1,000x): 84]","\"This is slightly too much.\""]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20 | Silent Treatment","paragraphs":["\"This is slightly too much.\"","Not only had he advanced by leaps and bounds, he also got Talent cards that could assist his wives and improve their living situation!","Mira is paralyzed and can’t move but with the Mana Hands, she could use the mana hands to do a few things.","Lyra can’t hear and speak but with the telepathy ability card she could speak directly timings kind and hear their outward thoughts. It was basically the same thing as being cured.","Finally, Selene. With the Echolocation talent card, she could see vibrations and map out the surrounding areas within 10 meters!","These abilities to others might be worthless but to his girls, they were everything.","Not to mention his investment had increased from 10 times to over 100 times!","His strength would be truly terrifying from now on.","Every investment he made from this point forward, would return one hundred times what it would have at base. He exhaled a turbid air and opened his eyes.","\"Weng!\"","Flames seem to dance around his eyes as he looked around with new found clarity.","Eighty-four more kills was the next upgrade.","---","A healer came to the tent.","She was a middle-aged woman with blue eyes. She smiled when she saw him.","Her Talent was called Healing Hands, and when she pressed her palms against the claw marks on Dexter’s back, a warm golden light seeped into his skin.","The deep wound slowly began to heal rapidly at a speed visible to the naked eyes and then the pain gradually vanished until there was nothing left.","The exhaustion that had been weighing on his bones since he canceled out Scorching Fury bloodline skill also vanished.","Dexter rotated his shoulder experimentally, there was not a single pain.","\"Rest up a few hours and you will be good as new.\" She packed her things and turned to leave.","Dexter didn’t respond. He was watching through the tent flap as Association workers hauled the Dark Hound carcasses onto transport vehicles.","They were taking everything. Dexter pursed his lips. He hadn’t remember to take the nexus fire if the beast.","Nexus cores are crystallized mana essence inside each beast’s heart and was very valuable — both for cultivation and for the money they’d fetch on the open market. Sixteen beasts meant sixteen cores. At market rate, that was enough to live on for months.","But it was too late. The Association had already claimed jurisdiction over the entire outbreak site.","One of the Association officers approached him — a neat man in a pressed uniform holding a clipboard.","\"Mr. Ashford. You and your dependents will be transported to a nearby hotel. Fully paid for by the Hero Association. You’ll stay there for a minimum of three days while we repair the damages done to your home and monitor the neighborhood for residual Gate instability.\"","Dexter nodded and sighed in relief. He didn’t have the money for repairs right now.","\"Someone from the Hero Association will come to meet you at the hotel in a few days regarding the beast carcass and your housing repairs.\" The officer paused, then added with a small nod of respect. \"Thank you for your service.\"","\"You’re welcome.\"","Dexter replied.","---","A black limousine pulled up outside the tent twenty minutes later.","Association staff loaded Dexter’s things, not that there was much. A few changes of clothes, the leftover food supplies, Selene’s medication, and the small case containing the old Type 1 bracelets and AI glasses he’d replaced. It all fit in two bags.","Two men assisted his wives into the vehicle. One guided Mira’s wheelchair into the spacious back compartment, securing it against the floor mounts. Another helped Lyra who helped Selene to the vehicle.","Dexter watched from outside the limousine.","He looked at his three wives as they settled into the leather seats. Mira’s eyes were forward, her expression closed. Lyra sat quietly, her hands folded, her new AI glasses dark. Selene was still, her face turned slightly away.","He clenched his fists at his sides.","The anger was still there. It had been burning in his chest since the outbreak. Since the moment Lyra had walked toward the door, waiting for death like the other girls.","They hadn’t struggled, not once. They just sat there and waited to die.","He huffed and got into the limousine. The door closed behind him with a soft thud.","The limousine pulled away from the tent, leaving the ruined neighborhood behind. Through the tinted windows, Dexter watched the street pass, Association vehicles with flashing lights.","The city was already recovering. People were already moving on.","He leaned his head against the window and said nothing. The atmosphere was incredibly awkward and thick with tension.","Mira suddenly opened her eyes as though she could feel his anger pressing against her skin.","Her lips crisped into a knowing smile and she closed her eyes again.","Lyra felt it too and she too turned to look at Dexter through her smart glasses before looking away.","Selene remained still but she shifted uncomfortably on the seat.","---","The hotel was called the Grand Meridian. It was the kind of place Dexter had only ever seen in movies. Marble floors, crystal chandeliers, and uniformed staff who acted like they’d been trained in a military academy for hospitality.","At the front desk, the clerk asked if Dexter wanted connecting rooms.","\"No, separate rooms.\" he replied.","The clerk checked his system and shook his head. \"I’m sorry, sir. We’re at capacity due to the monster outbreak evacuation. The only available unit is a premium suite with a single bedroom. It has a very large bed — more than enough to accommodate four guests.\" He glanced past Dexter at the three women behind him. There was a flash of jealousy in his eyes but he quickly hid it.","Dexter’s frowned. He didn’t want to stay in the same room with the girls but now, he had no choice.","\"I’ll take it.\"","The clerk handed him the key card. \"Twentieth floor. Elevator’s to your left.\""]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21 | Unexpected Kiss","paragraphs":["The elevator doors slid open onto the twentieth floor.","Without a word, Dexter wheeled Mira out into the quiet hallway. The carpet was thick and soft beneath the wheels, swallowing all sound. B","ehind them, Lyra gently held Selene’s hand, guiding her slowly as they stepped out of the elevator together.","The four of them walked in complete and heavy silence.","So he stayed silent.","Mira seemed to sense his mood. Every now and then she stole a glance at him from her wheelchair, her lips parting slightly as though she wanted to say something. But the words never came.","Lyra noticed it too. She occasionally looked at him through her smart glasses before quietly lowering her dark eyes again.","No one spoke.","They reached the suite. Dexter unlocked the door and pushed it open.","The room was luxurious — far beyond anything any of them had lived in recently. A spacious living room with elegant sofas, a polished dining table, and floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the city lights below.","A marble bathroom with a bathtub big enough for two. And beyond the living room, a single large bedroom with a bed that was, as promised, enormous.","Without saying anything, Dexter wheeled Mira inside and positioned her near the window. He walked into the bedroom, examined the layout, checked the locks on the windows and other stuffs.","Satisfied, he walked back into the living room and picked up the room service phone.","He ordered dinner for everyone, selecting dishes he thought each of them would enjoy based on what he’d observed over the past week. Mira liked rich, flavorful broths. Lyra ate enormous portions but preferred simple, hearty food. Selene hadn’t shown strong preferences, but she seemed to respond well to warm, soft meals.","Less than twenty minutes later, a staff member arrived with a cart covered in silver plates.","\"Here.\"","Dexter tipped him a 10, then heeled the cart to the dining table, and uncovered each dish carefully, arranging them neatly.","\"You should eat while it’s still warm,\" he said flatly.","Without waiting for a response, Dexter turned and walked toward the door.","There was a perfectly comfortable sofa in the living room. He’d intended to sleep there tonight.","But not yet.","---","The elevator carried him back down to the lobby.","Earlier, when they’d checked in, he’d noticed a small bar tucked into one corner of the ground floor. Warm amber lighting with wood and the faint sound of jazz drifting through the entrance.","The bar wasn’t crowded, but it wasn’t empty either.","Businessmen in loosened ties, a couple sharing a quiet drink, a few weary travelers staring at their phones.","Dexter ignored everyone, took an empty stool at the far end of the counter, and let out a long, slow breath.","The bartender approached with a friendly smile. \"What can I get you?\"","Dexter stared at the rows of bottles for a moment.","He hadn’t had a drink in weeks. Before the marriage, alcohol had been his way of surviving the Ashford estate.","He’d been an alcoholic, though he rarely admitted it to himself. He’d quit mostly because he couldn’t afford it anymore. Then the system appeared, his wives, and somewhere along the way, he’d simply forgotten that alcohol existed.","\"Whiskey,\" he said quietly. \"Neat.\"","\"Coming right up.\"","A few moments later, the bartender placed a crystal tumbler before him.","Dexter wrapped his fingers around the glass then took a slow sip.","The whiskey burned its way down his throat, warming his chest almost instantly.","He closed his eyes.","\"Sigh...I really missed this.\"","It has been a while truly.","Suddenly, something shifted beside him.","\"How long has it been?\"","Voice like a thousand mystical Sirens. The feminine voice sounded out from beside him.","Dexter opened his eyes and glanced to his left. A beautiful woman sat two stools away, dark hair cascading over one shoulder, vivid green eyes watching him with quiet amusement. She looked really elegant.","Dexter blinked and then glanced over his shoulder. But there was no one there.","When he looked back, she covered her mouth and chuckled lightly.","Realization dawned, and he gave a slightly embarrassed smile. \"You were talking to me?\"","She chuckled. \"I’d be a weirdo talking to ghosts if I wasn’t.\"","Dexter rubbed the back of his neck. \"Sorry. Just been stressed out a lot. What were you asking?\"","The lady nodded her head and pointed at his glass.","Dexter understood what she meant and replied. \"Oh. It’s been three weeks i took a drink last.\"","She raised her own glass, something pink and fruity. \"Mine is 16 hours .\"","Dexter bursted out laughing, making the girl laugh too.","She extended a hand. \"Rachel.\"","He shook it. \"Dexter.\"","\"Nice to meet you.\"","\"You too.\"","They both took another sip.","\"So,\" she said, turning slightly on her stool to face him. \"What happened today to make you break?\"","Dexter stared into his whiskey before giving a dry chuckle. \"Family.\"","She laughed softly. \"That bad?\"","\"It’s... complicated.\" He looked at her. \"What about you?\"","She sighed dramatically and raised her glass. \"Business.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Business?\"","\"Yeah. Business has been hectic and dangerous lately.\"","He shook his head and toasted with her. \"To life.\"","\"To tough life.\"","They smiled and drank up.","Before either of them realized it, the conversation began to flow naturally.","They talked about work stress, about how adulthood somehow became exhausting overnight and how money became the most important things.","Minutes slipped by, the drinks came and went. Dexter switched from whiskey to something lighter. Rachel ordered something sweeter. The jazz played on. The bar slowly emptied around them.","For the first time that day, maybe for the first time in weeks, Dexter smiled without forcing it.","The conversation gradually slowed, Rachel found herself looking at him differently now, a bit warmer.","More specifically, she found herself looking at his lips.","Dexter noticed her gaze linger for a fraction of a second. But was a little tipsy, so he dismissed it.","\"I really need to turn in,\" Rachel said, gathering her purse. \"I’ve got a meeting early tomorrow.\"","Dexter smiled. \"It’s been fun.\"","And he meant it. In the span of an hour, this stranger had made him feel more like a normal human being than anything had in the past three weeks.","She locked her eyes with his and it seemed magnetic. \"It’s been fun,\" she replied.","Then she suddenly leaned forward and kissed him!"]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22 | Extreme Slaughter Demon Body","paragraphs":["Dexter woke up before dawn and let out a long yawn. He was halfway out of bed, his brain already running a checklist for the kitchen, before he caught himself. He wasn’t at the bungalow. There was no rice to wash, and no breakfast to scramble together for the girls.","Instead, he was staring at a fancy ceiling, in a hotel room that cost more per night than he used to make in a month.","Right. The Grand Meridian.","They were still stuck here. The monster outbreak had turned their neighborhood into a graveyard, and the Hero Association had put them here.","\"Sigh. I could get used to this, right?\" He smiled as he muttered.","He glanced at the clock on the nightstand.","4:03 AM.","The room was silent, filled only with the hum of the air conditioner and the soft breathing of the three women in the massive bed behind him.","He felt a sudden, twitchy need to be busy.","Usually, every morning he was always busy by this time, Chopping vegetables, planning meals, but here, thwre was nothing to do.","Since sleep was a lost cause, he sat up on the couch and shook off the grogginess. He needed to be more Productive.","He closed his eyes and started the Starlight Meditation Technique.","A week ago, his mana affinity had been so low that trying to use it was like trying to drink water through a solid straw. He mostly did it back then just to keep calm his mind.","But things were different now. His affinity had jumped all the way to A-Rank, and the difference was like night and day.","The moment he triggered the technique, the mana in the room seemed to rush toward him. His body drank it up, his core filling like a dry basin under a waterfall.","So fast.","He kept his eyes shut, trying to keep his composure, but he was genuinely shocked. If he kept this up, he’d be able to stabilize his Tier 7 strength in no time.","After a few minutes of feeling that energy hum through his system, his mind drifted to the other thing he’d been putting off: the Demon Tempering Body Technique.","He’d gotten it as a reward, but he hadn’t had a second of privacy to actually try it out.","He stood up, gave his neck a quick crack, and cleared some space by pushing the coffee table aside.","The instructions were simple enough: 108 forms, extreme stress, and specific mana paths.","How hard could it be?","He kicked his legs up into a headstand, trying to twist his body into the required shape.","The first form was an absolute nightmare.","It was like someone had taken the worst parts of yoga and combined them with a medieval torture device.","\"Aarhus is really difficult.\" Dexter grunted as he tired practicing the technique.","His hips screamed in protest, his spine felt like it was being twisted like a wet towel, and he had to keep his mana moving through twelve specific points at the exact same time.","He lasted ten seconds. Then fifteen. By twenty, his arms were shaking so hard he thought he might shatter his own floor.","He collapsed.","\"Damn...\" he wheezed, flat on his back, his shirt already soaked through with sweat.","[Ding!]","[Extreme Slaughtering Demon Body — Form 1: Complete]","[Strength Increased: +1%]","He stared at the ceiling, feeling like a fool, until the notification popped up. He sat up, blinking at the blue text hanging in the air.","\"...Seriously?\"","Twenty seconds of feeling like his bones were being rearranged, and he’d gained a full percent of raw strength. That was insane. If he kept this up, he’d be a monster in a few weeks.","Then he looked at his mana bar.","Half of it was gone. Just like that.","The technique didn’t just train his muscles; it was literally burning his mana to build them. That was a hell of a price to pay.","\"This thing is terrifying,\" he muttered.","He wasn’t going to get any more training in without passing out, so he grabbed a fresh shirt and decided to head outside. The walls were starting to close in on him. He needed a run.","The hotel grounds were massive with green tall, grasses, leading the path and sculptures at the entrance. Dexter jogged along the perimeter, letting the cold morning air hit his face, burning off the restless energy that had been coiling in his gut for days.","He rounded a corner near the back garden, intending to finish another lap, when he saw something.","Five floors up, an old man was standing on a premium suite balcony.","He looked like any other retired guy in a tank top, white hair pulled into a messy knot, moving through some kind of slow-motion workout.","He was graceful, smooth, fluid, like he was moving through water as he practiced."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23 | The Old Man!!","paragraphs":["Dexter was about to keep jogging when his system pinged.","[Ding!]","[Slaughter Extraction System — Target Detected]","[Analyzing 7th Tier Grade Technique in progress...]","[Would you like to continue analysis? Remain within observation range.]","Dexter froze.","7th tier?","He’d never even heard of a 7-th grade anything. Those were the kinds of things that could cause an entire war, and here was some guy, doing it on a balcony at 4:00 AM like it was a morning stretch.","Without thinking, Dexter backwd up to a tree, keeping his eyes locked on the balcony.","The old man didn’t seem to notice. He just kept moving, shifting his weight, breathing in sync with movements that looked simple but clearly weren’t.","Dexter’s system started pulling data, mapping out the weird way the old man’s mana was circulating through his meridians.","Ten minutes. Then twenty. The old man finished with a long, slow exhale, wiped his face, and ducked back inside.","[Analysis Progress: 5%]","Only five percent?","He let out a frustrated huff.","At this rate, he’d have to live in these bushes for a week to get the whole thing.","He looked up at the empty balcony.","Every day, he thought. Every chance I get. I’m taking this.","The rest of the morning was a dull slog. Dexter went back upstairs, took care of the girls, and played his part in the quiet, awkward routine they’d fallen into.","But his head wasn’t in the room. He kept finding excuses to slip out, checking the balcony from the garden, from the lobby, from the window of the suite.","Finally, in the late afternoon, he saw movement.","He bolted for the back garden, hid behind a hedge, and watched. The old man practiced for another thirty minutes, his movements shifting, becoming more complex.","[Analysis Progress: 11%]","Still not enough. It was driving him crazy. He couldn’t exactly knock on the door and ask for a private lesson this guy was clearly a powerhouse.","He was stuck playing the long game.","Night hit. Back in the suite, Dexter was doing the usual thing—helping Mira from her wheelchair to the bathroom when he saw she was stained red.","She was in her period!","He went bright red. He couldn’t help it.","Mira just stared at him, then let out a dry laugh.","\"Why are you so red? I’m the one who should be red aren’t I.\"","Dexter’s jaw set. He didn’t say a word. So he went inside picked a pad and fixed it to a panties and helped her in it.","Then took her where she needed to go and walked out to the living room.","He was still angry. He was still bitter. And the way she’d teased him didn’t make it better; it just made things feel weird. He could feel Selene and Lyra watching him from the bedroom, but he didn’t care either.","He’d had enough. He grabbed the room key and walked out the door, needing to get away from the suffocating quiet.","At 7:00 PM, he was back at his post.","The old man was there again, moving through the same strange, fluid forms. Dexter watched, focused, as the system worked its magic.","[Analysis Progress: 17%]","When the old man went inside, Dexter sighed and turned to leave. He didn’t see the old man pause at the glass door, watching him with a sharp, amused glint in his eyes.","Inside the suite, a young woman’s voice drifted out.","\"Grandfather... are you intentionally teaching that boy?\"","The old man stroked his beard, looking down at the empty garden.","\"No.\"","The girl arched an eyebrow.","He chuckled.","\"It took you a year to learn the first stage. No way that brat gets it in three days. I’m just bored.\"","\"You’re playing with people again,\" she said with a sigh.","\"He caught my interest,\" the old man laughed. \"And he’s persistent. If he can steal this from just watching, he’s earned it. If not...\"","He shrugged.","\"Then he’s not worth the worry.\"","When Dexter got back to the room, he sat on the couch, exhausted.","The suite was quiet, but as he sat there, he heard it, tiny, jagged spikes of mana.","He focused.","It was as if someone was cultivating.","’Are the girls cultivating in the bedroom?’","If they truly are cultivating with shattered meridians, it would be incredibly painful!","Just like trying to force water through a rusted pipe. It hurt, it was dangerous, and their progress was probably almost zero.","They should have been resting. But they were sitting there, pushing through the agony, trying to put themselves back together.","’ Have they changed?’ Dexter shook his head and smiled, he felt it as ridiculous. They wouldn’t give up on killing themsolves just like that.","He went to say something, but he stopped.","Tomorrow, he thought. We’ll deal with tomorrow.","He laid back, closed his eyes, and drifted off to the sound of them fighting for every inch of progress.","The next morning, it was 7:00 AM, and the old man was already out there.","Dexter was back, eyes locked on the balcony.","The system was buzzing, the numbers creeping up—19%, 20%, 21%—when the old man just... stopped.","He didn’t finish the move. He just tilted his head and stared right at the tree where Dexter was resting.","Dexter’s heart dropped into his stomach. He wasn’t that well-hidden.","The old man raised a finger.","Come here.","Dexter pointed at his own chest, stunned.","The old man rolled his eyes, took a breath, and just stepped off the balcony.","Five stories.","Dexter eyes popped open, but the old man didn’t hit the ground like a sack of bricks. He landed like he was stepping off a curb—no sound, no impact, just a light tap of his sandals.","He walked over to the hedge, looking at Dexter with with a dangerous smile.","\"Interesting,\" he said, his voice sounding like gravel. He looked Dexter up and down, and for a second, Dexter felt like he was being X-rayed. \"A mere C-Rank affinity... and yet, you’re trying to steal my technique.\"","The old man’s smile went cold. The air suddenly felt like it was pressing down on Dexter’s shoulders.","\"Tell me, boy,\" the old man whispered. \"Are you not afraid of dying?\""]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24 | We’re Sorry!","paragraphs":["\"Tell me, boy...\"","\"Are you not afraid of dying?\"","Dexter eyes blinked as he felt a weight landed on his shoulder. Even with his strength, he felt his knee almost buckling and an illusion of an angry god with blue burning flames appeared behind the man.","Dexter throat perched and he opened his mouth,","But before a single word could leave his lips —","His expression changed instantly.","A sudden sharp sensation shot through his mind. It was like an ice pick driving deep into his skull. His Frost Sense, the ability that connected him to Selene’s unique energy.","Selene.","She was having another episode.","Dexter’s pupils contracted. His entire body went rigid for half a second. The old man noticed the change immediately but said nothing, only watching with curious eyes.","Without even bothering to answer the old man’s question, Dexter abruptly turned around.","\"Please stay here. I’ll be right back.\"","And then like the pressure the old man was putting on him was nothing more than paper weight—","He vanished.","BOOM!","His body exploded forward with terrifying speed. The floor tiles beneath his previous position cracked from the sudden release of force.","Using Flame Burst, Dexter shot through the hotel pathways like a meteor. The mana around his legs combusted and propelled him forward in violent bursts.","The polished hotel corridors became a blur around him. Golden wall lamps streaked past like lines of fire. Several customers walking nearby only felt a gust of scorching wind sweep past them. One woman’s dress fluttered wildly. A man’s hat flew off his head and tumbled down the hallway.","They froze in shock, their eyes wide and mouths hanging open.","\"What was that?!\" one of them shouted.","But Dexter was already gone. He ignored everything. The surprised gasps, the confused shouts, all of it faded into background noise. He pushed more mana into Flame Burst. The technique roared to life with even greater intensity. His body accelerated even faster. The air around him rippled with heat.","His Brain rapidly process things and he realized the elevator would be too slow.","He immediately changed direction and sprinted straight for the stairway. His right shoulder slammed into the stairwell door, bursting it open without slowing down.","His footsteps struck the stairs like explosions.","Bang. Bang. Bang. Bang.","In seconds—","He reached the hotel room.","BANG!","And the moment Dexter stepped inside, cold air slammed into his face like a wall. The temperature had dropped so low that his skin prickled with frost.","The room had turned into an ice chamber.","Frost covered the walls in thick white layers. The windows were frozen solid, completely with ice crystals spreading in spiral patterns. The carpet crunched under his boots. The entire bed was buried under layers of ice crystals that glittered in the dim light.","And on top of the bed—","Selene was convulsing violently.","Her entire body trembled uncontrollably as freezing energy leaked from her skin in visible waves. Her face was pale as death. Her lips were blue. Her fingers clawed at the frozen sheets. Frost spread outward from her body with every convulsion, creeping across the bed and up the walls.","At the side of the bed sat Mira in her wheelchair.","Beside her was Lyra, her smart glasses resting over her eyes. The AI writing the sounds it could hear to the best of its abilities.","Both girls stared at Selene with furrowed brows, worry evident on their faces.","Dexter acted instantly.","His right hand erupted into crimson flames. The fire roared to life, casting dancing shadows across the frozen walls.","The Berserk Flame Demon Bloodline activated fully, flooding his veins with lava. The flames rapidly melted the thick ice covering parts of the room. Steam immediately rose into the air, filling the space with a thick fog.","Without hesitation, Dexter reached into his pocket and pulled out the Suppressant Serum, took her arm and injected the serum and injected the liquid into her bloodstream.","Slowly, the violent shaking stopped. Selene’s convulsing body gradually relaxed. Her breathing, turned soft as the frost spreading throughout the room began receding, pulling back toward her body.","She fell asleep. Her face, which had been twisted in pain, softened into peace.","Dexter exhaled deeply","\"That was too close...\"","He activated his bloodline further and heatwaves spread through the room in turning the remaining frost into water mad then into steam.","Within moments, the bed had completely dried and the temperature turned normal.","Dexter carefully covered Selene with several thick blankets. He tucked the edges around her shoulders.","He paused as he at her stunning face, her silver hair spread out across the bed.","She looked both angelic and also fragile buried under all that fabric.","Suddenly, her eyes fluttered open. And she looked directly at Dexter.","For a moment, his breath caught in his throat.","But he then relaxed when he remembered she was blind. But she definitely knew he was still there.","He inhaled and left the bed to turn to Mira and Lyra.","Both girls were staring at him silently with an unreadable expression.","The room fell silent for several seconds","Finally, Dexter spoke. His voice was calm but flat.","\"If you two are hungry... I can call room service. I can order food for you.\"","Mira quietly shook her head. \"I’m not hungry.\"","Lyra’s glasses flickered. The words automatically displayed across the lenses. Strangely the foodie Lyra also shook her head.","Dexter raised an eyebrow in surprise. She had almost finished the entire hotel’s food this morning and afternoon, what’s wrong now?","He didn’t bother to ask, he turned around, preparing to leave. The old man was still waiting downstairs.","But suddenly—","A very soft voice sounded behind him. So soft he almost thought he imagined it.","\"...We’re sorry.\"","Dexter froze. His hand stopped just before reaching the door handle. For a long moment, he did not move. He did not even breathe. The words echoed in his mind, repeating over and over.","He slowly turned around. His expression was unreadable. His voice was quiet, careful.","\"What did you say?\"","Then—","Lyra spoke again. This time louder. Her voice was still soft, but there was strength behind it now. A strength that had not been there before.","\"We’re sorry.\"","Dexter stood still. He looked at Lyra. Then at Mira. Both girls were looking at him directly. Not avoiding his gaze.","’Did I hear wrong? ’","For a moment, he genuinely thought he had misheard.","He had been cold towards them throughout their stay here since they didn’t care for him nor themselves, he would only take care of them, earn rewards from the system and grow stronger.","After all, they had also remained silent toward him. They had not tried to bridge the gap. So what changed?","Then Mira lowered her head. Her dark hair fell forward as she spoke quietly.","\"We are sorry... for everything. And... thank you.\"","The words made Dexter emotional than he had he’d preferred to be.","Inside him, countless emotions surged at once, like a dam breaking. All the feelings he had suppressed came flooding back.","He wanted to complain. He wanted to yell. He wanted to ask them why they gave up so easily.","He wanted to remind them how lucky they were. They had lived normal lives for years before losing everything. They had seen the sky. They had walked on their own feet. They had experienced the world.","Meanwhile, some people were born blind. Some were born crippled. Some were born deaf. Some never once had the chance to experience life properly, not even for a single day. He wanted to say all of that. He wanted to make them understand how precious their lives were.","But somehow—","Those simple words erased all his anger."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25 | The Bet With The Strange Old Man","paragraphs":["\"You’re welcome.\"","The tension in the room finally disappeared.","Dexter rubbed the back of his head awkwardly making the corner of Mira’s mouth twitch upward.","\"There’s something I need to do,\" Dexter said. \"I’ll be back soon.\"","Mira suddenly smirked.","\"Oh? Do you have another wife hiding somewhere?\"","For the first time in two days, Dexter laughed at her banter.","He crossed his arms and raised an eyebrow. \"Are you jealous?\"","Mira snorted coldly but her eyes were brighter now. \"Please.\"","At the side, a faint smile tugged at Lyra’s usually cold lips.","Seeing their expressions, Dexter felt unexpectedly relieved.","\"I will be back in a bit. Don’t open the door for anyone other then me.\"","The girls nodded their heads.","Without wasting another second, he left the room. The door clicked shut behind him.","---","Outside, the old man was still standing exactly where Dexter had left him. Not a single inch moved. His posture was straight. His hands were clasped behind his back.","Dexter jogged over and wiped sweat from his forehead. His breathing was slightly heavy from the sprint.","The old man stared at him sharply.","Then said flatly, \"You actually left me standing here.\"","Dexter scratched his head awkwardly.","’I had to save one of my wives.’ but he didn’t say that.","\"It was... a matter of life and death.\"","The old man stared for several seconds. His expression was difficult to read. Then he nodded slowly. \"I see.\"","Suddenly, the old man tilted his head.","\"Let us make a deal.\"","Dexter blinked. A deal? \"What kind of deal?\"","The old man smiled faintly. \"If you manage to learn my technique for the duration of your stay here, I shall give you a gift.\"","Dexter’s expression shifted. A slight furrow on his brow. Bur internally he was laughing like a mad man.","’This old man doesn’t know what he’s walking into! Hahahaha!’","Externally, he sighed and puffed out his chest.","\"As long as you repeatedly demonstrate the technique,\" Dexter said, \"I can learn it in one day.\"","The old man froze and his eyes widened slightly. He had expected the boy to say a month. Maybe longer, wanting to play with his new toy...But a day?","\"One day?\" The old man’s voice was sharp with disbelief.","Dexter nodded firmly. \"One day.\"","Sddenly the old man laughed loudly. \"Hahaha. Arrogant, simple arrogant! The most talented take years to learn and you want to learn it in one day? Interesting. Very interesting.\" He stroked his long gray beard.","\"Fine. I’ll raise the stakes.\"","Dexter leaned forward slightly, curious.","\"If you can truly learn my technique in one day, I won’t simply give you an ordinary gift.\" His eyes gleamed with excitement. \"I will give you a treasure and not only that, I shall let you marry my granddaughter.\"","Dexter’s eyes widened slightly. A treasure from a powerhouse would definitely be powerful.","But the old man wasn’t done. He raised a single finger.","But then the granddaughter part made Dexter shake his head.","’I already have three women and they are giving me headache. One more would kill me!’","Dexter immediately shook his head. His response was instant, almost reflexive. \"No.\"","The old man blinked. His raised finger stayed frozen in the air. He looked genuinely caught off guard for the first time.","Dexter sighed. He ran a hand through his hair. \"I already have enough wives as it is.\"","For the first time, the old man looked genuinely surprised.","The he looked up at the stars","\"It is late. Come tomorrow morning. From sunrise until sundown. If you fail to learn the technique before sunset, the deal ends.\"","Dexter smiled. The challenge was set. \"Deal.\"","He bid farewell with a respectful nod and returned to his room.","---","Later that night, Dexter resumed taking care of the girls.","He helped Mira to the bathroom, removed her clothes without looking and getting tempted.","Only the face and of a single woman clouded his mind.","He helped her use the toilet, took her to the shower and washed her up with sponge and shampoo.","Her breasts weren’t massive but they stood firm and could be cupped on one hand.","They were milky white and the areola was actually very pink like a rose bud.","His hands went down her belly then between her legs, slowly caressing the center with care.","Mira let out a soft a gasp but Dexter pretended not to care. He went down her thighs one by one. They were strong dje to her previous exercise before she got crippled.","With this temptation, any man would be rock hard and tempted. However Dexter’s mind was else where or with someone else.","\"Are you gay? \"","’What the hell?’","Dexter was caught of guard and he almost stumbled on the bathroom floor.","He glared at her.","\"If I was gay, would I marry you? Why would you even ask that? \"","\"Well. You had no choice but to marry us. And I asked because you’re not hard.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes.","\"Can’t I be tired? Why did you associate me with being gay?\"","Mira looked down at his crotch then shook her head. \"I’ve never seen you hard.\"","Dexter suddenly smirked any wagged his eyebrows playfully.","\"Why? Do you want to see me aroused? If I was, do you want to do something about it? \"","\"Yes.\"","Dexter wagging eyebrows froze.","He couldn’t tell if she was serious or not. He shook his heard.","\"You’re insane.\"","The silence was awkward.","He got a new pad, fixed it and wore her panties for her. Then he carried her back gently on the bed.","Everything proceeded normally. Eventually, all three girls appeared to fall asleep.","Dexter walked toward the sofa in the main room. He prepared to rest, sinking into the cushions and closing his eyes.","But then—","He suddenly stopped. His enhanced hearing, picked up something unusual. From the bedroom, he heard synchronized breathing patterns. It wasn’t like normal breathing but like cultivating.","And occasionally, faint grunts of pain that were quickly suppressed.","Dexter narrowed his eyes.","They were cultivating again. Despite their damaged meridians. Despite the pain that must be shooting through their bodies every time they tried to channel mana and the miniscule amount of mana they would gain from that, they were still forcing themselves to continue.","Dexter stared toward the bedroom door silently. His expression was complicated.","’Looks like... it’s time I give them their present.’"]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26 | Gifting The Girls Talents!","paragraphs":["The girls are cultivating even with their shattered meridians and the pain it would cause them.","And yet they persisted.","A faint smile tugged at the corners of Dexter’s lips. There was pride in that smile, yes, but also guilt. He wishes he could help them better.","[Ding!]","The familiar notification materialized before him.","[10,000 Times Investment System Activated.]","[Multiplier: 100x.]","Dexter blinked with surprise. The 100x multiplier was the first time since three days he got it.","[You sincerely took care of your wife: Mira.]","[Reconciled with your wives, gave them hope for pone more trial at life]","[Evaluating rewards...]","[Rewards Granted.]","One by one, the notifications began cascading before him.","[Reward 1: Type-1 Relic Obtained.]","[Rainbow Feather Clothing.]","A defensive armor relic capable of adapting to the wearer’s body while offering excellent protection. The fabric shifts and morphs to accommodate any body type, becoming nearly weightless while maintaining defensive capabilities equivalent to military-grade body armor.","Dexter’s eyes widened ur was actually a relic for such a simple task?","[Reward 2: Grade-2 Herb Obtained.]","[Star-Shaped Leaf.]","A soothing medicinal herb capable of being brewed into tea. Calms the nervous system, restores mental fatigue, and when processed correctly, can accelerate the natural healing processes of the body. The leaves emit a gentle, starlight-like shimmer when exposed to moonlight.","[Reward 4: Grade-2 Herb Obtained.]","[Icy Lotus Leaf.]","A rare medicinal herb with cooling properties capable of stabilizing unstable mana fluctuations. Particularly effective for cultivators experiencing disruption in their energy circulation.","These herbs... they were exactly what the girls needed. Grade-2 medicinal herbs were extraordinarily difficult to obtain, and these particular varieties addressed precisely the issues the girls were facing with their damaged meridians.","[Reward 5: Skill Acquired.]","[Tier-2 36 Styles Massage Technique.]","A specialized body massage technique capable of relieving physical pain to the maximum degree, softening muscles, accelerating blood circulation, and increasing healing speed by 200% when used on others.","Dexter stared at the final notification, and he smiled because it was perfect for the girls.","During the past two days, although he had still been caring for the girls... he had been angry. His actions had not been sincere. That was why the system had not activated.","But now, after reconciling with them, he had genuinely cared for Mira.","And the system had responded.","His gaze shifted toward the bedroom door. Through it, he could still hear the girls’ strained breathing, through the walls.","And suddenly, he made a decision.","’I should help them’","He waited for about an hour when they finally fell asleep.","Dexter stood up and entered the bedroom.","The lights remained dim, just a small lamp on the bedside table casting a warm, amber glow across the room. All three girls were lying on the bed, their bodies arranged in a row beneath the covers.","Asleep.","Dexter stood there for a moment.","\"Awake?\"’","No one answered.","Then slowly, Dexter approached Mira first. She was sleeping closest to the edge of the bed, her amber hair spread across the pillow like fire captured in silk. Even in sleep, there was a certain fierceness to her features.","Carefully, he reached out and gently stroked her hair. The strands were softer than he had expected. At the same time, he spoke inwardly.","’System. Integrate Mana Arm into host.’","Immediately— a notification appeared in his vision, its text floating in the air like a holographic display only he could see.","[Do you wish to integrate ability: Mana Arm into designated host?]","Dexter answered instantly, without hesitation.","’Yes.’","A soft, faint eneegy passed through his palm and transmitted onto Mira.","Her sleeping expression didn’t change. It was as if nothing had happened.","Dexter exhaled softly, then quietly, he moved toward the middle of the bed.","Selene.","She was sleeping peacefully beneath the blankets, her dark hair a stark contrast to the white pillow.","Dexter gently touched her forehead, his fingers barely making contact with her skin.","System. Integrate D-Rank Talent Card: Echolocation.","[Do you wish to integrate D-Rank Talent Card: Echolocation into designated host?]","Yes.","The same faint energy emerged, flowing from his palm into her body like a stream finding its way to the sea. Selene’s eyelashes trembled slightly—but she remained asleep.","Dexter nodded to himself, in satisfaction.","Her glasses had been placed on the bedside table, leaving her face unobstructed.","Dexter gently brushed aside a strand of hair that had fallen across her face, tucking it behind her ear. Then activated the final gift.","System. Integrate D-Rank Talent Card: Telepathy.","[Do you wish to integrate D-Rank Talent Card: Telepathy into designated host?]","Yes.","The energy transferred silently into her body.","Dexter stared at the three girls quietly, his heart swelling with an emotion he couldn’t quite name. It wasn’t love, their relationship was too complicated, but it was something. Maybe responsibility?","None of them seemed to notice anything unusual.","Or so he thought.","Because in reality— two of them weren’t asleep.","Lyra had been pretending, her mind racing with questions about what Dexter was doing. And Mira— Mira had also been pretending.","Mira kept her eyes shut tightly, her body rigid with the effort of remaining still. But internally, she was confused.","\"Why is this pervert touching our heads in the middle of the night?\"","’I heard some people are into feet, is he not hair?’","A slight frown formed on her face. Then inwardly she muttered— Perverted gay guy...","Dexter, completely unaware of her thoughts wmiled as he completed his mission.","Satisfied with his secret gifts, he turned and made his way out of the bedroom without making another sound, closing the door behind him with a soft click.","Returning to the living room, he lay down on the sofa, staring up at the ceiling. Tomorrow would be an important day. The challenge with the old man. Learning the legendary technique. If everything went well, he would obtain not only a Legendary Technique but possibly another priceless reward.","Slowly— he closed his eyes."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27 | Hero Association Representative","paragraphs":["The morning came faster than expected, pale light seeping through the windows and painting the room in shades of gray and gold. Dexter woke with a start, momentarily disoriented before remembering where he was and what lay ahead. After washing up, he quickly changed clothes and prepared to leave, his movements efficient despite the early hour.","6:00 AM.","Just as he reached for the door—","Knock. Knock.","The sound was unexpected, making Dexter paused, his hand hovering inches from the doorknob. His brows furrowed slightly. He hadn’t ordered room service. Who could possibly be here this early?","Curious, and with a slight sense, he walked toward the door and opened it.","The moment the door swung open— both of them froze.","Dexter’s eyes widened, stunned and the woman standing in the hallway had equally widened eyes, her hand still raised in the position of having just knocked.","\"...Rachel?\"","Dexter couldn’t believe she was herw right now.","It had been a day they saw each other last.","The woman blinked, her long black lashes fluttered, she was just as shocked as his. \"Dexter?\"","Then Rachel tilted her head, a habitual gesture he remembered well from the bar.","\"What are you doing here?\"","Dexter scratched his cheek awkwardly, feeling suddenly self-conscious about his appearance. \"Well...\" he began, searching for the right words. \"This is where I’ve been staying ever since the monster outbreak destroyed our street.\"","Rachel frowned slightly, the expression pulling at features that were, if anything, even more beautiful than he remembered. \"Oh. So you were affected too?\"","Dexter nodded, \"Yeah.\"","Then he looked at her curiously, taking in her professional attire, it suggested she wasn’t here by accident. \"What about you? What are you doing here?\"","Rachel smiled. \"I’m the representative from the Hero Association assigned to handle matters regarding your damaged home...\" She paused, as if choosing her next words carefully. \"And... your situation.\"","Understanding flashed across Dexter’s face. The Hero told them they would send a representative in three days. So she’s the one they sent.","\"Ah.\" He stepped aside, gesturing into the suit. \"Come in.\"","Rachel nodded and stepped inside, and as she passed by him, Dexter found himself momentarily staring. She was still incredibly pretty. And the moment she passed by, a pleasant fragrance reached his nose. Vanilla. Mixed with jasmine.","Shaking away the thought with, Dexter closed the door behind him. \"You want something to drink?\"","Rachel nodded, already scanning the room. \"A soft drink is fine.\"","Dexter walked toward the fridge and handed her a cold bottle, the condensation wetting his fingers. But the moment Rachel stepped fully into the living room, she froze.","Three women were present.","Mira sat in her wheelchair near the television, her amber hair cascading over her shoulders.","Lyra stood quietly nearby, glasses resting over her eyes, her expression carefully neutral as she assessed the newcomer.","Selene sat silently on the couch, staring blankly ahead.","Rachel blinked several times as though hadn’t comprehended what she was seeing.","She turned toward Dexter, her expression had become very strange.","\"I thought...\" She hesitated, as if unsure whether to voice what was on her mind. Then asked carefully— \"...you were joking.\"","Dexter frowned, not following her train of thought. \"About what?\"","Rachel stared at the girls, then back at him. \"You actually have three wives?\"","Dexter shrugged, feeling suddenly uncomfortable under the combined attention of four women. \"Well... I tried telling you.\"","At that exact moment, Mira slowly turned her head.","Ber suspicious gaze moved between both of them, then she narrowed her eyes, as her face darkened.","\"...Do you two know each other?\"","Rachel immediately straightened her posture, her professional demeanor snapping back into place.","\"No.\" She caught herself, realizing how defensive that sounded.","She cleared her throat, then quickly corrected herself. \"I mean... we met briefly before.\"","She extended a hand politely toward Mira, the gesture formal and businesslike. \"Rachel. Representative from the Hero Association. I’m here to discuss matters regarding your current situation.\"","Mira stared at her for several seconds, her gaze unblinking.","Then slowly, a smirk spread across her face.","\"No.\"","Rachel blinked, clearly not expecting that response. \"No...?\"","Mira rolled her eyes.","\"It feels like something else.\"","Her eyes moved between Rachel and Dexter with the precision of a predator tracking prey.","Then she casually asked— \"Did you two hook up?\"","Dexter nearly choked out on his own spit.","Rachel’s face stiffened, a faint flush creeping up her neck that she quickly suppressed it.","Dexter immediately coughed awkwardly, trying to regain his composure. \"What kind of question is that?\"","Mira smirked wider, clearly enjoying his discomfort. \"Well?\"","Dexter rolled his eyes, feeling a headache beginning to form behind his temples. \"We’re married. Why would I sleep with someone else?\"","Mira simply gave him a mocking smile, she clearly didn’t believe him but didn’t press the matter either.","She turned away without another word, ignoring then both.","The atmosphere immediately became awkward.","At the side Selene and Lyra had also shifted their attention. Unlike before, they weren’t ignoring the conversation. Instead— they were staring directly at Rachel.","Dexter noticed immediately. And to his surprise, it almost looked like they were trying to intimidate her.","Like they were marking their territory.","For some reason— that made him smile slightly, a warm feeling spreading through his chest despite the awkwardness of the situation.","Rachel quickly returned to business, clearly eager to move past the uncomfortable exchange.","She crossed one leg over the other and spoke professionally, her voice regaining its measured cadence. \"The repairs on your house are nearly complete. By tomorrow, everything should be fully restored. You and your family can move back in.\"","Dexter nodded. \"That’s good.\"","Rachel continued, her eyes focused on her tablet as she scrolled through information. \"There’s also the matter regarding the sixteen beasts you killed during the outbreak. Their carcasses have been processed. The Nexus Points and compensation have already been calculated.\"","Dexter listened carefully, his interest piqued. Nexus Points were the currency of the hero world, used to purchase everything from weapons to techniques to rare materials and could be used for cultivation."]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28 | Meeting Rachael!","paragraphs":["Rachel looked up from her tablet. \"The processed value of the beast carcasses amounts to approximately... sixty thousand dollars. That is the maximum compensation we were able to extract from the remains.\"","Dexter thought for a moment, doing quick mental calculations. It was a significant sum and with his system he could double it.","But he wanted more.","Then he shook his head. \"I’ll take half the money.\"","Rachel frowned, clearly not expecting that response. \"And the other half?\"","Dexter smiled, a plan already forming in his mind. \"I want the half of the monster nexus core given to me.\"","Rachel immediately shook her head, her expression apologetic but firm. \"That won’t be possible.\"","Dexter blinked, not understanding the refusal. \"Why?\"","Rachel explained calmly, her tone suggesting this was a common misconception she had to address regularly. \"Nexus cores can only be issued to registered heroes. You’re currently unlicensed. If you want access to resources... you’ll need to officially register with the Hero Association first.\"","Dexter slowly nodded, processing this information.","\"I see.\" Then he smiled,","\"Well... looks like I’ll have to become a licensed hero then.\"","Rachel smiled back, the expression transforming her face from attractive to genuinely beautiful. \"I figured you’d say that.\"","Then her expression shifted, becoming more personal. \"From what I’ve heard... you killed beasts two levels above your rank during the outbreak.\" She leaned slightly closer, her vanilla-jasmine scent washing over him again. \"With feats like that... passing the Hero Association exam shouldn’t be difficult for you.\"","Dexter smiled awkwardly, feeling uncomfortable with the praise. \"Thanks.\"","For a brief second— neither spoke.","\"Well then, I will be leaving.\"","Then suddenly, Rachel stood up and before Dexter could react— she stepped forward. And hugged him.","Dexter froze, his body going rigid with surprise before instinct took over and he used one hand to hug her back.","Rachel slowly pulled away, and when she did, a strange smile had formed on her lips.","She lightly licked her lower lip.","Then she said softly. \"I’ll be seeing you very soon.\"","With that, she turned around and left.","Dexter stared at the closed door for several seconds, then shook his head and chuckled.","Then he turned around.","The moment he did— Mira had opened her eyes. And was glaring directly at him.","\"So...\" She said slowly, each word measured and precise. \"That’s who you’ve been going out to see these past two days.\"","Dexter stared at her blankly. Then sighed. \"She’s not. And I already have the three of you to deal with. Why would I want another woman added into the mix?\"","Mira narrowed her eyes, her glare intensifying. \"Oh? So now we’re burdens?\"","Dexter immediately groaned, running a hand through his hair in frustration. \"There you go twisting my words again. You know that’s not what I meant.\"","Mira simply snorted.","Dexter shook his head helplessly, then looked at all three girls, taking in their varied expressions. \"Do any of you need anything? Food? Room service?\"","Lyra immediately nodded. Mira remained silent, still pouting.","Selene said nothing, but judging by her expression— she was clearly still annoyed, though whether at him or at Rachel or at the situation in general was impossible to tell.","Dexter sighed, the sound carrying an acceptance of his role in this strange domestic dynamic they had developed. \"Fine. I’ll order food.\"","While waiting for room service, he suddenly remembered the herbs he had obtained from the system.","The Star-Shaped Leaf and Icy Lotus Leaf. A thought crossed his mind.","Quietly, so as not to attract attention, accepted the rears and they appeared in his hands as if materializing from thin air, their presence somehow feeling both natural and otherworldly.","The Star-Shaped Leaf lived up to its name, its five points arranged in a perfect star pattern, each point tipped with a faint luminescence that seemed to pulse gently.","The Icy Lotus Leaf was its opposite in appearance, a deep blue-green color that seemed to radiate cold even without direct contact.","Walking toward the kitchen area— he carefully prepared tea using both ingredients, following instincts of a Master Chef.","A soothing aroma slowly began spreading through the room, It was unlike any tea Dexter had ever encountered, carrying with it a sense of calm that seemed to seep directly into the bones.","Minutes later— Dexter returned carrying three cups, each one steam rising in delicate spirals. Placing them on trays, he handed one to each girl.","Mira frowned suspiciously, eyeing the cup as if it might contain poison. \"What kind of tea is this?\"","Dexter simply crossed his arms, not rising to her suspicion. \"Just drink it.\"","Mira clicked her tongue, the sound sharp with irritation. She still felt annoyed after seeing Rachel earlier, the woman’s obvious familiarity with Dexter stirring feelings she didn’t want to examine too closely. So naturally— she wanted to refuse, out of pure spite.","But then— the aroma reached her nose.","A strange sensation immediately spread through her body. Warm. Refreshing. Like sunlight breaking through clouds on a winter day, or the first breath of spring air after months of cold.","Even before drinking it, she felt her entire body becoming lighter, the constant background ache that had become so familiar she had almost stopped noticing it beginning to fade.","Her eyes widened slightly,","’What... is this?’","---","Mira opened her mouth and Dexter poured the entire tea in her mouth.","As it hit her throat, her expression changed instantly.","A strange sensation immediately spread through her body.","Warm. Refreshing.","Even before drinking it, she felt her entire body becoming lighter.","Her eyes widened slightly.","’ What... is this?’","The moment Dexter brought the tea to her lips and she took the first sip—","Her lips quivered.","She could feel mana moving brought her body.","Not just moving—","It was flowing through her body far more smoothly than usual.","Even more shocking, it wasn’t painful and she could feel her damaged meridians being nourished.","Tiny strands of energy were gently repairing the broken channels inside her body.","Her breathing immediately grew heavier.","She looked at Dexter then and the teacup he was holding, clearly stunned beyond words.","[A/N: 26 more powerstones to mass release!]","[This extra one is a teaser!]"]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29 | Learning The Technique (100 PS Bonus - )","paragraphs":["\"Tell me. Where did you get it?\"","Dexter simply smiled but said nothing.","Mira stared at him for several seconds, then quietly looked away.","She didn’t push further.","Instead, she drank the entire cup in one go.","Then immediately closed her eyes.","Mana began circulating through her body as she focused entirely on guiding the medicinal energy toward her damaged meridians.","At the side—","Lyra and Selene had heard the entire conversation.","At first, both were skeptical.","But after seeing Mira’s reaction—","They immediately drank theirs too.","The effect was instantaneous.","Their breathing immediately grew heavier.","Mana fluctuations surrounded both of them.","Without wasting another second—","They closed their eyes and began circulating the medicinal energy through their own damaged channels.","Dexter smiled faintly as he watched them.","Thankfully—","The herbs he received from the system were plentiful.","Nearly a pound each.","Enough for them to continue drinking for at least a week.","Unfortunately...","There was one drawback.","Rewards obtained from the system...","Could not be reused to trigger new rewards.","Otherwise—","This would have been ridiculously overpowered.","He needed fresh methods of gaining rewards.","Just then— Knock. Knock.","The room service had arrived. A staff member rolled a tray of food into the room, the smells of fresh bread, cooked eggs, and steaming meat filling the space.","After taking the tray, Dexter closed the door behind him. \"The food is here,\"","But none of the girls responded. All three remained seated silently, eyes shut, completely focused on circulating the medicinal energy through their damaged meridians.","Dexter chuckled softly. Then suddenly— a thought crossed his mind, sobering his mood.","The Divine Pill.","The reward he had obtained earlier, before his reconciliation with the girls. It had the power to completely repair one damaged body.","But he only had one.","One pill.","If he gave it to Mira— then Selene and Lyra would be left out. If he gave it to Selene, the other two might feel abandoned, If he gave it to Lyra— same problem.","No matter what— someone would feel left behind. And in a relationship as fragile and complicated as theirs, that could create unnecessary tension, could reopen wounds that had only just begun to heal.","After thinking for a moment, weighing the options in his mind— Dexter shook his head. Not yet. I’ll wait.","Quietly, he moved toward the door, casting one last look at the three women who had become such an unexpected and important part of his life. \"I’ll be back soon.\"","None of them answered. All three were still fully immersed in cultivation, their bodies still, their breathing synchronized with the flow of energy through their systems.","---","Outside— the old man was already waiting. But unlike before— this time he wasn’t standing on the balcony.","Instead, he stood calmly in the open hotel courtyard below, hands clasped behind his back, his posture somehow both relaxed and focused.","As though he had been waiting for a long time.","Dexter approached quietly and greeted. \"Good morning.\"","The old man nodded. Then asked calmly. \"Are you ready?\"","Dexter smiled, feeling a strange mixture of anticipation and nervousness. \"Yes.\"","The old man said nothing further.","Instead, he slowly inhaled, his chest expanding with a deep breath that seemed to pull in more air than his frame should have been able to contain. Then exhaled, the release lasting far longer than any normal breath should.","And instantly. his aura changed.","Without warning, he began moving. His body entered the first form, then the second. Then the third. His breathing shifted with every movement, each inhale and exhale.","At that exact moment, a system notification appeared before Dexter, its text flickering rapidly as it processed what it was observing.","[Analyzing Legendary Technique...]","[Progress: 25%]","Then— 26%... 27%... 28%...","The percentage began climbing steadily,","Twenty minutes later— the old man completed one full cycle, He stopped and looked at Dexter, his eyes sharp and assessing.","\"Did you get it?\"","Dexter smiled faintly and replied. \"Getting there.\"","The old man narrowed his eyes, clearly dissatisfied with that answer but not surprised by it either. Then immediately began again.","And again.","And again.","Over and over.","Repeated endlessly.","The hours passed. Morning slowly turned into afternoon, the sun climbing higher in the sky until it was directly on top of them.","Heat covered the courtyard, the air shimmering with thermal distortion,","Yet, the old man continued moving. Again. Again. Again. Like a machine.","Four full hours passed.","And through it all, there wasn’t a single bead of sweat on the old man’s body.","Dexter watched in stunned silence, his respect for the old man growing with each passing hour.","Even standing nearby, Dexter could feel an invisible pressure radiating from the old man, and he knew the man was probably a hidden powerhouse.","[Ding!]","[Extraction of Legendary-Tier Technique Successful.]","[You have learned...]"]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30 | Grand Cosmos Scripture","paragraphs":["The moment the notification appeared before Dexter— his eyes immediately locked onto the description, drinking in every word as if his life depended on it.","---","═══════════════════════════════════════","[Grand Cosmos Scripture]","(Seventh-Tier )","═══════════════════════════════════════","Description:","A legendary cultivation technique that abandons the traditional path of meridians and transforms the human body into a miniature universe.","Upon activation, dormant Star Nodes hidden throughout the body awaken one by one. Each Star Node functions as an independent celestial core capable of storing vast quantities of mana.","Unlike ordinary cultivators, practitioners of the Grand Cosmos Scripture do not circulate mana through meridians. Instead, every awakened Star Node generates a powerful gravitational force, automatically drawing surrounding mana into itself while the user meditates.","Once a Star Node reaches full capacity, it permanently strengthens the body and serves as an inexhaustible source of mana. The cultivator may then awaken the next Star Node.","═══════════════════════════════════════","Current Star Nodes: 0/360","First Firmament : 1–100 Star Nodes","Second Firmament : 101–200 Star Nodes","Third Firmament : 201–300 Star Nodes","Grand Firmament : 301–360 Star Nodes","═══════════════════════════════════════","Effects:","• Eliminates the need for meridian-based cultivation.","• Awakened Star Nodes automatically absorb surrounding mana during meditation.","• Every Star Node acts as an independent mana reservoir.","• Massively increases total mana capacity.","• Permanently enhances physique with each awakened Star Node.","• Cultivation speed increases as additional Star Nodes are awakened.","• Damage to one Star Node does not affect the others.","═══════════════════════════════════════","Ultimate Effect:","When all 360 Star Nodes are completely filled with mana, they resonate as one, forming a complete Inner Cosmos.","The practitioner will automatically break through the Peak Ultra Warrior Realm and become Legendary.","No bottlenecks.","No breakthrough pills.","No external assistance.","═══════════════════════════════════════","Dexter stood there frozen in shock.","This technique... it was perfect. Absolutely, impossibly perfect.","His thoughts immediately drifted toward Mira, Lyra, and Selene. All three of them had suffered catastrophic damage to their meridians. The pathways they once used to cultivate had been shattered almost beyond repair, leaving them crippled in ways that went beyond physical injury. Without a divine-tier treasure— recovery was nearly impossible.","And even then... he only had one Divine Pill. One. If he gave it to one girl— the other two would inevitably feel left out, would wonder why they hadn’t been chosen, would feel their worth measured and found wanting. It would create resentment, would drive wedges between people who were only just beginning to come together.","But this technique... this changed everything.","The Grand Cosmos Scripture completely abandoned meridian-based cultivation. It didn’t need meridians at all. Meaning, the girls could cultivate again.","Dexter’s eyes widened further as he smiled at the girls.","The technique... was priceless. Beyond priceless. It was the kind of treasure that families would go to war over, that nations would sacrifice generations to obtain.","And he had just learned it by watching an old man practice for a few hours.","---","At that exact moment— the old man noticed Dexter’s strange expression. His brows slowly furrowed.","’Don’t tell me... this brat is distracted while I’m teaching him?’","The old man narrowed his eyes, a spark of irritation flaring to life.","’Well... he doesn’t know what happens if he loses the bet. I suppose I should keep teaching him seriously for now, make sure he has every opportunity to succeed before I collect my winnings.’","A dangerous glint flashed through his eyes, then he resumed practicing, preparing to demonstrate the technique again.","But suddenly, and he was in quite disbelief by what he saw.","Because something impossible was happening.","Dexter had suddenly begun breathing strangely, the pattern matching exactly what the old man had been demonstrating. The breathing pattern perfectly synchronized with the technique, each inhale and exhale hitting the precise timing required.","The old man’s eyes widened slightly. Them more. Then more again.","Because Dexter had begun copying him. No. Not copying. Learning.","The Grand Cosmos Scripture had two components. The first— the Meditation Aspect. A breathing technique designed to gather mana and guide it into hidden Star Nodes. The second— the Physical Aspect. A sequence of body movements designed to stimulate the body, open every pore, and dramatically increase mana absorption.","Using both together created perfect synergy, each aspect amplifying the effects of the other. While it was possible to cultivate using meditation alone— combining both aspects, increased efficiency.","And right now— Dexter was performing both. Perfectly.","The old man stood completely frozen, his own practice abandoned as he watched in disbelief. His jaw slowly dropped, also low it almost hit devil’s head.","He couldn’t believe what he was seeing.","’Impossible!’","It hasn’t even been a day.","’How...?’ ’How the hell did he learn it already?’","The old man stared at Dexter as if looking at a monster, his previous confidence crumbling to shock. What kind of freak is this? No... What kind of demon is this?","Meanwhile— Dexter remained completely focused, unaware of the old man’s reaction, his entire being consumed by the effort of performing the technique for the first time.","His body moved through the cultivation forms.","Unlike the old man— he wasn’t proficient yet. His movements were rough, slightly stiff, unrefined.","Because of that— it took him almost forty minutes to complete one full cycle. Twice as long as the old man.","By the time he finished— sweat covered his entire body, soaking through his clothes and dripping from his chin onto the courtyard stones.","His chest rose heavily, as his lungs burned.","He could feel mana entering his body, could sense the energy being drawn in by the technique’s innate properties. But, nothing happened.","No Star Node had awakened. Which meant— he still hadn’t located the first dormant node inside his body.","Dexter wiped sweat from his forehead, his arm feeling heavy with exhaustion.","Then looked toward the old man, expecting to see satisfaction or approval or at least acknowledgment of his effort.","Only to freeze.","The old man was staring at him with his mouth wide open, an expression of pure, shock and something else was in the old man’s face.","It was so completely out of character with the composed, superior demeanor he had displayed until now, that Dexter found himself momentarily confused.","Suddenly, without saying a single word, the old man turned around and walked straight into the hotel.","Dexter blinked, his confusion deepening. \"...Huh?\" He scratched the back of his head, a habitual gesture when he was puzzled. \"What did I do?\""]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31 | Gifting The Ladies The Technique","paragraphs":["Five minutes passed and just when Dexter was beginning to think he should simply leave and return to the girls, to check on their progress, the old man returned.","\"Here’s your gift.\"","It had a strange black cord attached to a circular pendant split into two colors. Black and white.","Dexter blinked, taking the necklace automatically. \"What is this?\"","The old man simply stared at him, and then shook his head and sighed.","\"Keep it safe.\"","Before Dexter could ask anything, the old man turned around and left without explanation.","Dexter stood there, still holding the necklace, completely confused.","A few seconds later, he looked upward, toward the balcony of the old man above.","Standing there, was a young woman.","She was staring directly at him, her gaze intense and unblinking. Long black hair flowed down her shoulders like ink with two beautiful violet eyes.","For a brief second, Dexter found himself stunned. She was incredibly attractive almost comparable to Mira, Lyra, and Selene.","The young woman merely stared at him silently, her expression unreadable.","Dexter lowered his gaze, suddenly uncomfortable with the intensity of her attention.","---","Whatever this necklace was— it was definitely not ordinary.","After staring at it for a moment longer, Dexter shrugged, forcing himself to relax. \"Well...\" he muttered to himself, a wry smile tugging at his lips. \"It’s probably something good.\"","Without thinking too much about it, he placed the necklace around his neck, then he tucked it beneath his shirt, hiding it from view. Satisfied, Dexter turned around and headed back toward his room.","---","As he walked he kept thinking how perfect the scripture would be to the girls.","Their meridians have been shattered which means they would be useless for life until it’s repaired.","But with this scripture, it removed the need for meridians entirely.","’I’m giving it to them.’","Without hesitation, Dexter entered the room. They had already finished eating, the empty dishes pushed to the side.","He glanced at all three of them. \"I need to talk to three of you.\"","A few moments later, all three sat in the living room, staring at him curiously.","\"Don’t tell me you want to announce your fourth wife.\"","Lyra’s eyes widened and Selene’s sandwich almost fell to the ground.","Dexter’s lips curled to a smile.","\"Even better.\"","\"Two wives?\" Mira frowned this time.","Dexter stood in front of them and chuckled.","\"Nop, I have a cultivation technique.\"","The girls blinked, their confusion deepening rather than resolving.","Dexter continued. \"I want to give it to all of you.\"","Silence.","Mira rolled her eyes, in disappointment.","\"Seriously?\"","\"No matter what cultivation technique you have... it can’t possibly compare to our family cultivation arts.\"","Dexter simply remained silent, allowing her to express her doubts without interruption.","Mira smiled smugly. \"Our families trained us using Tier Four cultivation techniques. Even after everything... those are still among the best techniques in this entire city. They’ve been refined over generations, perfected through centuries of careful study and practice.\"","She paused, her expression taking on a condescending quality. \"So unless you somehow found something better than that...\"","She suddenly stopped speaking.","Because Dexter was smiling.","Smiling.","’Did he actually...?,","Mira eyes narrowed.","She didn’t believe he found one better than Tier 4.","Even Selene was staring intently now.","Then— without warning— Dexter stepped forward.","And placed his hand gently on Mira’s forehead.","Mira flinched instinctively, her body stiffening. She felt like pushing her head away, but then, she lowered her head and submitted, wondering what the hell their husband was up to.","Inside his mind, Dexter immediately commander","\"System. Transfer Grand Cosmos Scripture.\"","[Ding Imparting Processing.","Unlike ordinary techniques— a Seventh-Tier Technique could not simply be taught verbally.","It needed direct transmission.l to be imparted.","That was why the old man had been so horrified earlier.","Techniques of this level were typically shared through controlled rituals and secretly.","Dexter learning the technique simply by observing... without direct imparting was monstrous. It meant he had done something nearly impossible, had achieved in hours what should have taken years or decades.","A faint light appeared around Dexter’s hand. Then— the information transferred directly into Mira’s consciousness.","Mira’s eyes immediately widened, then slowly closed, her eyelids fluttering as a torrent of information flooded her mind.","Seeing the process succeed— Dexter moved toward Lyra.","She quietly set aside the bag of chips, then obediently closed her eyes.","Dexter placed his palm against her forehead, feeling the warmth of her skin beneath his fingers.","’Transfer Grand Cosmos Scripture.’","The second transfer began. Countless streams of information entered her consciousness, her body going rigid for a moment before relaxing as she adapted to the influx.","Then finally, Selene.","Dexter approached carefully, aware that she was the most guarded of the three.","This time, Selene didn’t flinch when he touched her, didn’t pull away or tense up at his approach.","Which immediately caught Dexter’s attention. That was progress.","Without wasting time, he transferred the technique into her as well, and then— silence.","All three girls remained completely motionless, eyes shut, their bodies perfectly still except for the slow rise and fall of their breathing.","Forty minutes, passed","Finally, after nearly an hour, all three slowly opened their eyes one by one.","And the moment they did— Dexter immediately noticed something strange.","All three expressions had changed.","Instead, their expressions had become deadly serious.","All three stared directly at him, their eyes unblinking and their faces froze as they stared dumbfoundedly at him.","It was as though they were looking at something they could not comprehend.","As if staring at a monster.","Or worse— a demon.","Dexter blinked, suddenly uncomfortable under their combined gaze. \"...Why are you all looking at me like that?\"","None of them answered immediately.","Because right now, their minds were in absolute chaos.","The technique they had just received... was real, a genuine, complete, Seventh-Tier Cultivation Technique.","And that made absolutely no sense.","Tier Seven techniques... were practically myths. Stories told to young cultivators to inspire them, to give them something to aspire to, even if they never had any realistic hope of achieving such heights.","Across the entire city— the strongest known cultivation technique was only Tier Five. And it belonged to the most powerful family in the city, the Colwell Family, whose influence extended into every aspect of supernatural society.","Even then— the Colwell Family guarded that technique jealously. Only the family head was allowed to cultivate it.","Other members, no matter how loyal or talented, were restricted to Tier Four techniques at best.","The secret of the Tier Five technique was perhaps the most closely guarded piece of knowledge in the entire region.","Yet now— Dexter had casually handed them something two entire levels higher. Something far beyond anything their families possessed.","Their thoughts spiraled wildly, each trying to make sense of something that defied sense.","Who exactly is Dexter?","Where did he get this?","How is this possible?","For a long time now— they had suspected Dexter wasn’t ordinary. His sudden growth in strength, his strange abilities that seemed to appear from nowhere and other wierd things but they hadn’t care at all.","But now— all doubts disappeared.","Dexter was hiding insane. And their must be a massive problem organization behind him.","And suddenly, for the second time this week, all three girls began seeing him differently.","At that moment, the three girls came to the exact same conclusion.","Their husband... was far, far more terrifying than they had ever imagined."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32 | Storm Empress!","paragraphs":["The rest of the day felt... strange. Not because anything wild happened. But because nothing happened.","It was too quiet.","At first, Dexter didn’t mind. The girls finally had hope again.","He’d handed them a way to cultivate that danced right past their shattered meridians.","That was huge.","Of course they’d be excited.","But after several hours, he realized he had been ignored.","Completely ignored.","They’d eaten exactly once the whole day — early morning, when the food cart arrived and he’d made them that medicinal tea.","After that? Nothing. Lunch came and the plates sat untouched Cold food, closed doors, and three girls lost in their own glowing little worlds.","Dexter leaned against the bedroom doorway, arms crossed, watching them like a parent whose kids had discovered a new video game.","Mira was by the window in her wheelchair, eyes pressed shut. Tiny waves of mana rose and fell around her like a warm breeze. Inside the bedroom, Selene sat cross-legged on the bed, breathing slow and steady, each inhale and exhale perfectly in sync with the Grand Cosmos Scripture.","And Lyra? She’d claimed the living room sofa, glasses on, eyes closed, deep in her own cultivation trance.","Three spots. Three girls. Three absolute cultivation maniacs.","Dexter sighed loud enough to shake the walls. \"I’m starting to feel like a forgotten houseplant in this room.\"","No one even twitched.","He shook his head, a tiny smile tugging at his lips. \"Maybe I should’ve waited a few more days before teaching them.\"","But he wasn’t really upset. Honestly? This made him happy. The way they dove in so obsessively meant one thing: those dark thoughts of ending it all were gone. They’d found hope again. A belief that one day they’d stand at the top once more. And that was everything.","So, with nobody interested in food, Dexter sat down alone and pulled the entire dinner tray toward himself.","As he ate, he noticed something else his bloodline evolution had done to him.","His appetite had gone completely wild.","Since his body upgraded, he needed almost three times as much food. His stomach was like a bottomless pit.","He stabbed a hunk of steak and muttered, \"Great. First Lyra was the endless eater... now I’m turning into a clone of her.\" He chuckled at his own joke, then grabbed the remote and flipped on the TV.","The screen flicked through boring stuff, political chatter, monster attack updates, Hero Association announcements, ads for protein bars. Then suddenly, an emergency broadcast took over.","A female reporter’s urgent voice cut through.","The screen showed chaos. Big yellow letters at the bottom read: [LIVE BROADCAST — DETROIT COUNTRY DISASTER RESPONSE].","Dexter’s eyebrow went up.","The camera zoomed out. Far off in the ocean, a gigantic luxury yacht had snapped clean in two.","Both halves were sinking fast.","People screamed, jumping into the churning water, clinging to bits of wreckage while others were already slipping under.","The reporter’s voice shook. \"A disaster off the coast of Detroit Country! The Aurora Queen, a massive luxury vessel, has suffered a catastrophic structural collapse and split in half roughly twelve kilometers from shore. Over one hundred passengers are now stranded at sea—\"","Before she could finish, the camera jerked upward. A howling gust of wind ripped across the ocean. The clouds spun like a stirred pot.","And then she dropped from the sky.","Long silver-white hair streamed behind her like a banner. A tight battle suit gleamed under the sun. Her eyes were gold and cold as winter.","She hung in the air, not moving, yet the sheer power bleeding off her made the screen seem fragile.","The broadcaster’s voice exploded with excitement. \"She’s here! The pride of the younger generation! The rising symbol of global hero supremacy! Storm Empress!\"","Dexter’s eyes narrowed. He set his fork down.","She moved.","\"BOOM!\"","The air cracked like thunder. She shot forward so fast the camera could barely track her. In a blink, she reached the broken yacht.","Each half of that ship weighed several hundred tons, heavy as a small building. Without a pause, Storm Empress reached out both hands. One grabbed the front half, the other grabbed the rear half. And she lifted.","Dexter’s chewing stopped dead. His eyes stretched wide. She was carrying both halves. In each hand. Like they were grocery bags.","The giant chunks of metal rose into the sky as if they weighed nothing. Passengers still trapped onboard screamed in disbelief.","Calmly, she flew both sections to the beach and set them down, gentle as placing a sleeping baby.","Then she turned and shot back over the water, a blur of wind. The camera struggled to keep up. She plunged into the ocean and came back up clutching three people.","Then five. Then ten. Over and over. A living hurricane. In minutes, nearly eighty stranded passengers had been scooped up and set safely on dry sand.","The newscaster’s voice boomed like an announcer at a sports final. \"Another impossible feat by one of humanity’s greatest young protectors! Storm Empress proves again why she’s the strongest hero of her generation! At only twenty-four, she continues to rewrite what modern heroes can be! This — is the hope our generation looks up to!\"","Dexter stared at the screen, jaw tight. His chest felt heavy. What he’d just seen was terrifying.","She could actually fly! And that speed, it was insane.","Enough raw strength to lift hundreds of tons like it was nothing. Durability to rocket through the ocean without a scratch. She’d left the Superhero Realm in the dust and was most likely at the Ultra Realm.","A 24 year old Ultra realm hero was astonishing. She has most likely broken some sort of record.","He leaned back and sighed.","The gap between him and the world’s true monsters was still an ocean wide. He fixed his eyes on Storm Empress frozen on the screen. So that’s the level I need to reach someday... No. That’s the level I need to crush.","Right at that moment—","DING!","A familiar golden glow blinked in front of his face. The 10,000 Times Investment System.","Dexter straightened up, heart kicking. A second message appeared beneath it.","---","[10,000x Investment System Activated.]","[You imparted the Grand Cosmos Scripture to your wives.]","[Calculating multiplier...]","[Multiplier Achieved: 100x.]","[Reward Generation In Progress...]","---","[You have received...]"]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33 | Limitless Grand Cosmos Scripture","paragraphs":["As soon as the first golden screen faded, a new one popped right in front of Dexter.","---","[10,000x Investment System Activated.]","[Reward ready.]","[Congratulations, Host.]","[You have received a Ninth-Tier cultivation technique.]","[Primordial Universe Star Scripture.]","---","Dexter went completely still. Then his eyes flew open so wide they almost hurt.","Ninth-Tier.","The highest tier to ever exist and no one had set their hands on.","His face fished red with excitement.","The system showed more.","---","═══════════════════════════════════════","[Limitless Grand Cosmos Scripture]","Ninth-Tier Technique","═══════════════════════════════════════","Description:","The perfected form of the Grand Cosmos Scripture.","No longer limited to forging a miniature universe, this supreme cultivation technique transforms the practitioner’s body into a boundless cosmos capable of containing countless celestial bodies.","Within the body lie 3,600 dormant Star Nodes. Every awakened Star Node becomes an independent celestial core, possessing its own gravitational field and serving as an inexhaustible source of mana.","Meridians become completely obsolete.","Once awakened, each Star Node continuously draws in the surrounding mana on its own, requiring no manual circulation. As more Star Nodes awaken, the attraction force of the Inner Cosmos grows stronger, allowing the practitioner’s cultivation speed to increase exponentially.","Every completed Firmament causes all previously awakened Star Nodes to evolve, increasing their capacity, density, and quality of mana.","═══════════════════════════════════════","Current Star Nodes: 0/3,600","═══════════════════════════════════════","Effects:","• Completely abandons the meridian system.","• Every awakened Star Node automatically absorbs surrounding mana.","• Each Star Node is an independent world capable of storing immense quantities of mana.","• Every completed Firmament upgrades all existing Star Nodes to the next celestial tier.","• Mana reserves increase to levels far beyond ordinary cultivators.","• Cultivation speed grows exponentially as additional Star Nodes awaken.","• The destruction of individual Star Nodes does not collapse the Inner Cosmos.","• The body gradually evolves into a true Cosmic Physique.","═══════════════════════════════════════","Ultimate Effect:","When all 3,600 Star Nodes reach perfection, they resonate simultaneously, giving birth to a complete Infinite Cosmos.","The Inner Cosmos becomes self-sustaining, generating celestial energy without relying solely on the surrounding world.","The practitioner transcends mortality, breaking all worldly limits and ascending as a being whose body rivals the universe itself.","═══════════════════════════════════════","Dexter stared at the screen so long his eyes started to sting. His whole body trembled.","A Ninth-Tier technique... Did something like this really exist?","He seriously doubted anyone in the entire country had one. Probably no one on the whole planet. This was the kind of secret that would start wars. The kind that would erase cities off the map just to own it.","Three thousand six hundred star nodes.","That meant he could keep mana in 3,600 different spots inside his body. He could use them for attacks, defense, speed—everything.","Normal cultivators had only a tiny fraction of that.","If he filled every single node, his mana reserves would be... insane.","And his raw strength would grow so much it might smash right through the Superhuman Realm, tear into the Ultra Realm, and maybe even climb higher than that.","And there was the matter of gaining the Truw Cosmic Physique!","He clenched his fists. Excitement buzzed under his skin like a live wire. He wanted to start give the girls.","But then his thoughts drifted to the girls. Mira, Lyra, Selene.","They were already giving him weird looks because of the Seventh-Tier technique he’d shared earlier. If he suddenly handed them a Ninth-Tier one... no way they’d ever treat him normally again.","He shook his head.","’ Not yet ’.","The Grand Cosmos Scripture was already a treasure for them. This one... this one was his. For now.","---","Night finally arrived. Outside the hotel window, city lights glittered like scattered stars.","Dexter sat cross-legged on the floor and took a slow breath. He began moving through the first steps of the Primordial Universe Star Scripture. His muscles stretched and relaxed in a steady rhythm. The air around him stirred, and tiny bits of mana started drifting toward him.","About twenty minutes passed. Then, there was a small ’click’ deep inside.","He found it. The very first Primordial Star Node, still dark and asleep.","Grinning, Dexter focused everything he had. He matched his breathing with the gentle body movements and pulled mana inward. Slowly, the node started to glow. Power trickled into it like water filling a cup.","It worked.","Hours slipped by. He trained without stopping, lost in a quiet, bright world inside himself.","Until a knock thumped on the door.","Knock. Knock.","Dexter opened his eyes.","\"Room service.\"","Dinner.","Tonight was their last night at this hotel. The Hero Association had put them up here for free, and since everything was covered,","Dexter had gone all-out. He’d ordered extra portions. Partly because his appetite had turned monstrous lately, and partly because Lyra existed.","The cart rolled in, loaded with trays. Steak, rice, soup, chicken, seafood, desserts, a small army of drinks. Dexter looked at the mountain of food and nodded, satisfied. Perfect.","Then he turned to the three girls.","All three were still deep in their own cultivation. Mira sat quietly in her wheelchair. Selene stayed cross-legged on the bed. Lyra hadn’t moved from the sofa. None of them even twitched.","Dexter sighed. \"...Seriously? You’re ignoring this?\"","Silence.","He crossed his arms. \"You all need to eat. Real food. Not just mana.\"","Still nothing.","Frowning, Dexter walked over and started bothering them one by one. He gave Mira’s shoulder a little shake. He tapped Selene right on the forehead. Then he lightly kicked Lyra’s leg.","All three sets of eyes slowly opened and locked onto him. Three perfectly synchronized death stares.","Dexter raised both hands, innocent as a puppy. \"Food. It’s here.\"","The girls narrowed their eyes, but they knew he was right. Cultivating without rest could mess up your foundation and make your mind fuzzy. So even though they were annoyed, they stopped and came to eat.","The difference was instant. They ate fast. Really fast.","But then Dexter noticed something terrifying. Lyra was a whole other beast. In minutes, she finished one plate. Then another. Then a third. Three full meals disappeared into her mouth in less than ten minutes.","Dexter stared, mouth hanging open. \"How...?\"","He had watched her eat impossible amounts for ages, and yet she never gained even a tiny bit of weight. Not once.","Suspicious, his eyes unconsciously traveled downward. To her hips. Then lower. Then back up to her chest.","Realization hit. He nodded slowly. \"...Ah. I get it now. So that’s where it all goes.\"","At that exact moment, Lyra froze.","She must have felt his stare. Her cheeks turned bright red. She quickly stood up, fumbled with her glasses, and rushed toward the bedroom without a word.","Dexter blinked. \"...Did she just get embarrassed?\"","Mira rolled her eyes so hard it looked painful. Selene just stared at him with the blankest expression in history.","He coughed awkwardly and went back to his food, ears burning.","After dinner, the three girls returned to cultivation, leaving Dexter alone in the quiet.","He shook his head with a helpless smile.","Tomorrow would be their last day at the hotel. Tomorrow they would probably go home. And more importantly, tomorrow he planned to visit the Hunter Association and finally get his official Hunter License."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34 | Mira’s Mana Arms Manifesting","paragraphs":["Boom! Boom! Boom!","Dexter’s eyes snapped open.","Not because of a sound, it was more like a ripple and then, a muffled, deep thump. Then another. Then a third.","They weren’t loud. Ordinary ears might have missed them entirely.","But Dexter’s senses weren’t ordinary. His Passive Talent kept a low, constant hum of awareness around him—even more so while he slept or cultivated.","It was an invisible net, ready to catch anything unusual. And right now, that net was vibrating.","Something had happened.","He stood up from the sofa in one quick motion, heart already thudding. The explosions had come from the girls bedroom.","He crossed the room in a few strides and shoved the door open.","And stopped.","All three girls were wide awake on the bed. Mana distorting the air around them like sun on heating up the asphalt. The explosions weren’t attacks—they were breakthroughs.","Lyra had jumped from Fourth Stage Awakening Realm to Fifth. Mira, same leap, and Selene, who’d been at Third Stage, now radiated the steady pulse of the Fourth.","Dexter just stared. Less than a day. He’d handed them the Grand Cosmos Scripture less than twenty-four hours ago, and they’d already found their Star Nodes, swallowed mana, and pushed through. The sheer talent was staggering.","Three pairs of eyes slowly opened and found him. For a heartbeat, Dexter forgot to breathe.","They were smiling. Really smiling.","Small, soft, unguarded smile with no hint of bitterness, nor coldness.","Just quiet happiness. It was the first genuine smile he’d seen from any of them, ever.","And in that moment, stripped of their usual hard expressions, they looked... beautiful. Not just pretty, they looked truly beautiful.","Then they noticed his stunned expression. They blushed as they closed their eyes and sank back into cultivation as if nothing had happened.","Mira glared at him and also continued cultivating.","Dexter stood there for a second longer. Then a quiet smile tugged at his own lips. They’re changing. Little by little.","He turned, walked back to the living room, and settled onto the sofa.","He wasn’t exactly falling behind.","He’d already located his first Primordial Star Node, right at his forehead. It sat there like a tiny gray ember, dormant.","Before filling it, he had to crack a mental barrier around it. Now, with the bedroom quiet again, he intended to do exactly that.","He folded his legs, closed his eyes, and began to move.","The Primordial Universe Star Scripture wasn’t just mental—it required slow, flowing body movements that guided mana in faster.","Muscles stretched, breath steadied, and the air stirred around him. Mana trickled toward his forehead. The gray node began to glow, slowly filling like a glass held under a faucet.","An hour drifted by.","\"BOOM!\"","A silent explosion detonated inside his skull. His body jerked as the gray node erupted into bright silver light, fully awake and flooded with mana.","Power flooded his limbs, muscles tightening, bones humming, blood racing. The barrier between stages shattered.","Eighth Stage Awakening Realm.","Dexter opened his eyes, clenched his fist, and grinned. One more step forward.","---","A glance at the time: 5:00 a.m. They’d be leaving the hotel today.","The girls were still in their cultivation cocoons, so Dexter took care of packing. He folded Mira’s clothes neatly, tucked in Selene’s things, then Lyra’s.","Luggage lined up by the door. He spent another hour quietly stabilizing his new realm, then stood and entered the bedroom.","He gave a light clap. \"Alright, time to wash up. We’re heading out soon.\"","They nodded and shuffled off. After Selene and Lyra were done, it was Mira’s turn.","Dexter helped her as usual—carefully washing her hair, drying her skin, then sorting through her clothes. He pulled out a soft summer dress dotted with sunflowers and held it up with a smile.","\"This one.\"","Mira’s frown was immediate. \"No.\"","He blinked. \"No?\"","She gestured with her head to another outfit lying nearby, much shorter, tighter, and cut low enough to make his eyebrows climb.","\"That one.\"","Dexter saw it and was about to take it when his eyewes flashed.","He smirked and shook his head. \"Nope. That’s way too short, and half your chest would be saying exposedto the world.\"","Mira grinned. \"That’s exactly why I want it.\"","He lifted the sunflower dress higher. \"No chance.\"","She glared at him angrily making her look really cute.","\"I’m paralyzed. You have to listen to me.\"","Dexter gaze narrowed with a dangerous smile on his face.","\"Oh? So you’re helpless now? Funny... didn’t you say, when we first met, you said I could do anything I wanted with you body right?\"","Mira froze as she remembered the night of their wedding.","She gritted her teeth. \"I was only joking.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"I took it seriously. So, I’m putting this on you whether you like it or not.\"","Her cheeks flared red. \"You—!\"","But before he could even start, the air around them distorted as mana trembled through the void.","\"I said I don’t want! \"","Behind Mira, two mana circles appeared around her and then with a muffled bang, the rings expanded, undurling like wings and formed two spectral arms made entirely out of mana, floating behind Mira just above her shoulders, fingers flexing slightly as if alive.","The room fell absolutely silent.","Dexter stared at the arms, then at Mira’s shocked face. He blinked slowly, the sunflower dress still dangling from his grip.","\"...Well. That’s new.\""]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35 | Is This Love?","paragraphs":["Dexter looked at the two glowing orange arms floating behind Mira, and while he showed mild surprise on his face, inside he wasn’t completely shocked.","After all, he was the one who had secretly slipped her the D-Rank Mana Arm Talent Card.","Still, he hadn’t expected it to show up this fast.","Before he could say anything, one of the spectral arms moved on its own.","\"Slap!\"","It smacked the sunflower dress right out of his hand.","Dexter blinked at the empty air where the dress had been, then at the floating arm.","\"...Well. That’s new.\"","Mira looked just as stunned.","The two orange arms hovered behind her shoulders, right where her real arms would be. She slowly turned her head to look at them, and the mana arms moved with the thought, as if they’d always been part of her.","One of them floated forward and stopped right in front of her face. She stared, wide-eyed.","The translucent fingers flexed. It was pure, glowing mana shaped like an arm—slightly bulkier than a human one, but definitely hers.","Her breathing quickened. Then her eyes flashed and she looked at Dexter, shock written all over her face.","Dexter folded his arms and spoke quietly. \"...Dual talent awakening?\"","Mira frowned, but then her eyes lit up with understanding. \"...Yeah. That’s probably it.\"","But even saying the words didn’t erase the wonder from her face.","Double awakeners were impossibly rare, something like a 0.001 percent chance.","Across the whole city, there wasn’t a single known one. Yet here she was, a second ability blooming from within her. Mana Spectral Arms.","Slowly, a mischievous smirk spread across Mira’s lips.","Dexter felt a warning prickle. Without warning, one spectral arm shot toward the pile of clothes and grabbed the tiny, revealing dress Mira had wanted earlier.","Dexter narrowed his eyes. \"...You’re still trying that?\"","Mira’s smirk only grew.","She tried to command the arms to dress herself. But there was one problem, she had zero control.","They grabbed the dress, pulled hard, and—","\"RRRIP! \"","The whole thing tore right down the middle.","Silence.","Mira froze. The spectral arms froze. She looked down at the ruined fabric, then slowly up at Dexter.","Dexter stared at her for two full seconds.","Then he burst out laughing.","\"Hahaha—! See? Now you have no choice. You’re wearing this one.\" He held up the sunflower dress, triumphantly","Mira glared daggers at him, sitting there in just her bra and underwear, her cheeks flushed","She clicked her tongue. \"Fine. Do whatever you want.\" The spectral arms crossed in front of her chest, exactly like a person folding their arms in anger.","Dexter couldn’t help smiling; it was strangely adorable. \"Good. We’ve reached an agreement.\"","The arms immediately uncrossed and stretched outward, waiting.","But there was still a problem. Her real arms still didn’t work, which meant Dexter had to help her anyway.","He gently picked up the sunflower dress and helped her slip it on, adjusting the straps carefully. As he did, a thought popped into his head.","He looked at the floating mana arms. \"Since you awakened this... could you make more arms? And if you learn to control them, maybe you could integrate one into your real arm, force the muscles to move. Do the same with your legs, and maybe... you could walk again.\"","For a moment, Mira’s eyes blazed with a dangerous amount of hope. But then her expression turned soft and a little bitter. She shook her head.","\"My control is terrible. I just tried to put on clothes and tore them apart. If I shoved one of those into my real arm now, I’d probably destroy it.\"","Dexter nodded slowly. \"...Yeah, that makes sense.\" Too risky. She needed practice first. He let the subject drop.","A few minutes later, they came out of the bathroom and into the living room.","Selene sat on one sofa, still cultivating.","Lyra was cross-legged nearby, also lost in her own world of mana.","Even though they’d be leaving soon, neither had stopped. Dexter wasn’t surprised. For the first time in years, they could cultivate without agony. Of course they were obsessed.","He suddenly heard Mira grunt in pain.","’The chronic pain is still affecting her? \"","Even after using the type 2 relic ir still didn’t help.","Then Dexter remembered something.","The ring. That artifact the system had given him, the one that could take give his pain to someone else... He could actually use it to take someone else’s pain onto himself.","Without thinking too much, he slipped it onto his finger and quietly walked over to Mira.","Before she could ask, he reached out and touched her shoulder. Then he activated the ring.","For a split second, nothing. Then—","\"Bang!\"","The pain swallowed him whole.","It was like being hit by a truck made of broken glass and fire.","Years of nerve damage, years of constant aching, all the suffering Mira had endured—every single ounce of it poured into Dexter in an instant.","’Fuck me! ’","His body spasmed violently.","His knees buckled and he crashed to the floor, muscles convulsing, nerves screaming as if they were being torn apart from the inside. Cold sweat drenched him. He shook uncontrollably.","The sudden noise made everyone jump. Selene’s eyes flew open. Lyra spun around. Mira stared in shock. All three focused on Dexter, crumpled on the ground.","It took several agonizing seconds for him to force a breath. Gritting his teeth, he pushed himself up, still trembling hard. The pain hadn’t faded; it chewed violently at his nerves, a living fire inside his body.","It was so much worse than he’d expected.","Lyra grabbed her phone, her glasses speaker spoke in that mechanical voice: \"What happened?\" Selene stopped cultivating, brows tight. \"Dexter... what’s wrong? Are you hurt?\"","He forced himself upright, every inch of him screaming, even breathing hurting. Yet somehow, he managed a strained smile. \"...I’m fine. Just... got a little shock.\" Neither Selene nor Lyra looked convinced.","But Mira wasn’t listening.","She was frozen, staring at him. Because for the first time in years, the pain was gone completely. The relentless agony she’d lived with every second of every day had simply vanished.","Then she saw Dexter’s reaction and then eyes lowered to the ring on his finger.","Then she realized what Had happened, he had d taken her pain. Transferred it onto himself, for her. Without a word, without a second thought.","Mira slowly lifted her head and looked deep into Dexter’s eyes.","Something deep inside her shifted. The coldness in her eyes melted into something warm, soft, and entirely new.","Not for family, not for friends, not even for the fiancé She had once had before the accident.","The way she looked at Dexter now was different, like she was seeing him for the very first time.","He kept surprising her again and again and again, through effort and pain and also through his actions without asking for nothing in return.","Was there truly anyone so selfless?","Meanwhile, Dexter was still fighting through the fire in his body. He cleared his throat, smile still shaky. \"...I’m really okay. You guys... excuse me for a second.\"","He Without waiting for an answer, he turned and walked toward the bathroom. Each step was a little unsteady, his body still trembling from the overwhelming pain.","Behind him, Mira just kept staring, unable to look away. Something inside her she thought she’d never have suddenly started to bloom.","’is this what they call, Love?’"]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36 | Rewards! Rewards! Rewards!","paragraphs":["The girls clearly didn’t believe him.","Selene’s eyes narrowed with worry. Lyra’s fingers hovered over her phone, ready to type another question. Mira just watched him, her expression unreadable but heavy with something new.","But before any of them could speak—","Dexter turned around.","\"I’ll... be back in a minute.\"","He staggered toward the bedroom and quietly closed the door behind him.","Only then, alone, did he finally let out a groan.","\"Urgh...\"","The pain was unlike anything he had ever experienced.","He couldn’t believe someone had endured this for years.","And then, a familiar mechanical voice echoed inside his mind.","[Ding!]","---","Inside the bathroom, Dexter gripped the edge of the sink with both hands.","His knuckles turned white.","Every nerve in his body screamed in agony. It felt like thousands of red-hot needles were being driven through his muscles, his bones, his internal organs—all at the same time.","Cold sweat streamed down his face. His breathing turned ragged.","\"...So this... this is what she’s been enduring...\"","He had always known Mira lived in constant pain. He’d seen her expression tighten whenever she tried to move. He’d watched her force smiles despite the suffering.","But knowing and experiencing were two entirely different things.","Now that he was carrying the pain himself, Dexter finally understood.","No wonder she had wanted to die. No wonder she had lost all hope.","He’d once heard someone say that women possessed an unbelievable tolerance for pain. Back then, he hadn’t paid much attention.","Now, he believed it wholeheartedly.","\"How... did she endure this for years...?\"","He let out a long breath and forced himself to relax, bit by bit. His body slowly adapted. The pain never disappeared—but it became... bearable.","Just then—","[Ding!]","A familiar system notification appeared before him.","---","[Overall Affection Threshold Reached 100%]","[New System Function Unlocked: Cultivation Sharing]","---","Dexter blinked. \"Cultivation... Sharing?\"","The system continued immediately.","---","[From now on, whenever an investor breaks through, the host will automatically receive cultivation according to that investor’s affection level.]","Current Investors:","Mira — 50%","Lyra — 10%","Selene — 20%","Jasmine — 70%","Rachael — 30%","[0% → Stranger → 10% → Acquaintance → 20% → Familiar → 30% → Friendly → 40% → Friend → 50% → Trusted Friend → 60% → Best Companion → 70% → Lover → 80% → Romantic Partner → 90% → False Soulmates → 100% → True Soulmates ]","---","The very next instant—","A tremendous amount of mana flooded into Dexter’s body.","His eyes widened.","\"So this is... Mira’s breakthrough!\"","The cultivation she had gained from reaching the Fifth Stage surged into him. Fifty percent of it merged directly into his own.","Immediately afterward, another wave arrived. Lyra’s. Then another. Selene’s.","The three streams of cultivation merged together like rivers flowing into the sea.","\"Boom!\"","His aura erupted.","The Eighth Stage, which he had only recently broken through, stabilized in an instant.","Then his cultivation kept climbing.","Early Eighth Stage... Middle Eighth Stage... Late Eighth Stage... Peak Eighth Stage...","The mana still hadn’t stopped.","Another explosion echoed inside his body.","\"Boom\"","Dexter’s eyes flew open. \"I broke through again?\"","His aura expanded once more. He had stepped into the Early Ninth Stage of the Awakening Realm.","Dexter stared blankly at the notification. He had advanced two entire stages in a single morning.","\"If this continues... it won’t be long before I enter the Superhuman Realm.\"","His heartbeat quickened. The stronger the girls became, the stronger he would become as well. No wonder the system called them his Investors.","---","Just then, another notification appeared.","Knowing the multiplier reward would soon activate, Dexter rushed out of the bathroom and went to the girls.","They were still staring at the door in confusion. Of course they had felt the blast from his breakthrough and were stunned.","They were even more stunned when Dexter smiled at them, stepped forward, and patted Lyra’s shoulder. Then he gently held Selene’s palm with his hand.","She didn’t flinch—just as he had expected.","\"Pain absorb.\"","Dexter’s face turned pale. Sweat dripped down his body. Pain from broken meridians flooded him. The ringing sensation from Lyra’s ears. The burning feeling she had been enduring in her throat. The pricking sensation Selene had been feeling in her eyes, and the icy flames burning through her body constantly.","Dexter wanted to scream. He wanted to roar and deactivate the ring immediately—but the system rewards hadn’t come yet.","\"What?\" Lyra’s glasses spoke for her, the mechanical voice tight with shock. \"What did you do?\"","The two girls were stunned. The pain that had been their neighbor for more than three years had simply vanished at Dexter’s touch.","It didn’t take long for them to figure it out, with their intelligence.","\"Excu—\" Dexter couldn’t form any words. He rushed back into the bathroom.","Pain! Intense pain colliding with every single one of his senses. His eyes, his ears, his throat, his meridians, his skin, his muscles, his brain. It was inconceivable.","[Ding!]","---","[10,000× Investment System Activated]","Investment Target: Mira, Selene, Lyra","Investment: You sincerely bore your three wives’ pains","Multiplier: 100×","Calculating Returns...","[Rewards Obtained:]","• D-Rank Talent Card — Pain Perception","A passive talent that allows the host to sense the physical and emotional pain of bonded targets from a great distance. Danger, injuries, illness, and suffering can all be detected instantly.","• Type-6 Relic — Ring of Shared Burdens","An upgraded version of the Pain Transfer Ring. Effects: No distance limitation. Can transfer any form of physical pain, chronic pain, poison agony, soul pain, and curse backlash. Can be activated or cancelled at will. The transferred pain is borne entirely by the wearer.","• Sixth-Tier Legendary Body Cultivation Technique — Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture","A legendary body-refining art that converts pain into strength. The more suffering the practitioner endures, the stronger the body becomes. Pain is transformed into vitality, increasing regeneration, durability, mental resistance, and poison resistance.","• Grade-4 Divine Medicine — Phoenix Heart Elixir ×3","A precious healing medicine capable of repairing damaged organs, restoring vitality, and greatly reducing permanent injuries.","• Mana Affinity Increased","A-Rank → S-Rank","Mana absorption speed increased dramatically.","---","Dexter’s breathing became uneven. \"So many rewards...\"","The Ring of Shared Burdens immediately caught his attention. \"No distance limit...\" That meant even if Mira, Selene, or Lyra were thousands of kilometers away, he could still take their pain upon himself.","His gaze softened. \"If Selene’s illness acts up again... I won’t have to just watch her suffer anymore.\"","Then his attention shifted to the Phoenix Heart Elixirs. Although they couldn’t completely heal shattered meridians like a Divine Pill, they were still priceless treasures. \"They’ll be useful later.\"","Finally, his eyes settled on the Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture. A slow smile spread across his face. \"This technique... it was practically made for me.\"","He was already cultivating the Demon Tempering Body Technique, a cultivation art that constantly pushed his body to its limits.","Now, with the Eternal Endurance Scripture, every bit of pain he experienced would become nourishment for his body instead of just suffering.","The stronger the pain, the stronger he would become. And with the girls always in pain... wouldn’t he become a god in no time?","Dexter closed the system window.","He tried to cultivate, tried to pull his mind away from the pain. He washed his face with cold water and took a deep breath. His expression gradually returned to normal.","Only then did he leave the bathroom.","Outside, three pairs of eyes immediately turned toward him.","Shock was written across their faces, and now a hint of awe and respect could be seen there, too."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37 | Heading Back & Jealousy","paragraphs":["Dexter had already ordered an Blitx Ride before they finished packing.","He pulled out his phone while the girls were in the sitting room, either cultivating, still folding their clothes or stuffing toiletry bags.","The app showed a four-minute wait. Perfect timing. He confirmed the pickup and waited on the sofa.","He neatly folded the last of Mira things when his mind went to his rewards once more.","He eagerly checked his rewards and smiled.","D-Rank Talent Card — Pain Perception","Type-6 Relic — Ring of Shared Burdens","Sixth-Tier Legendary Body Cultivation Technique — Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture","Grade-4 Divine Medicine — Phoenix Heart Elixir ×3","• Mana Affinity Increased","A-Rank → S-Rank","Mana absorption speed increased dramatically.","He smiled and stretched out his hands as the 6th-tier ring of shared burden appeared before him.","He removed the tier 2 ring, relief washed over him while the girls froze as their pain returned.","They immediately turned towards the bedroom where Dexter had vanished into.","But it didn’t take long before the pain vanished once more and they equally sighed in relief but their gaze toward the bedroom didn’t stop.","What does it mean to have someone literally take your pain away and burden themselves with it?","He could have held it over them, used the rings ability to take advantage of them and even threat them with it.","But not Dexter, he didn’t say anything and simply touched them, taking their pain away without another word and then pretended like nothing happened.","\"Stupid.\"","Mira couldn’t help but mutter and the rest nodded their heads in agreement. Even Lyra who couldn’t hear nodded as she read it through the Type 2 AI Glasses and knew it was Mira talking.","By the time everyone was ready to leave, the vehicle had already arrived outside the hotel.","A dark sedan idled at the curb, its hazard lights blinking rhythmically.","Dexter received a notification on his phone, looked down the window and spoke.","\"Alright, it’s time to leave.\"","He pushed Mira’s wheelchair out of the room first. The wheels rolled smoothly across the carpeted hallway.","Mira sat with her hands folded in her lap, her posture straight despite the fatigue still clinging to her body.","Her amber hair had been brushed neatly over her shoulders, and her pale skin stood out sharply against the fabric of her clothes.","Lyra and Selene followed behind with the luggage. Lyra dragged two suitcases, one in each hand, her small frame somehow managing the weight without complaint.","Her smart glasses sat perfectly on her nose, the thin frames catching the fluorescent light overhead.","Selene carried a single bag slung over her shoulder. She moved carefully, one hand lightly trailing along the wall, counting steps out of habit even though Lyra walked right beside her.","Together, they entered the elevator and rode down to the lobby.","Dexter’s face was furrowed in deep pain but he was excited as the pain was strengthening his body rapidly due to the Eternal Endurance Scripture.","The soft hum of the elevator filled the small space.","Mira glanced up at Dexter. He was staring at the metal doors with a calm expression, his hands resting on the handles of her wheelchair.","She studied the side of his face for a moment before looking away. Lyra also did the same thing but hers was more subtle.","\"Ding!\"","A soft chime announced their arrival.","The doors slid open.","After returning the room key and completing the checkout process at the front desk, the four of them stepped out of the hotel through the rotating glass doors.","The morning air was cool and fresh. Sunlight poured across the wide entrance, casting long shadows behind them.","Almost immediately, Dexter felt countless gazes but he was half excited and half deep in misery to care.","\"Hm... \"","Mira’s voice took his attention as he looked down at her.","\"What?\"","Mira noticed his expression and chuckled softly from below.","\"Do you realize how many strange looks you’re getting?\"","Dexter blinked before instinctively looking around.","She was right.","People passing by couldn’t help but stare.","He was coming out of a hotel with three extremely beautiful women by his side, one even crippled but he actually got them into the hotel.","A businessman in a gray suit slowed his pace, his coffee frozen halfway to his mouth.","Two women standing near a bus stop saw him and were stunned as they turned to whisper to each other.","An elderly couple sitting on a bench openly watched the group with wide eyes.","Some men looked at him with open admiration.","One young man in a hoodie even secretly gave him a thumbs-up before flashing him a look that said, ’Brother, teach me your ways.’","His friend elbowed him hard in the ribs, but the grin never left his face.","Others looked at him with disbelief.","A security guard standing near the hotel entrance raised an eyebrow so high it nearly disappeared into his hairline.","Some women glanced at him curiously before shifting their attention to the three beautiful women accompanying him.","Their expressions ranged from jealousy to pure confusion.","The combination was certainly eye-catching.","One breathtaking beauty sat in a wheelchair. Her delicate features and pale complexion made her look like a porcelain doll.","Another possessed an elegant, scholarly aura.","Her smart glasses gave her an air of quiet intelligence, and her smooth dark purple hair fell neatly past her shoulders. She walked with a calm grace that drew attention without trying.","The last had an icy temperament that kept everyone at arm’s length. Her silver-white hair caught the sunlight like spun moonlight, and her unfocused eyes gave her an ethereal quality that made people instinctively step aside.","And somehow...","All three were accompanying the same man.","An ordinary-looking man.","Nothing about his appearance was remotely extraordinary. Average height. Average build. Plain features and a face you’d forget five minutes after seeing it.","Yet here he was.","Walking out of a luxury hotel.","With three stunning women.","Mira snorted, trying to suppress a laugh that was growing harder to contain.","\"You must be feeling pretty proud right now.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","\"Proud?\"","\"Your male ego must be soaring.\"","She gestured her chin toward the people staring at him.","\"Walking out of a luxury hotel with three gorgeous women.\"","\"Every man here is probably dying of jealousy right now.\"","Dexter immediately sensed a trap.","He had fallen for her teasing enough times to know better.","Mira had a talent for baiting him into saying something she could twist later. Her innocent smile was always the first warning sign.","So this time...","His lips curled to a smirk and he harrumped.","\"Hmph. You want to cause trouble again.\"","The he ignored he further teasing.","Seeing him refuse to respond, Mira clicked her tongue.","\"Hmph. No fun.\"","Dexter smiled faintly but said nothing.","Lyra glanced between them with a small smile of her own. The AI translated everything so she heard every word.","Selene, unable to see the exchange, listened and tilted her head, slightly amused.","Their Vehicle soon pulled up in front of the hotel.","\"You’re Dexter?\"","Dexter responded positively and then carried Mira into the back seat carefully, making sure her legs were positioned comfortably before reaching for the seatbelt. He buckled it for her without being asked.","Then he folded her wheelchair and placed it in the trunk.","Lyra and Selene got in afterward. Lyra helped guide Selene into the seat beside her before settling in herself.","The driver, a middle-aged man with a neatly trimmed beard, glanced at them through the rearview mirror.","’This perverted guy. He actually has three women.’","Finally, his gaze landed on Dexter.","The driver looked as though he wanted to ask a question.","In the end, he wisely chose to remain silent.","The engine hummed to life, and the vehicle smoothly pulled away from the hotel."]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38 | Assassin!","paragraphs":["Dexter sat in the front passenger seat while the SUV rolled through the bustling streets of the City.","Morning sunlight reflected off towering glass buildings as streams of vehicles flowed across the highways. Advertisements flickered on massive billboards. Some advertised hero gear. Others promoted dungeon raiding gear or cultivation supplements. One massive billboard displayed the face of a famous hero winking at the camera above the words \"Protect Tomorrow, Today.\"","Below the billboards, the city moved with its usual energy. Pedestrians crowded the sidewalks. Food vendors called out from street corners. Children laughed as they walked to school in small groups.","Occasionally, awakened heroes streaked across the distant skyline, leaving faint trails of light behind them as they headed toward missions only they knew about. Some flew. Some ran across rooftops. Others rode specialized vehicles that hummed with mana.","In the vehicle behind Dexter, Selene sat in the middle of the back seat with her eyes closed. Her silver-white hair rested neatly over her shoulders. Her hands lay calmly in her lap. She was listening to the familiar rhythm of the city.","Beside the window, Mira rested comfortably in the chair. Her seatbelt was fastened securely across her chest.","She silently admired the city outside, watching buildings and people pass by through the glass. The sunlight caught her pale skin and made her look almost delicate.","On the opposite side, Lyra leaned against the door, watching everything through her AI glasses. The smart lenses continuously translated the sounds around her into text.","[Car horn. Left side. Thirty meters.]","[Engine. Front. Close.]","[Wind. Moderate.]","She found it fascinating how much information she could gather just from reading those simple labels.","Dexter had his eyes closed as well.","He wasn’t sleeping. Far from it.","Instead, he was silently circulating the Primordial Universe Star Scripture, using its profound breathing method to suppress the unbearable pain that still lingered throughout his body. Every breath followed a specific pattern. Inhale for four counts. Hold for seven. Exhale for eight. Each cycle pushed mana through his meridians in tiny, controlled bursts.","Every nerve felt as though it were being stabbed by countless needles.","The pain he had absorbed from Mira, Selene, and Lyra hadn’t disappeared. Like a fire that refused to go out no matter how much water he poured on it.","His body had merely begun adapting to it.","The human body was remarkably adaptable. Given enough time, it could grow accustomed to almost any level of suffering. But adaptation wasn’t the same as healing. The pain was still there.","Fortunately, the cultivation technique continuously soothed his nerves, preventing the agony from affecting his expression. The mana flowed through his pathways like cool water over a burn. It didn’t heal the damage, but it kept the pain manageable.","---","The SUV continued moving smoothly along the elevated highway. The driver hummed quietly to himself, keeping a steady speed in the middle lane.","Then —","Buzz...","A faint sound brushed past Dexter’s enhanced hearing.","It was so soft that it resembled a mosquito flying beside his ear. Even awakeners with enhanced hearing might have dismissed it as background noise.","But Dexter didn’t.","His eyes snapped open.","\"...?\"","Slowly, he turned toward the driver.","His pupils contracted.","A perfectly round hole had appeared on the side of the driver’s head.","For a brief second...","Dexter couldn’t comprehend what he was seeing. One moment the driver was fine, humming his little tune. The next moment, there was a hole in his head.","Then blood slowly trickled down the driver’s temple before dripping onto his collar.","The driver’s lifeless eyes rolled upward, showing only white. His mouth fell open slightly. His hands went limp on the steering wheel.","His head slumped forward onto the horn.","\"HOOOOONK —\"","The horn blared continuously.","The steering wheel jerked violently to the right as the driver’s full weight fell against it.","The SUV immediately veered across the highway, cutting across two lanes in an instant.","Only then did realization strike Dexter like a bolt of lightning.","The driver was dead.","A sniper.","Someone had just killed the driver with a single shot.","Without hesitating, Dexter lunged forward.","His left hand seized the steering wheel while his right shoved the driver’s corpse aside. The body slumped against the window with a sickening thud. Dexter pulled the wheel hard to the left, barely preventing the vehicle from crashing into the guardrail.","\"Get down!\" he roared.","\"Assassin!\"","The shout exploded through the car like a bomb.","Selene reacted instantly.","Despite being blind, she trusted Dexter without question.","She immediately pulled Mira downward while shielding her with her own body.","Lyra didn’t hesitate either.","The warning flashed across her AI glasses almost instantly. The text appeared in bold red letters.","[ASSASSIN — GET DOWN]","She ducked beneath the window, pressing herself against the seat to avoid the line of fire.","Dexter lowered his own body while struggling to keep control of the speeding vehicle. The SUV was still moving forward at highway speed with no driver. The engine revved loudly as the car drifted between lanes.","Horns blared across the highway as terrified drivers tried to avoid the out-of-control vehicle.","Cars scattered in every direction. One minivan swerved so hard it nearly rolled over. A delivery truck slammed its brakes, sending crates tumbling inside its cargo hold.","Dexter gritted his teeth.","Where...?","Where is the sniper...?","His hearing expanded to its absolute limit.","The world around him suddenly became incredibly clear. Every sound within hundreds of meters flowed into his mind simultaneously. It was overwhelming.","Then —","Click.","A tiny metallic sound.","Barely audible. Like a pen being clicked in a quiet room.","But to Dexter...","It sounded like thunder.","Someone was chambering another sniper round.","His eyes narrowed.","Above.","Overhead bridge.","The sound had come from the bridge they were approaching. The concrete overpass that stretched across the highway approximately two hundred meters ahead.","Without even looking, Dexter instantly slammed his head downward.","A split second later —","\"BANG!\"","The bullet pierced straight through the windshield. The glass didn’t shatter immediately. The round punched a clean hole through it, sending a spiderweb of cracks radiating outward from the impact point.","The bullet flew exactly through the space where his head had been less than a heartbeat earlier. The round continued through the cabin and tore out through the rear window in a shower of shattered glass.","Glass fragments rained down onto the back seat.","The girls froze.","Had Dexter reacted even a fraction of a second slower..."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39 | A Level 3 Super human Assassin","paragraphs":["Dexter tightened his grip on the steering wheel.","His enhanced hearing remained stretched to its absolute limit. Every sound within several hundred meters flowed into his mind like a river of information.","The assassin on the bridge had already chambered another round.","He was waiting...","Waiting for the perfect angle.","The bridge was getting closer. In a few seconds, the SUV would pass directly beneath it. The sniper would have a clear, unobstructed shot straight down into the vehicle.","Dexter glanced at the rearview mirror.","The girls were still crouched beneath the windows.","\"Stay down!\" he shouted.","\"Don’t raise your heads no matter what happens!\"","The three silently obeyed.","Another faint metallic click echoed above.","The sniper had locked onto them again.","Dexter immediately made his decision.","If I keep driving, he’ll keep shooting...","He has the high ground. He has the angle.","\"Then I’ll take away his line of sight.\"","His right hand yanked the handbrake with all his strength.","SCREECH — !","The tires screamed against the asphalt.","The SUV spun nearly 180 degrees across the highway.","Several nearby vehicles slammed on their brakes as tires screeched. Fenders crumpled.","One sedan clipped the rear of the SUV, sending sparks flying as traffic descended into complete chaos.","The vehicle now sat sideways in the middle of the highway.","The sniper could no longer see them.","Dexter finally released a slow breath.","But the relief lasted less than a second.","Thud.","Thud.","Two heavy impacts echoed from the sides of the vehicle.","Dexter’s pupils shrank.","Someone had landed on both sides of the car simultaneously.","The sniper wasn’t acting alone.","This wasn’t just an assassination.","It was an ambush.","The next instant —","A black-clothed figure leapt from the bridge above.","BOOM!","He landed squarely on the hood of the SUV.","The entire vehicle shook violently. The hood caved in like a piece of paper being crushed by a fist. Deep dents spread outward from the point of impact.","The windshield shattered completely. Thousands of glass fragments flew inward like transparent rain.","The engine compartment collapsed with a sickening crunch.","Even the front tires burst instantly.","Smoke rose from the ruined vehicle. Thin gray wisps that curled upward into the morning sky.","The man’s black combat suit fluttered in the wind. It was tight against his body, revealing lean muscles and a frame built for speed and power. A mask concealed his face. Only his cold eyes remained visible. They were cold dark and deadly.","He slowly lifted his head.","Through the shattered windshield...","His gaze met Dexter’s.","A terrifying pressure filled the air.","Dexter immediately sensed it.","Superhuman Realm...","At least Level Three.","His expression became solemn.","This was no ordinary assassin.","Before he could react further —","Bang!","The rear door on Mira’s side was suddenly ripped open. The door flew across the highway and tumbled end over end before crashing into the guardrail.","A second masked assassin reached inside, his gloved hand grabbing toward the nearest girl. His fingers closed around Selene’s arm.","Dexter didn’t even turn around.","His wrist flicked.","A silver hairpin appeared between his fingers and shot through the air almost silently. It moved so fast it was barely visible.","Pfft!","The needle pierced straight through the assassin’s temple.","The masked man froze. His grip on Selene’s arm loosened. His eyes went blank.","His body collapsed lifelessly onto the highway. He hit the ground with a dull thud and didn’t move again.","Before the corpse even touched the ground —","The opposite rear door was yanked open.","A third assassin lunged toward Lyra. This one was faster. More careful. He moved low, keeping his body below the window line as he reached inside.","Dexter’s fingers moved again.","Another needle flew.","This particular assassin reacted much faster this time. He tilted his head sharply to the side, narrowly avoiding the attack. The needle sailed past his ear by less than an inch.","A cruel smile appeared beneath his mask.","\"So that’s your trick —\"","He never finished the sentence.","The flying needle suddenly changed direction in midair. It curved unnaturally, as if pulled by an invisible hand.","The Aim Assist ability engraved into the weapon redirected its path with perfect precision.","The needle pierced straight through his throat.","Pfft!","The assassin’s eyes widened in disbelief. His hands flew to his neck. Blood poured between his fingers, hot and dark. He made a wet gurgling sound as he tried to breathe.","He collapsed beside his companion. His legs twitched twice before going still.","Silence.","Two assassins...","Dead within seconds.","The man standing atop the hood witnessed everything.","His eyes narrowed dangerously.","\"So...\"","\"You’re Dexter.\"","His voice was cold enough to freeze the air as his face was expressionless.","Then, slowly...","He drew two blades from behind his back.","They were long and thin, almost like elongated daggers. Blue lightning crackled across their edges of the blade as the air trembled.","His aura expanded and the pressure of a level 3 Super human hero spread out.","\"You just killed two of my men.\"","\"And now...\"","\"I’m going to carve you into pieces.\"","...","Dexter slowly pushed open the damaged car door.","He stepped out onto the highway.","The moment his feet touched the asphalt, his aura quietly spread outward. It wasn’t flashy. There were no visible flames or lightning. Just a subtle pressure that made the air around him feel heavier.","His gaze remained locked on the masked assassin standing atop the ruined hood.","Dexter said calmly. \"Attacking innocent civilians in broad daylight. You’ve got quite the nerve.\"","The assassin let out a cold chuckle.","\"Innocent?\"","His eyes swept toward the girls still crouched inside the car. His gaze lingered on them for a moment before returning to Dexter.","\"Why would I care if you are innocent?\"","Before Dexter could reply —","\"BOOM!\"","The assassin kicked off the hood. The already-crushed metal exploded beneath his feet, sending chunks of steel flying in every direction.","Like a bolt of lightning, he shot straight toward Dexter as a sonic boom echoed behind him.","The twin swords whistled through the air, aiming directly for Dexter’s neck. The blue lightning on their edges screamed with a high-pitched whine.","[Thank YOU Reader AATROXVOID and reader PLAGUE READER for the golden tickets!!!","[6 bonus Chapters for the Golden Tickets milestones coming right up! ]"]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40 | Spatial Cleave!","paragraphs":["The twin swords whistled through the air, aiming directly for Dexter’s neck. The blue lightning on their edges screamed with a high-pitched whine.","Fast.","Far faster than any opponent Dexter had fought before. The assassin closed the distance in the blink of an eye. One moment he was on the hood. The next moment he was right in front of Dexter’s face.","Without hesitation, Dexter waved his hand.","A long black saber instantly appeared in his grip. It materialized from his system inventory in a flash of light, the weight settling into his palm as if it had always been there.","The Type-3 Macro Splicing Saber.","He had kept it inside his system inventory ever since receiving it. Never drawn it","Now, for the first time...","He finally drew it in real combat.","\"CLANG!\"","Steel collided with steel.","A powerful shockwave erupted from the impact. A visible ring of force expanded outward, kicking up dust and debris from the highway surface.","The asphalt beneath Dexter’s feet cracked apart. Spider webs of fractures spread in every direction.","The shattered remains of the SUV were pushed backward several meters, scraping across the road with a metallic screech.","The assassin’s eyes narrowed behind his mask.","\"Your strength is impressive. It’s no wonder you are confident.\"","Dexter didn’t answer.","Instead, he twisted his wrist and slashed horizontally. The black saber cut through the air with speed that it left a dark afterimage.","The assassin blocked with one blade while counterattacking with the other.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","Three rapid collisions rang across the highway. Each one louder than the last. Each one more violent.","Sparks scattered like fireworks. They flew in every direction, landing on the asphalt and burning tiny black marks into the surface.","Nearby abandoned vehicles shook from the force. One car’s windows shattered from the pressure alone.","Blue lightning collided repeatedly with the dark steel of the Macro Splicing Saber. Each impact sent arcs of electricity crawling along the blade’s edge.","Although Dexter managed to block every strike, each collision forced him another step backward. His feet slid across the asphalt as his arms absorbed the brunt of every hit.","\"Bang!\"","His arms became numb as his feet dug trenches into the asphalt. Two long grooves trailed behind him, marking every step he had been forced to take.","\"So this is the strength of a Superhuman...\" Dexter muttered through gritted teeth.","The gap in raw cultivation still existed.","Suddenly—","His enhanced hearing picked up another sound.","A faint metallic click.","Someone was reloading a sniper rifle.","Dexter’s face changed instantly.","There was still another assassin!","Without hesitation, he activated Flame Burst.","Boom!","Flames exploded beneath his feet.","His speed increased fivefold.","His figure disappeared from before the superhuman assassin.","The masked man swung instinctively—","His blades sliced through empty air.","At that same moment...","Nearly three hundred meters away...","A sniper squeezed the trigger.","Bang!","The bullet crossed the battlefield in an instant.","Its target... Selene.","Still inside the SUV, she had no way of seeing the attack coming.","Dexter’s eyes widened.","He swung his saber toward the incoming bullet.","Too late.","The projectile had already reached her.","For a split second...","His heart nearly stopped.","Then—","A brilliant violet barrier suddenly bloomed around the girls.","BOOM!","The sniper bullet struck the barrier head-on.","Ripples spread across the protective shield.","But...","It didn’t break.","Not even a crack appeared.","Dexter let out a long breath of relief.","The Type-Three Protective Amulet had activated.","As long as the barrier remained intact...","The girls would be safe.","The sniper fired again.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","Three more anti-mana rounds slammed into the barrier.","Each impact created massive ripples...","Yet the shield remained completely unharmed.","The assassin standing opposite Dexter frowned beneath his mask.","\"So they have protective artifacts...\"","His killing intent intensified.","\"If that’s the case...\"","\"I’ll kill you first.\"","Blue lightning suddenly exploded around his body. It wasn’t just on his blades anymore. It covered his entire form. Crackling arcs of electricity danced across his arms, his chest, his legs.","Crack!","Crack!","Crack!","Bolts of electricity crawled across the ground beneath his feet. The asphalt blackened wherever the lightning touched.","His aura surged explosively as he activated his Thunder talent and disappeared into a streak of lightning. He was way faster this time as tranformed into a streak of lightning.","Dexter’s enhanced vision barely managed to follow the blur. He saw a streak of blue light moving toward him with insane speed.","He wang d to dodge but his body was simply too slow.","Without hesitation, he activated Flame Burst bloodline skill.","\"Bang!\"","Crimson flames erupted beneath his feet as his speed increased by 500%!","Just as he moved —","Slash!","One of the lightning blades grazed across his chest. The edge cut through his shirt like it was made of paper. The fabric split open instantly, revealing the skin beneath.","Blood trickled down his chest but it was kbkyrwt a superficial injury.","But the lightning energy embedded in the cut sent tiny shocks through his nerves.","Dexter’s expression darkened.","Even after dodging...","He had still been injured. The assassin was simply too fast. His attacks covered too much area. Even when Dexter moved, the blade’s reach was long enough to catch him.","The assassin smirked beneath his mask.","\"Your reaction speed is impressive.\"","\"But your cultivation is too low.\"","\"The gap between Meta Human and super human is as vast as the ocean. You cannot possible hope to bridge the gap between the Awakening Realm and the Superhuman Realm.\"","He was right. The difference between the two realms was vast.","At the awakening realm, each level up increases inches strength by 25 stats across all attributes.","But for Super human realm, each level up is a whole 50 stat points in each attribute!","Every physical attribute was elevated to a completely different level upon entering the Superhuman Realm.","Dexter tightened his grip on the Macro Splicing Saber.","Without hesitation he immediately activated Scorching Fury.","\"Bang!\"","A wave of heat burst from his body as the air around him shimmered and trembled.","His muscles swelled as tremendous strength coursed through every fiber of his being.","He could feel the power flooding through him like lava.","His combat power instantly rose by eighty percent.","A crimson aura surrounded him. It flickered like flame, dancing across his skin and along the length of his blade.","The assassin laughed.","\"Good.\"","\"I was hoping you weren’t weak.\"","In the distance, terrified civilians had already fled the highway. Cars sat abandoned in long rows. Some had their doors still hanging open where their owners had fled without thinking.","Some people hid behind abandoned vehicles, peeking over the hoods with wide, frightened eyes.","Others recorded the battle with trembling hands. Phone cameras shook violently as they tried to capture the superhuman clash.","Emergency sirens echoed faintly from afar. Getting closer. Someone had already called the authorities.","But neither fighter cared.","The assassin suddenly smirked.","\"Now, let’s battle for real!\"","The next instant —","The assassin thrust both swords toward the sky.","Lightning suddenly gathered as the morning sky darkened.","Crackling arcs of lightning danced between the two blades as a terrifying pressure spread throughout the battlefield.","The fleeing civilians looked back in horror.","\"What is that?\"","\"Is that... lightning?\"","\"Heaven...\"","The assassin roared.","\"Thunder God’s Slash!\"","The accumulated lightning poured into both sabers. The blades became blindingly bright as he slashed directly at Dexter r with unbelievable speed.","Dexter’s pupils contracted.","He instinctively knew he couldn’t block this attack through brute force alone. If he tried to meet it head-on with a simple slash, he would be cut in half along with his blade.","He took in a deep breathe and he face turned cold.","Pouring mana into the Macro Splicing Saber as he activated one of the skills of the Type 3 weapon.","Spatial Cleave!"]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41 | Killing Four Assassins","paragraphs":["Spatial Cleave.","Dexter swung his blade at the thunder attack.","A compressed crescent-shaped slash, nearly two meters tall, shot forward silently with insane speed.","There was no explosion or even a rumble, Just a clean, perfect arc of cutting force that moved through the air like a blade through water.","The attack silently split the air itself. A faint trail of distorted space followed its path, like heat rising from hot pavement.","The two techniques collided.","BOOOOOOM!!","A deafening explosion echoed across the entire highway. It shattered every remaining window on every car within a hundred-meter radius.","Lightning exploded outward in every direction. Arcs of blue electricity shot across the road like angry snakes. They struck cars, guardrails, and light poles, leaving scorch marks wherever they touched.","Space distorted violently. The air around the collision point bent and warped.","The surrounding asphalt cracked apart for dozens of meters. Massive chunks of road surface flipped into the air. A crater formed beneath the impact point, deepening with every passing millisecond.","For a brief moment...","Neither attack gave way.","The lightning pushed forward. The spatial slash pushed back. The two forces ground against each other in a contest of pure destruction.","Then —","A sharp cracking sound echoed.","The lightning slash shattered. It broke apart like glass hit by a stone. Fragments of blue energy scattered and dissolved into the air.","Dexter’s Spatial Cleave continued forward, tearing through the remaining thunder. The crescent of distorted space surged ahead with undiminished power.","The assassin’s eyes widened.","Impossible!","He had poured everything into that attack and it was his most powerful technique.","But it had been actually been overpowered.","He hurriedly crossed both sabers before him as the spatial Cleave struck.","CRACK!","Both sabers shattered into countless fragments. The metal exploded outward. Shards of steel flew in every direction like shrapnel.","The assassin froze.","For a heartbeat...","Everything became silent. The world stopped.","Then a thin crimson line appeared across the center of his body.","His eyes slowly widened in disbelief.","\"N-No...\"","Before he could finish his words, his body split cleanly into two halves as they fell in opposite directions.","Blood sprayed across the ruined highway in a wide arc. The hot red liquid splattered across the asphalt, the guardrails, and the nearby abandoned cars.","Both halves collapsed onto the ground with a dull thud.","Dexter remained standing, breathing heavily. Sweat rolled down his forehead and into his eyes. His arms trembled from exhaustion.","Nearly half the mana inside his body had vanished from that single strike. Spatial Cleave was powerful, but its cost was enormous.","Just when he sighed in relief.","He remembered there was a fourth assassin.","At this moment, a blur appeared before the SUV. The fourth assassin had given up on using sniper and rushed in personally.","Inside the vehicle, Mira, Selene, and Lyra remained protected by the shimmering violet barrier created by the Type-3 Protective Amulet.","The assassin suddenly raised his sword high into the air.","Golden flames erupted around the blade as he swung downward with all his strength.","\"BOOM!\"","The flaming sword slammed against the violet barrier as a shockwave blasted outward, sending dust and debris flying in every direction.","The shield rippled violently. Countless waves spread across its surface like ripples in a pond as the color dimmed a little but it didn’t break.","The assassin frowned. His brow furrowed behind his mask.","He attacked again and again and again but the shield actually held.","Golden flames exploded repeatedly against the barrier. Each strike sent another shockwave across the highway.","Yet the violet shield merely trembled before returning to normal each time.","Inside the barrier, the girls watched with cold and expressions on their faces. Mira’s jaw was clenched. Selene’s hands were balled into fists. Lyra’s eyes were wide behind her glasses.","But the girls weren’t panicked at all. They were filled with rage and anger.","In their prime, a Level 5 Superhuman was nothing in their eyes. Before their injuries, they were insanely strong and could handle anyone below the peak Super Human realm..","They were monsters who had faced monsters and enemies that would make this assassin tremble with fear.","They had once fought monsters that could destroy cities.","And now...","Now a low-rank hero was actually showing off and threatening to kill them. A Level 5 Superhuman. Someone they would have swatted aside like a fly in their prime.","Moreover, they lacked the strength to defend themselves. They couldn’t fight. They couldn’t run. They could only sit and watch as someone attacked them like helpless prey.","This made the three girls really, really angry.","The Type-3 Protective Amulet truly possessed defensive power capable of blocking attacks from Peak Superhuman experts","As long as the barrier remained active...","The assassin was he was about to strike again.","But —","A streak of crimson flames shot across the battlefield.","The second assassin sensed the danger and immediately abandoned the barrier and he turned just in time to block.","CLANG!","The Macro Splicing Saber collided with the flaming sword.","Sparks exploded everywhere. Crimson sparks from Dexter’s flame-enhanced blade.","Golden sparks from the assassin’s burning sword. They mixed in the air like two colors of fire dancing together.","The force of the collision pushed both men backward several meters. Their feet carved grooves into the asphalt as they skidded apart.","The assassin smirked beneath his mask. His eyes glittered with amusement.","\"Because you killed Thunder Blade, you assume you can do the same to me?\"","He twirled his sword casually. Golden flames spiraled around the blade in elegant patterns.","Golden flames erupted around his body. His entire figure became enveloped in blazing fire. The heat was intense. Oppressive. It radiated outward in waves.","\"C-Rank Talent...\"","Golden Flame Body.","The temperature around him rose instantly and the air shimmered.","Even from several meters away, Dexter could feel the heat pressing against his skin. It was like standing next to an open furnace.","Dexter narrowed his eyes.","Another elemental talent.","And this time he was a Level 5 Superhuman. Two full levels above the first assassin.","This battle...","...was becoming far more dangerous than he had anticipated."]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42 | KILL!!!","paragraphs":["Golden flames roared around the assassin like a blazing cloak.","Dexter tightened his grip on the Macro Splicing Saber.","This assassin was even more dangerous than the first.","His mana was still only half full after using Spatial Cleave.","Scorching Fury had already been active for nearly a minute and he had activated Flame Burst Constantly.","The techniques put tremendous strain on his muscles. Every second it remained active, his body endured more stress.","He couldn’t afford a drawn-out battle. Not against a Level 5 Superhuman or with half his mana gone.","The assassin grinned.","\"So you’re the one Lord Voss wants dead.\"","\"I expected someone stronger.\"","The name meant nothing to Dexter. Lord Voss. He filed it away for later. If he survived.","Before Dexter could reply —","\"Boom!\"","The assassin vanished. One moment he was standing there, wrapped in golden flames. The next moment, he was gone.","Golden flames exploded beneath his feet as he appeared behind Dexter almost instantly.","His flaming sword descended toward Dexter’s back as he slashed at his neck.","Dexter reacted purely on instinct activating Flame Burst to raise his agility as he spun around and raised his saber.","Clang!","The collision sent sparks flying in every direction. Dexter’s entire arm went numb from the impact as he was blasted backward.","He flew through the air for several meters before crashing into an abandoned sedan parked across the highway.","\"Bang!\"","Dexter’s back slammed against the car’s hood. The metal crumpled beneath his weight. The windshield shattered. The entire vehicle slid backward several meters before smashing into the guardrail with a screech of metal.","Its alarm immediately began blaring. A loud, piercing wail that added to the chaos of the battlefield.","Dexter barely had time to steady himself. He pushed himself off the crumpled hood and raised his saber.","The assassin was already in front of him.","His speed was frightening. He had crossed the distance in the time it took Dexter to blink.","The flaming blade thrust toward Dexter’s abdomen like a venomous snake.","Dexter eyes suddenly turned vicious and instead of dodging he stepped forward into the blade.","\"Shhhk!\"","The assassin’s eyes widened behind his mask as he hadn’t expected for Dexter to step towards his own death.","The blade pierced straight into Dexter’s side.","The flaming sword slid underneath his ribs with a sickening ease. The heat cauterized the wound instantly, preventing excessive bleeding but sending blinding pain through every nerve in his body.","Shhk!","Pain shot through Dexter’s body as his vision blurred and his knees buckled.","The assassin grinned viciously. The blade was buried in Dexter’s side. One pull and the intestines would follow.","\"You’ve lost.\"","But the smile on Dexter’s face only widened.","\"...Got you.\"","Before the assassin could react —","Dexter’s left hand shot forward, gripping the assassin’s sword arm with terrifying force.","The assassin ws stunned and he immediately shot backwards but he Dezt r followed as he held his hand like his life depended on it.","The assassin struggled and frienws to pull free.","But Dexter’s grip was absolute. He didn’t give him a single change to.","Then...","Dexter’s chest began glowing.","Molten crimson light spread from his heart to his throat.","Veins of blazing gold crawled across his neck as they pulsed with energy.","The temperature around him rose explosively.","The assassin’s expression finally changed and for the first time since the battle began, fear appeared in his eyes.","\"W-What are you —\"","Dexter opened his mouth.","\"ROOOOOOOOOOAAAR!\"","\"Flame Demon’s Wrath.\"","A torrent of demonic fire erupted from his mouth.","BOOOOOOM!!","The crimson-gold inferno engulfed the assassin completely as it wrapped around the assassin’s body like a living thing, seeking every gap in his defense.","The flames were crimson at their core and gold at their edges. They burned with a heat that melted the asphalt into liquid. The air itself ignited. Oxygen became fuel.","The man roared in pain as he desperately unleashed his own Golden Flame talent. His body blazed with golden fire. A blazing golden barrier formed around him, a sphere of protective flame that he poured every ounce of his mana into maintaining.","The two flames clashed violently. Crimson-gold against pure gold. Demon fire against human talent.","For several seconds...","The golden flames resisted and the barrier held. The assassin’s C-Rank talent was strong enough to temporarily withstand the demonic fire’s assault.","But only temporarily.","The demonic fire devoured everything in its path. It ate through the golden barrier like acid through paper. It consumed the golden flames and grew stronger from them. It fed on the assassin’s own energy and turned it against him.","The assassin’s inhuman screams echoed across the highway. The sound was inhuman. It was the scream of a man being burned alive from the inside out.","\"AAAAAAAHHHHH!!\"","His flesh burned away almost instantly. The golden barrier collapsed. The flames reached deep into his skull and feasted.","His face fell off and liquidfy against the demonic flames. His muscles dripped to the ground and his bones blackened and within seconds...","Nothing of his face remained except a charred skeleton skull replacing his head.","His body was actually intact and within seconds, he fell to the ground and collapsed.","Silence.","Dexter staggered backward as he felt dizzy.","His breathing had become ragged and each breath burned his lungs as he tasted ash in his mouth.","The Flame Demon’s Wrath had consumed an enormous amount of mana. It was one of his most powerful techniques, but its cost was devastating. He could feel his core nearly empty.","Combined with the wound in his abdomen...","His body was reaching its limit.","He looked down at the sword still embedded in his side.","Grimacing, he gripped the hilt. His fingers wrapped around the hilt and he dqueezed tight.","\"...Tch.\"","With one swift motion —","Shhk!","He pulled the blade free. The metal slid out with a wet sound. Blood followed immediately. It poured from the wound in a steady stream, running down his side and dripping onto the ground.","But almost immediately...","The regenerative power of his Origin Bloodline and the Slaughter Demon Body technique activated as his cells started to regenerate and heal rapidly."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43 | Extract C Rank Talent: Thunder & Golden Flames","paragraphs":["The Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture and his Origin Bloodline began working simultaneously.","Warm energy spread through his body.","The torn flesh around the wound slowly wriggled before beginning to close.","Although the injury wasn’t healed completely, the bleeding quickly stopped.","Dexter tore a strip from his ruined shirt and wrapped it tightly around his abdomen before letting out a long breath.","\"I really need to stop getting stabbed...\"","He gave a bitter smile.","This battle had shown him just how dangerous the Superhuman Realm truly was. If he wanted to survive more assassination attempts, then he would need to get stronger.","The fastest way to grow stronger is to level up. And to level up one needs to head into dungeons to kill monsters and level up quickly.","He staggered towards the corpses of the assassins and activated his second system.","\"Extract!\"","A faint golden light enveloped the corpse. The light pulsed twice before a translucent blue notification appeared before Dexter’s eyes.","[Extracted +5 Strength, +6 Agility]","The numbers flowed into his body like warm water. He could feel the changes immediately. His muscles tightened slightly. His reflexes sharpened. The change wasn’t dramatic, but it was real.","He moved to the second corpse. The assassin whose throat he had pierced with the curving needle. The man’s neck was still stained dark with dried blood.","\"Extract!\"","[Extracted +5 Mana, +6 Agility, +5 Strength, +6 Physique]","More energy flowed into him. This time the sensation was stronger. His mana pool expanded slightly. His body felt sturdier. More resilient. Like someone had reinforced his bones with steel.","He moved to the third corpse. The first Superhuman assassin. The one he had cut in half with Spatial Cleave. The two halves lay side by side on the asphalt, separated by a pool of darkening blood.","\"Extract!\"","[Extracted + C-Rank Golden Flame, +3 Strength, +7 Agility]","Dexter’s eyes widened.","He actually extracted their talents too?","The Golden Flame ability surged into his body like a wave of liquid fire. It settled deep inside his core, nestling beside his existing abilities like a new addition to a family. He could feel the flame’s potential. Its heat. Its hunger. It was a C-Rank talent, which was considered above average for most awakeners.","He had just stolen a dead man’s talent.","The implications were staggering.","Finally, he moved to the fourth corpse. Or what remained of it. The charred skeleton of the second Superhuman assassin. The bones were black and brittle. They crumbled slightly when Dexter knelt beside them.","\"Extract!\"","[Extracted + C-Rank Thunder Manipulation, +7 Strength, +1 Agility, +3 Mana, +4 Physique]","A crackling surge of electrical energy raced through his body. Blue sparks danced across his fingertips for a brief moment before fading. The Thunder Manipulation talent embedded itself beside the Golden Flame ability, creating a small storm of competing energies inside his core.","Dexter stared at his hands.","He now possessed two additional C-Rank talents.","Golden Flame.","Thunder Manipulation.","Combined with his existing abilities...","His combat potential had increased dramatically.","But the excitement was short-lived.","He suddenly heard sirens in the distance.","Woo — Woo — Woo —","The sound was faint at first. Barely audible over the ambient noise of the city. But it grew louder with each passing second. More sirens joined the chorus. From multiple directions.","Dexter’s expression shifted instantly.","More than a dozen police vehicles sped toward the highway from both directions.","Behind them came several armored response trucks belonging to the Hero Association.","Their flashing lights illuminated the battlefield.","Within moments, the entire highway was surrounded.","Officers quickly aimed their weapons toward the scene.","When they saw four masked corpses lying on the ground and only one bloodied young man still standing...","Every one of them froze.","\"...What happened here?\"","One officer muttered in disbelief.","Another looked at the assassin whose body had been sliced perfectly into two.","His eyes widened.","\"That... wasn’t done by an explosion.\"","\"It was one slash.\"","Nearby, another investigator examined the burned face corpse.","\"There isn’t even enough face left for identification...\"","The surrounding civilians, who had hidden behind abandoned vehicles, slowly emerged once they heard the commotion stop. The battle was over. The danger had passed. Police and heroes were on the scene.","People stepped out from behind cars, bushes, and guardrails. Some were shaking. Some were crying. Some were recording on their phones despite the earlier destruction of most devices close to the battle.","A woman holding a child hurried toward the nearest officer.","\"Officer! Officer! There was a battle!\"","\"We saw fire and lightning!\"","\"It was terrifying!\"","An elderly man approached another officer.","\"I’ve never seen anything like it.\"","\"The whole highway shook.\"","\"I thought it was an earthquake at first.\"","More witnesses gathered. Each one tried to explain what they had seen. Their accounts were fragmented. Confused. Contradictory.","Some mentioned a man with a black sword.","Others mentioned blue lightning.","Some mentioned golden flames.","Some mentioned crimson fire.","None of them could provide a clear description.","---","Dexter remained calm despite the dozens of eyes fixed on him.","He had already changed into a fresh set of clothes from his system inventory while the police were busy securing the scene. Apart from the bandage wrapped around his abdomen beneath his shirt, there was nothing to suggest he had just fought two Superhuman assassins and killed them too.","The lead investigator stopped before him.","\"I’m Senior Inspector Harris of the City Police Department. I need your statement.\"","Dexter nodded.","\"I’ll cooperate.\"","The investigator activated a recording device.","\"Tell me exactly what happened.\"","Dexter took a deep breath before speaking.","\"\"We were driving home from the hotel when the driver was suddenly shot.\"","His voice was steady. Measured. He allowed a slight tremor to enter his tone to sell the fear.","\"I didn’t see the bullet. I just heard a sound and then... the driver’s head...\"","He paused as he swallowed uncomfortably.","\"The car started swerving. I grabbed the wheel and managed to stop it beneath the bridge.\"","\"Then several masked men attacked us.\"","The investigator’s eyes narrowed."]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44 | Investigation","paragraphs":["The investigator’s eyes narrowed.","\"How many?\"","\"Four that I saw,\" Dexter said. \"There might have been more.\"","\"What happened after that?\"","Dexter frowned as though recalling the terrifying scene. His brow furrowed. His hands clenched slightly.","\"Before they could reach us... someone arrived.\"","\"Someone?\"","\"A hero.\"","The officers immediately leaned closer. The word \"hero\" carried specific weight in their world. Heroes were licensed combatants registered with the Hero Association.","But unlicensed heroes existed too. Powerful awakeners who operated outside the system. Some were vigilantes. Some were simply private citizens who intervened when danger arose.","\"Did you recognize the hero?\"","Dexter slowly shook his head.","\"No.\"","\"He wore a black mask and a long coat. I couldn’t see his face.\"","\"He moved too fast.\"","\"I only remember seeing flashes of fire and sword light.\"","\"The battle lasted less than a minute.\"","\"By the time it was over... the assassins were already dead.\"","The investigator studied Dexter’s face carefully. His eyes searched for signs of deception.","Dexter met his gaze without flinching.","He had practiced controlling his expressions during his time with the Ashford family. Years of hiding his true feelings behind a neutral mask had given him near-perfect control over his facial muscles.","The investigator asked one final question.","\"Did the hero tell you his name?\"","Dexter shook his head again.","\"No.\"","\"He only told us to stay inside the barrier.\"","\"Then he left.\"","\"Immediately.\"","\"I wanted to thank him, but he disappeared before anyone could react.\"","The investigator held his gaze for a moment longer before sighing. He stopped the recording. The red light vanished.","\"We’ll investigate further.\"","\"If we identify the hero, the Hero Association will certainly reward him.\"","Dexter merely nodded.","\"I hope so.\"","He kept his expression neutral. Inside, he felt a spark of satisfaction.","His story was airtight. The battlefield supported his account. The level of destruction was far beyond what an Awakening Realm cultivator should be capable of.","Neither pointed toward a recently awakened young man.","Both pointed toward a powerful, unidentified hero.","The police would search for this phantom hero. They would waste time and resources chasing a ghost.","Meanwhile, Dexter would remain hidden in plain sight.","The investigator glanced toward the armored police vehicle where the three girls were resting.","\"We’ll also need statements from your wives.\"","\"They were present during the attack.\"","Dexter’s expression softened.","\"I understand, Inspector... but I’d rather you leave them alone.\"","\"They’ve already suffered enough.\"","\"They’re all disabled.\"","\"One is blind.\"","\"One is deaf and mute.\"","\"And one is completely paralyzed.\"","\"They’ve only just begun recovering from the trauma of the previous attack.\"","\"If they’re questioned right now...\"","\"They’ll only relive today’s incident all over again.\"","\"I can answer anything you need.\"","The investigator looked toward the medical vehicle where his wives are being examined.","He saw Mira sitting silently in her wheelchair.","Selene’s face was pale and blind","Lyra sat beside them with her head lowered, clutching her phone tightly.","The three girls genuinely looked traumatized.","After a long moment, the investigator sighed.","\"...Very well.\"","\"We won’t question them today.\"","\"But if this investigation requires it later, we’ll have to ask for their cooperation.\"","Dexter inclined his head.","\"Thank you.\"","Inside, he breathed a sigh of relief.","---","As the investigation continued, several officers began questioning nearby witnesses. Their statements were recorded and cross-referenced. Each witness told a slightly different version of the same event, which was normal. Human memory was unreliable, especially under stress.","One of the younger policemen suddenly looked toward Dexter. His eyes widened. His mouth opened slightly. He took a step forward.","\"Wait...\"","\"You’re that guy, aren’t you?\"","Dexter turned toward him with a politely confused expression.","\"The one from the news.\"","The officer snapped his fingers as he tried to recall the details.","\"The bastard son of the Ashford Family...\"","\"...who married three disabled girls.\"","Several officers immediately recognized him as well. Murmurs spread through the group like wildfire.","\"I remember him.\"","\"The Hero Association publicly compensated him after his house was attacked.\"","\"That’s right. The monster attack. It was all over the news.\"","\"Poor guy.\"","\"Now assassins are after him too?\"","\"What did he do to piss someone off this badly?\"","Whispers spread among the gathered crowd. Not just among the officers. The civilians who had gathered nearby also began to recognize him. Phones were raised. Cameras clicked.","Some looked at Dexter sympathetically. Their eyes carried genuine pity. They saw a young man who had been dealt a terrible hand in life. Born into a wealthy family that rejected him. Married to three women who couldn’t care for themselves. Attacked by monsters. And now targeted by assassins.","Others simply shook their heads.","\"What terrible luck...\"","\"The poor man just can’t catch a break.\"","\"First monsters. Now assassins. What’s next?\"","\"Someone up there really doesn’t like him.\"","Dexter smiled awkwardly but didn’t respond. He rubbed the back of his neck. He looked down at his feet. He played the part of the embarrassed, unfortunate victim perfectly.","The less attention on his true strength, the better.","Fortunately, no one had managed to record the battle clearly.","The violent shockwaves from the clashes had shattered the phones of everyone standing nearby.","Those farther away had only captured blurry flashes of lightning and fire from hundreds of meters away.","The videos circulating online were nothing more than indistinct streaks of light.","No one could identify the mysterious swordsman.","---","After nearly an hour, the police finished collecting evidence.","The four assassin corpses were loaded into specialized containment vehicles.","The damaged vehicle was towed away.","Fragments of the shattered weapons were carefully sealed as evidence. The broken pieces of the first assassin’s twin lightning blades were collected in a special mana-dampening container. The melted remnants of the second assassin’s flaming sword were scraped off the asphalt and stored separately.","Senior Inspector Harris walked over once more. His trench coat fluttered slightly in the morning breeze. His expression was grave.","\"Mr. Dexter.\"","\"We’ll arrange transportation.\"","\"Given today’s incident, it isn’t safe for you to travel alone.\"","Dexter nodded.","\"Thank you.\"","A heavily armored police vehicle escorted them all the way home. The vehicle was reinforced with mana-infused plating and equipped with multiple defensive systems. It could withstand attacks from Superhuman-level threats.","Two patrol cars led the convoy while another followed behind. Their sirens blared continuously, clearing traffic from their path. Drivers pulled aside as the procession passed, their faces pressed against their windows in curiosity.","The entire journey passed without incident.","Inside the vehicle, silence filled the compartment.","The girls remained unusually quiet.","Several minutes later, Mira finally broke the silence.","\"...Are you hurt?\"","Her voice was softer than usual.","Dexter looked toward her and smiled.","\"I’m fine.\"","\"You saw me, It was only a few scratches.\"","Mira frowned but didn’t reply.","She didn’t believe him. Selene lowered her head.","Although she couldn’t see him earlier, she had heard the sounds of battle.","Every explosion...","Every collision...","Every scream...","She knew how dangerous that fight had been.","Lyra quickly typed on her phone.","The AI voice spoke.","\"Are you really okay?\"","Dexter looked at the three worried faces before chuckling.","\"I told you, I am tougher than I look.\"","Only then did the tense atmosphere inside the vehicle ease slightly.","Even so...","The three girls secretly resolved to become stronger.","If they had been stronger today...","Dexter wouldn’t have had to risk his life protecting them again.","But Dexter’s mind was elsewhere.","[Ding! 10,000 Times Investment System]"]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45 | REWARDS! REWARDS!! REWARDS!!!","paragraphs":["[10,000x Investment System Activated...]","Calculating Investment Return...","Target Protected: Mira, Lyra and Selene from Super human assassins, host fought above his realm and won.","Reward Multiplier: ×100","Congratulations! You have received the following rewards:","---","1. Type-4 Spatial Storage Ring","A high-grade storage treasure capable of storing up to 10,000 cubic meters of items.","Unlike ordinary storage rings, living creatures can survive inside for a short period of time, and time flows ten times slower within the storage space, greatly preserving herbs, food, and treasures.","---","2. Mysterious Primordial Beast Egg","An ancient egg sealed for countless ages.","Status: Unhatched.","\"Cultivate with it by your side and it will eventually hatch.\"","---","3. Talent Upgrade Cards x 3","Three rare upgrade cards capable of raising any talent below C-Rank directly to C-Rank without side effects.","---","4. Mana Affinity Upgraded","S-Rank → SS-Rank","---","5. Foodsmith Advancement","Peak Grandmaster → Early Great Grandmaster Foodsmith","Permanently strengthen the body.","Increase cultivation speed.","Heal internal injuries.","Remove impurities.","Improve mana recovery.","Slightly increase talent potential after long-term consumption.","---","6. Five Years of Pure Cultivation","Without suffering bottlenecks or unstable foundations, you instantly obtained five years’ worth of cultivation.","---","7. Heavenly Treasury Gift Pack","50 Origin Sun Fruits","30 bottles of Star Essence serum","10 Heavenly Marrow Cleansing Capsule","5 Millennium Blood Ginseng","5 Void Spirit Lotuses","---","8. Type-4 Regeneration Ring","A powerful healing treasure.","After a serious injury, the ring automatically accelerates regeneration by 500% while continuously supplying vitality.","Even broken bones and pierced organs could heal rapidly, provided there’s enough life force remaining.","---","9. Ancient Weapon Blueprint","Reward Obtained: Origin Forge Manual","A mysterious forging inheritance containing methods to create Type-4, Type-5, and Type-6 weapons.","---","10. Bloodline Evolution Crystal: Grants or evolve bloodlines.","11. Extreme Slaughter Demon Body Tier 4 evolve to Tier 5","12. Talent Upgraded — D-Rank → C-Rank (Enhanced Hearing)","13. Bloodline Upgraded — Origin Grade → Ancient GRADE","[New Bloodline: Chaos Flame Demon Bloodline (Ancient Grade)]","14. Bloodline Upgraded — Origin Grade → Ancient GRADE","15. Type 5 Protective Amulet","16. Type 5 House Protection Talisman","17.Type 5 Void Star Blade.","18. Endurance Buddha Scripture upgrades to 6th Tier Technique","---","\"Void Star Saber\"","[Rank] Type-5 Divine Weapon (Sealed)","[Description]","A legendary saber forged from Void Star Iron and tempered within the heart of a dying star. Infused with the power of space itself, every swing distorts reality, allowing its wielder to cut through both matter and space. Most of its true power remains sealed.","---","[Passive Effects]","\"Void Edge\"","➤ Increases sword attack power by 100%.","\"Star Velocity\"","➤ Increases sword attack speed by 30%.","\"Armor Break\"","➤ Ignores 20% of an enemy’s physical defense.","\"Self-Regeneration\"","➤ Automatically repairs minor damage and can never become dull.","\"Spatial Resonance\" (Sealed)","➤ Grows stronger alongside its wielder, unlocking additional abilities as its seals are broken.","---","[Active Skills]","\"Void Slash\"","➤ Releases a compressed blade of spatial energy that travels hundreds of meters, slicing through everything in its path.","[Cooldown]: 20 Seconds","\"Star Rend\"","➤ A lightning-fast strike capable of cleaving through armor, barriers, and reinforced defenses.","[Cooldown]: 45 Seconds","\"Spatial Rift\"","➤ Tears open a temporary rift in space, allowing attacks to bypass obstacles and strike hidden enemies.","[Cooldown]: 2 Minutes","\"Void Domain\" [Locked]","➤ Creates a domain that suppresses enemies while greatly enhancing Dexter’s sword techniques.","[Unlock Requirement]: Break the Second Seal.","\"Star Annihilation\" [Locked]","➤ The weapon’s ultimate technique. A world-cleaving slash capable of devastating an entire battlefield.","[Unlock Requirement]: Fully awaken the Void Star Saber.","---","[Weapon Spirit]","\"Void Star Spirit\" [Dormant]","An ancient weapon spirit slumbers within the blade. It will awaken once Dexter reaches the Superhuman Realm or fulfills the hidden conditions required to break the saber’s first seal. Upon awakening, it can guide Dexter’s swordsmanship, unlock sealed abilities, and reveal the weapon’s forgotten legacy.","...","[Bloodline Evolution Crystal]","A rare crystal born from the essence of ancient bloodlines. It can awaken dormant bloodline abilities, evolve an existing bloodline into a higher tier, or strengthen inherited talents. The effectiveness depends on the user’s talent, compatibility, and the rarity of the bloodline.","---","[Type-5 Protective Amulet]","A high-grade defensive treasure capable of automatically creating a powerful energy barrier when its wearer is in mortal danger. The barrier can withstand several attacks from Type-5 opponents before shattering. Once depleted, the amulet requires time or energy to recharge.","---","[Type-5 House Protection Talisman]","A large-scale defensive formation talisman that envelops an entire residence. Once activated, it creates a barrier capable of resisting attacks from Type-5 experts, conceals the house from spiritual detection, and warns the owner whenever an intruder attempts to enter.","---","[Origin Sun Fruit]","A legendary fruit nourished by the essence of the primordial sun. Consuming it greatly enhances vitality, strengthens the physique, purifies spiritual energy, and significantly increases cultivation speed. Those with fire or light affinity gain even greater benefits.","---","[Star Essence Serum]","A refined serum containing concentrated stellar essence. It rapidly replenishes mana, accelerates recovery from exhaustion, and permanently increases mana reserves with repeated use. It also improves the body’s affinity for absorbing ambient mana.","---","[Heavenly Marrow Cleansing Capsule]","A supreme body-refining pill that cleanses the bone marrow, removes accumulated impurities, and reconstructs the body’s foundation. It enhances talent, strengthens the skeletal system, and increases the user’s potential for future breakthroughs.","---","[Millennium Blood Ginseng]","A precious herb that has absorbed energy for over a thousand years. It greatly restores vitality, replenishes blood essence, heals severe internal injuries, and extends one’s lifespan. It can also be used as a primary ingredient in high-grade alchemy.","---","[Void Mana Lotus]","A mysterious lotus born within unstable spatial rifts. It nourishes the soul, strengthens spiritual power, improves comprehension, and grants resistance against soul attacks and mental illusions. It is an invaluable treasure for mages, and anyone cultivating mental techniques.","-","Dexter was in shock through out the entire ride.","These amount of rewards if taken to the outside world was enough to start a war!","...","20 minutes later, they pulled directly in front of the house.","Most people had gone to work so the street was deserted.","Dexter carried Mira out and the others got out themselves.","\"Mr Ashford, we will keep a vehicle out front overnight just to be careful.\"","Dexter nodded at the officer and replied. \"Thank you. \""]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46 | Diamond Rice & Promise Not To Leave","paragraphs":["He opened the door and under the envy and pity of the officers, Dexter and his wives all they all went in.","The apartment finally felt like a home again.","Everything had been repaired. The window, the door, the chairs and even the cracked floor.","It was as though nothing ever happened there.","Dexter spent the next hour arranging everyone’s luggage.","He carried each bag to the appropriate room without rushing. He neatly placed Mira’s belongings beside her room, organized Selene’s clothes inside the wardrobe with precision, and helped Lyra arrange hers as well.","As he looked around the bedrooms, he scratched the back of his head.","\"Two more beds...\"","Three girls sharing two beds wasn’t exactly ideal. Once he earned more money, new beds would be one of the first things he purchased.","With that decided, Dexter headed into the kitchen.","He rolled up his sleeves and washed his hands. He opened the refrigerator and examined the ingredients inside. Vegetables. Eggs. Rice. Seasonings. Nothing special, but enough to work with.","He pulled out a cutting board and began slicing vegetables with practiced ease. The knife moved rhythmically against the wood as he sliced them precisely.","Soon, the aroma of freshly cooked food spread throughout the apartment, making throat dry and stomach grumble.","At that moment, a system notification rang out inside of his head.","[Ding! Congratulations! You’ve successfully prepared your first Effect Meal!]","[Name: Comfort Vegetable Fried Rice]","[Grade: 1]","[Effect: Soothes the consumer’s muscles, relieving minor fatigue and accelerating physical recovery for 30 minutes.]","[Description: A simple yet nourishing meal infused with a vast amount of mana. While its taste is slightly above, it’s effects are impressive, capable of easing sore muscle soreness and restore stamina, sooth the meridians and increase mana recovery after strenuous activity.]","The smell seeped under bedroom doors and drifted through every corner of the small living space.","Even though everyone had eaten before leaving the hotel, especially Lyra, who had consumed enough food for three people, she still wandered into the dining room with sparkling eyes the moment she smelled Dexter’s cooking. Her feet padded softly against the floor. Her nose led the way.","\"...Hungry already?\" Dexter laughed from the stove.","Lyra nodded without the slightest embarrassment. Her eyes were fixed on the pan where eggs sizzled in golden oil.","Mira rolled her eyes from her wheelchair.","\"She’s a bottomless pit.\"","Selene simply smiled faintly before taking her seat at the table. She found her chair by memory and sat down gracefully.","The four of them ate breakfast together.","The moment the first bite entered their mouths, the girls froze.","A warm current flowed through their bodies like liquid sunlight. It soothed their muscles, eased their joints, and replenished their stamina.","Even the exhaustion from cultivating throughout the night and day disappeared almost instantly.","The internal soreness in Mira’s legs faded. The stiffness in Selene’s shoulders melted away. The fog in Lyra’s mind cleared.","Lyra’s eyes lit up like two burning stars.","Without hesitation, she began stuffing food into her mouth at an alarming speed. Rice disappeared in spoonfuls. Vegetables vanished between bites. She barely chewed before swallowing.","One bowl.","Two bowls.","Three bowls...","Dexter watched in amazement.","\"At this point, I’m convinced your stomach is connected to another dimension.\"","Lyra read the words and smiled sheepishly with rice grains stuck to her cheek and continued eating.","---","[Ding!]","[10,000× Investment System Activated]","[Investment Target: Mira, Selene, Lyra","[Investment: You sincerely cooked for your three wives]","[Multiplier: 100× ]","[Calculating Returns...]","[Rewards Obtained:]","[Cooking Mastery has advanced.]","[Foodsmith Rank: Peak Master → Grandmaster.]","[Grandmaster Foodsmith]","[Info: You can now prepare foods capable of nourishing the body, strengthening physiques, restoring vitality, healing internal injuries, and granting temporary or permanent attributes depending on the ingredients used]","Dexter blinked.","\"...Grandmaster already?\"","He stared at the translucent blue screen floating before his eyes. The golden letters gleamed softly.","Before he could react further, another notification appeared.","[Rewards Obtained:]","- Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot","- 50 kg Diamond Rice","Dexter’s eyes widened.","The information flowed into his mind immediately. It arrived like a stream of pure knowledge, filling his understanding without effort.","Diamond Rice was an extremely precious grain nurtured inside high-density mana fields. Every single grain contained pure life essence condensed over months of careful cultivation. The grains absorbed ambient mana from their environment, storing it inside their crystalline structure.","Long-term consumption greatly strengthened the body. Muscles became denser. Bones grew harder. Reflexes sharpened.","Legends even claimed that someone who ate Diamond Rice continuously for an entire year would awaken the legendary Diamond Physique — a body with skin as tough as steel and bones as hard as diamonds. Blades would break against it. Blunt force would barely dent it.","Most people dismissed it as a myth.","Not because it was impossible...","But because no one, not even the wealthiest family in the city could afford enough Diamond Rice for a year. A single kilogram could cost more than most families earned in a year.","Yet inside Dexter’s system inventory...","There was an entire fifty-kilogram bag.","He couldn’t help smiling.","This time, even Mira who usually didn’t finish her food told Dexter to continue feeding her till not even a single grain was left.","As he stood up to clean the dining table, the girls glanced at each other as though in silent communication and didn’t stand to go cultivate.","Dexter frowned and asked. \"is there something wrong?\"","Mira glanced at the girls then Selene opened her mouth to speak in her tiny voice. \"We just want to ask.\"","Dexter raises an eyebrow as he placed the bowls in the sink. \" Ask what?\"","\"Why?\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and asked. \"Why what?\"","Lyra types something on her phone and a female robotic voice came out. \"Why are you doing all of this? Risking your live for us, taking care of us, taking our pain away. Why? What do you gain from it all? No one truly does anything so selfless.\"","\"You are a good person and we all know that. But at this moment, it’s gotten a bit extreme. You risking your lives to save ours and killing those assassins. Not kneingvif you would live or die...its a bit much for us to handle. We haven’t owned anyone such huge a favor.\""]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47 | First Level Of Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture","paragraphs":["Mira opened her mouth and she continued. \"From what we could discern over the past few days, you’re obviously not from a normal background. If you were lucky enough to come across a 7th tier technique, you could have given any of the Seven main families in the city in exchange for resources and power. But you gave them to us to use instead. Which means you weren’t lucky to come across the technique but was given to you instead by.\"","Mira’s eyes glinted as she deduced him.\"It’s obvious you have a mysterious person or even a company backing you. One that is even greater than the seven families combined. We are just confused as to why you still decide to stay with us, playing the perfect husband for his three Crippled Wives.\"","Mira’s tone changed as she continued dryly","\"And don’t tell me you fell in love with one of us.\"","\"You see me naked everyday but never aroused.\"","The girls blushed slightly when they heard Mira say this so indifferently.","But Mira continued.","\"So I know it’s not love nor is it lust that’s making you stay with us but something else entirely.\"","Dexter froze slightly at Mira’s deduction. The girls were actually smarter than they looked.","He looked at three of them andsmiled. \"Do you want your pain back or want to stop cultivating the 7th tier technique? Or do you want me to stop taking care of you three?\"","The girls blinked their eyes, they certainly don’t want that. Mira frowned. \"That’s not what we’re asking you.\"","Dexter shrugged and turned around to wash the plates. \"I certainly have my reasons for being with you three and rest assured, my intentions are pure. I don’t have plans on leaving you three any time soon. Unless either of you want to leave me, then that’s fine.\"","He turned back and his expression turned serious. \"I promise not to leave you three. Satisfied?\"","The three stared at Dexter with various expressions on their faces. While they truly wish to know his intentions, him specifically telling them he would never leave them made thee hearts fluttered and even the indifferent Mira’s felt her belly tickled with butterflies.","Selene squeezed her legs as she stared at Dexter with an expression different from the two girls.","Dexter hadn’t particularly answered their questions but they were quite satisfied.","Mira grunted an unknown word while Selene and Lyra smiled internally as they each head to their favorite position to cultivate.","Dexter was deep in thought. It was true. Without the system, he most likely wouldn’t have cared for them.","But now, he was starting to carw for them even without the system. And the system had become an added bonus reward for him.","---","That evening, Dexter prepared dinner once more.","He used the new Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot for the first time. The pot was crafted from a dark metal that seemed to absorb light. Its surface was smooth and warm to the touch. When heated, it distributed temperature perfectly across every inch of its interior.","No hot spots. No cold zones. Perfect circulation.","The food cooked faster and more evenly than anything he had prepared before.","The moment he finished cooking...","[Ding!]","[100× Return Activated.]","[Reward Obtained: E-Rank Talent — Alchemist Flame.]","A warm crimson flame suddenly appeared above Dexter’s palm.","It flickered gently like a candle in a quiet room.","Unlike ordinary fire, it emitted no burning heat. It didn’t scorch. It didn’t spread.","Instead, it carried a gentle warmth that perfectly controlled temperature. He could feel the flame responding to his will. Hotter. Cooler. Wider. Narrower. Every adjustment happened instantly.","It was the ideal flame for cooking.","It was also the ideal flame for alchemy.","But that was a thought for another day.","\"This will make fodd smithing meals much easier...\"","The corners of his lips rose.","He cultivated the entire night but just an hour into the cultivation, his body rumbled as he broke through to the first level of the Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture.","The Flesh Tempering Realm.","Eternal Buddha Endurance Scripture","A legendary body-refining art that transforms pain into power. Every wound, hardship, poison, and trial endured permanently tempers the body. The greater the suffering, the greater the growth.","---","First Stage – Flesh Tempering","The practitioner’s body begins to convert pain into vitality. Muscles, tendons, and bones gradually become stronger with every injury, while minor wounds heal faster than before. Fatigue also recovers more quickly, allowing the practitioner to withstand longer battles.","---","Second Stage – Iron Bones","The skeleton undergoes a complete transformation, becoming as tough as refined steel. Bones are far more difficult to break, and even when fractured, they mend at an astonishing rate. The practitioner’s resistance to pain and ordinary toxins also increases significantly.","---","Third Stage – Golden Organs","The internal organs are refined into a far more resilient state, making them resistant to internal injuries and disease. The practitioner’s vitality and stamina increase greatly, while regeneration becomes noticeably faster. Most common poisons lose much of their effectiveness.","---","Fourth Stage – Vajra Flesh","The flesh and skin become incredibly durable, allowing the practitioner to withstand powerful physical attacks with minimal damage. Heat, cold, and harsh environments become easier to endure, while wounds close much faster than those of an ordinary cultivator.","---","Fifth Stage – Diamond Marrow","The marrow is reborn, producing blood infused with extraordinary vitality. The practitioner’s regenerative abilities improve dramatically, physical endurance reaches an exceptional level, and aging slows considerably. Most poisons become incapable of causing lasting harm.","---","Sixth Stage – Bodhisattva Heart","The practitioner’s heart and mind become as unshakable as a mountain. Fear, intimidation, and many forms of mental interference lose their effect. Rather than weakening the practitioner, pain sharpens their focus and strengthens their resolve in battle.","---","Seventh Stage – Eternal Vajra Body","The body reaches a level of resilience where ordinary weapons and techniques struggle to inflict meaningful damage. Even grievous injuries no longer significantly reduce combat ability, and lost flesh or damaged limbs can slowly regenerate over time.","---","Eighth Stage – Nirvana Rebirth","Every brush with death becomes an opportunity for rebirth. The practitioner recovers from devastating injuries at miraculous speeds, and each recovery permanently strengthens every aspect of the body. Their lifespan expands greatly, and the body continues evolving after every life-threatening ordeal.","---","Ninth Stage – Eternal Buddha Body","The practitioner’s body ascends beyond mortal limitations, becoming an indestructible vessel tempered through endless suffering. Pain is instantly transformed into overwhelming vitality, regeneration, and strength. The flesh, bones, blood, and even the soul possess extraordinary durability, making the practitioner nearly impossible to kill. As long as they are not completely annihilated, they can recover from almost any injury, and every hardship they endure permanently increases their power without a true limit."]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48 | Five Years Cultivation","paragraphs":["That night, the small bungalow was unusually quiet.","Dexter had already returned to his room, and the girls had also settled into theirs. The house was no longer the cold, lonely place it had been just a few days ago. Through his newly awakened Enhanced Hearing, he could hear the faint, steady rhythm of breathing coming from the room opposite his own. The three women had entered their nightly cultivation. It was peaceful.","Dexter remained seated on his airbed for a few moments. The mattress shifted slightly under his weight. He took a deep breath, but instead of lying down to sleep, he suddenly stood up.","There was still one very important thing left to do.","He stepped out into the dark hallway. Opposite his room was the girls’ room, its door closed completely shut. He paused and glanced at it briefly. He remembered how helpless they had looked when the Ashford family butler had dumped them here with just an old key and ten thousand dollars. He would not let them be helpless again.","Dexter walked quietly toward the living room and reached into his system’s storage space. A small, magical paper appeared in his hand.","It was the Type-5 House Protection Talisman.","The talisman itself was only the size of his palm. However, it felt heavy with power. It was covered in countless silver runes that glowed faintly, looking like tiny stars trapped beneath the surface of the paper.","Dexter looked around the dim living room for a suitable hiding place. His eyes scanned the old furniture, the peeling wallpaper, and the worn-out floorboards. Eventually, his gaze landed on the decorative rug positioned right beneath the center table.","\"Perfect,\" he whispered to himself.","He carefully lifted the heavy wooden center table and pushed it aside. Then, he folded back the edge of the dusty rug. He placed the glowing talisman flat against the cold floor before covering it up once more. He dragged the table back to its original position, making sure everything looked exactly as it had before.","No one would ever think to look there.","The moment the heavy rug settled back into place—","Buzz!","A faint, warm ripple spread outward from beneath the floorboards. An invisible wave expanded through the living room, rushing through the hallway, and passing through every wall, every window, and every dark corner of the property.","For a brief moment, Dexter felt as though an enormous, transparent glass dome had formed around the entire house. It shimmered in the dark before disappearing completely from sight.","The barrier had activated.","A wide smile appeared on Dexter’s face. With this powerful talisman protecting the house, ordinary street thugs like Kreg and his men would never be able to force their way inside again. Even professional, highly trained assassins would find it nearly impossible to sneak into the bungalow unnoticed.","Not only would the barrier block unauthorized entry, but it would also hide the house from magical detection techniques. Best of all, it would immediately send a warning straight to Dexter’s mind if anyone even tried to breach the perimeter.","For the first time since moving to this broken-down house, he felt completely relieved. He let out a long breath.","\"Now they’re safe.\"","Satisfied with the security, Dexter returned to his small bedroom and closed the wooden door gently behind him. Only then did his thoughts drift toward another mysterious item resting quietly inside his system storage.","The Primordial Beast Egg.","The egg was incredibly ancient. It looked like a stone that had survived for millions of years. Even the all-knowing system itself hadn’t revealed what kind of species it belonged to. Its only instruction had been very simple:","> [Cultivate beside the egg and it will eventually hatch.]","Dexter strongly considered taking it out and gicing the girls to cultivate with because it would be faster to make it hatch with three of them cultivating it but he quickly abandoned the idea.","If the girls saw a massive, glowing egg sitting in the house, they would naturally ask questions. He couldn’t answer those questions without revealing his system.","Instead, a much better idea formed in his mind.","When coming back from the Hero Association, he could pretend to have found it and bought it.","It was a believable excuse for bringing a giant egg into the house first.","His thoughts shifted again. This time, he thought about the Talent Upgrade Cards.","Currently, only Mira’s dormant talent had surfaced. She possessed the Spectral Arm Talent. Using the upgrade card, he could immediately raise her talent from D-Rank up to C-Rank.","Unfortunately, Lyra and Selene’s hidden talents had not yet shown themselves.","There was no point in rushing the upgrade.","He would simply wait until their new abilities surfaced naturally before making his move. Patience was also a form of investment.","His thoughts then drifted to the Five Years of Cultivation Reward","Dexter then turned his attention entirely inward.","His mana affinity had already risen to the legendary SS-Rank. Even now, while he was just standing there without actively cultivating, mana continuously flowed into his body from the surrounding air.","The difference was almost absurd. He remembered his past life clearly. Back when he possessed a trash F-Rank affinity, absorbing mana had been like trying to catch a slippery fish with greasy hands.","Now? It felt as though the entire world itself was pouring a waterfall of mana directly into his veins. The sensation was absolutely intoxicating.","Dexter sat down cross-legged on his soft airbed. His Flame Demon Bloodline had evolved, making his physical body had transformed into something much stronger. His physical strength had increased several times over.","But before checking his status screen to see his new numbers, there was one major reward he wanted to claim first.","The Five Years of Cultivation Reward.","Dexter slowly closed his eyes and entered a deep state of meditation. His breathing slowed down to a steady rhythm. His racing thoughts calmed into a quiet pool. One minute later, after completely entering his focused cultivation state, he spoke quietly into the empty room.","\"System.\"","[Ding!]","\"I accept the Five Years Cultivation Reward.\"","For a brief, agonizing moment—nothing happened.","Then—","BOOM!!","A massive tsunami of pure, liquid mana erupted from deep within his body. It felt as though a gigantic, heavy dam had burst open somewhere inside his chest. Mana flooded every single meridian, every major organ, and every tiny cell in his body.","Surprisingly, there was absolutely no pain. The energy was powerful beyond human imagination, but it was also strangely gentle."]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49 | Super-Human Hero Breakthrough!","paragraphs":["Surprisingly, there was absolutely no pain. The energy was powerful beyond human imagination, but it was also strangely gentle and incredibly warm.","It surged through his body like an endless, glowing river, strengthening everything it touched. His cultivation level began rising rapidly, breaking past his previous limits.","Eleventh Stage...","Twelfth Stage...","He crossed into the Twelfth Stage of the Awakened Realm almost instantly. But the incoming energy didn’t stop there. Instead, it began stabilizing his core and refining his foundation, making it thick and unbreakable.","Initial Twelfth Stage.","Middle Twelfth Stage.","Late Twelfth Stage.","Peak Twelfth Stage.","Peak...","Peak...","Peak...","Eventually—","Crack!","A massive barrier inside his soul shattered into a million pieces.","At that exact moment, Dexter’s conscious mind was pulled away from his physical body. The bedroom vanished, and he found himself standing in a vast, endless universe of absolute darkness.","Yet, within that dark void, floated two brilliant, glowing stars.","These were his Star Nodes. The two Star Nodes he had ignited through the Limitless Grand Cosmos Scripture shone brilliantly, looking like miniature suns burning within an endless, empty universe. Apart from those two bright stars, everything else remained completely empty.","Then, suddenly—","A gigantic structure appeared between the two suns. It resembled an enormous strand of human DNA, but twisted into a cosmic helix.","The massive structure was divided into twelve distinct segments. Each segment was connected to the next while remaining clearly separated.","All twelve segments were gray. Silent. Lifeless. Ancient.","The leftover mana from the five years of cultivation quickly surged into this dark universe and slammed directly into the first segment of the helix.","All twelve segments were currently gray, silent, and lifeless, looking like ancient stone.","Suddenly, a tear opened in the dark space, and the massive pool of mana from his five years of cultivation poured into this inner universe. A strong pull came from the first gray segment of the helix, sucking the colorful mana inside.","\"WENG!\"","A vibrant, rainbow-colored light flared at the base of the first segment. The dead, gray outer shell began to crack and crumble away, revealing a beautiful, glowing energy beneath.","The light spread rapidly.","Ten percent.","Twenty percent.","Fifty percent.","Eighty percent.","Until finally—","The entire first segment exploded with dazzling, blinding radiance. The dead gray shell shattered completely, revealing the pure power underneath.","Then, something totally unexpected happened. From the bottom end of the first segment, countless multicolored tendrils emerged. They looked like living tree roots, or glowing cosmic tentacles. They stretched outward through the empty space and attached themselves tightly to the second segment.","The moment the connection formed, energy began flowing rapidly.","The second segment lit up in a flash. Gray turned into bright light. Decay turned into vibrant life. The second segment awakened completely. More glowing tendrils erupted from its end. They quickly connected to the third segment.","The process repeated itself. The third segment slowly began to awaken.","Ten percent.","Twenty percent.","Thirty percent.","Until finally, the energy stopped completely.","The third segment had only been partially activated. The massive power of the five years of cultivation had finally been exhausted. Complete silence returned to the cosmic darkness.","Then Dexter opened his real eyes. Golden light flashed brightly through his pupils. Raw power surged aggressively through every inch of his physical body. He slowly clenched his right fist, feeling the air pop around his knuckles.","Finally... he had reached the Superhuman Realm.","Never in his miserable life, when he was treated like a slave by his family, had he imagined reaching this incredible level. Yet, not only had he broken through—he had directly entered the Third Stage of the Superhuman Realm.","The difference between the lower Awakened Realm and the Superhuman Realm was simply overwhelming. Mana flowed through his veins effortlessly, like blood. His muscles had become much denser and heavier. His bones were stronger than steel. Even his skin cells seemed to contain endless, buzzing vitality.","Without even activating his Enhanced Hearing Talent, he could already hear the soft sounds of insects moving within a hundred-meter radius.","His eyesight had sharpened tremendously. Colors appeared brighter, clearer, and much more vibrant.","Even without using his mana to enhance his vision, he could perfectly see a tiny, brown ant crawling along a tiny crack in the far wall. He could distinguish individual, microscopic grains of dust floating slowly through the bedroom air.","It felt as though the entire world had been upgraded to high definition. Everything was more detailed. More alive.","Dexter couldn’t stop smiling.","If he encountered that same Fifth Stage Superhuman assassin from the bridge again—he was absolutely confident he could kill the man with a single, casual strike. No wonder the battle had been so difficult before.","The gap in power between major realms was simply too large. If his current self fought ten versions of his former self... he could probably kill all ten of them within three seconds.","That was the terrifying difference a major realm represented.","Dexter inhaled deeply to calm his racing heart before speaking aloud.","\"System. Open Status.\"","╔═══════════════════════════════╗","10,000x INVESTMENT MULTIPLIER SYSTEM","╚═══════════════════════════════╝","[Name]: Dexter Ashford","[Race]: Human (Berserk Flame Demon Bloodline — Origin Grade)","[Occupation]: Rank 3 Great Grandmaster Food smith(early)","[Mana Affinity]: SS-Rank","[Rank]: Superhuman Hero","[Level]: 3","════════════════════","[Attributes]","════════════════════","Strength: 594","Agility: 580","Physique: 582","Mana: 570","════════════════════","[Talents]","════════════════════","- Enhanced Hearing (D-Rank)","- Alchemist Flame (E-Rank)","- Golden Flame (C-Rank) [Extracted]","- Thunder Manipulation (C-Rank) [Extracted]","════════════════════","[Bloodline]","════════════════════","Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline (Ancient Grade)","...","Dexter leaned his head back slightly against the hard headboard, a deeply satisfied smile appearing on his face.","Although his official cultivation level had only reached the Third Stage of the Superhuman Realm, his actual, raw combat strength was far, far beyond that. According to his own rough estimation, his base physical combat power alone was already perfectly comparable to a Sixth Stage Superhuman Hero.","And if he truly went all out in a fight... if he unleashed his demonic bloodline abilities, his magical talents, and his martial techniques all simultaneously... he could probably fight evenly against Eighth Stage or even Ninth Stage Superhuman Heroes.","The thought alone made his heart race with excitement.","For the very first time in his entire life, he finally possessed enough personal strength to stand proudly on his own two feet, instead of hiding in fear behind others. He no longer needed to lower his head in shame or fear. He no longer needed to watch helplessly as rich families bullied him or the innocent people around him.","He had finally gained the absolute power to protect his new family."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50 | Thunder & Flames","paragraphs":["Dexter slowly exhaled a breath of hot air. Then, his thoughts drifted toward the special rewards he had obtained from killing the assassins earlier. More specifically—their talents.","Two distinct talents had been forcefully extracted from the assassins’ bodies after their deaths by the system.","The first was: [C-Rank Talent: Thunder Manipulation]","The second was: [C-Rank Talent: Golden Flame Manipulation]","Both were pure, highly destructive offensive talents. They were true combat abilities.","Dexter couldn’t hide the bright excitement shining in his eyes.","Until now, almost every single talent he possessed had been purely supportive in nature. They were very useful abilities, certainly. But they did not help him kill his enemies quickly.","But these... these were true deadly talents.","With Thunder Manipulation and Golden Flame Manipulation added to his personal arsenal, Dexter estimated that his overall combat strength could easily rise by another entire major level.","Combined with the brutal, violent nature of his Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline, his full destructive power might even threaten Eleventh Stage or Twelfth Stage Superhuman Heroes.","The thought was completely exhilarating. Finally, he possessed heavy attack methods that were truly worthy of his growing strength.","After calming his wild excitement down slightly, Dexter shifted his attention toward his remaining system rewards. More specifically, the legendary Heavenly Treasures.","One after another, the magical names appeared floating in golden text before him.","* [Origin Sun Fruit]","* [Star Essence Serum]","* [Heavenly Marrow Cleansing Capsule]","* [Millennium Blood Ginseng]","* [Void Spirit Lotus]","Even Dexter couldn’t help inhaling sharply. His eyes went wide.","Each and every one of these rare treasures was worth an absolute fortune. Any single one of them would be more than enough to trigger a bloody gang war among ordinary heroes in the city.","Naturally, he wanted to give all of them directly to the girls.","However... doing so directly would create far too many dangerous questions. Where did he get them? How could an ordinary, newly awakened hero who lived in a rundown bungalow afford ancient treasures that even the most wealthy, powerful noble families struggled to obtain?","No. Handing them over directly would be far too suspicious.","Fortunately, he had another, much safer solution. Dexter smiled cleverly.","He was now a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith. If he carefully incorporated these powerful treasures into his daily medicinal meals and cooked them alongside the precious Diamond Rice, the extreme magical effects of the treasures would become much gentler, easier for their weak bodies to absorb, and far less suspicious. The girls would simply assume that his cooking skills were getting better and that the meals themselves were naturally extraordinary.","The more he thought about this cooking plan, the more excited he became. Tomorrow’s morning cooking session suddenly became something he was desperately looking forward to.","His eyes shifted toward his digital bank account balance.","30,000 Credits.","The money Rachel had promised him for the mission had already successfully arrived in his account. Originally, he had chosen to split his mission rewards evenly between pure money and monster Nexus cores. At the time, he strongly believed the Nexus monster cores would be incredibly useful for buying future cultivation resources.","But now... with his overpowered system by his side, basic cultivation resources were no longer something he desperately lacked. If anything, he almost regretted not taking all the reward in raw money instead.","Still, he quickly shrugged his shoulders. If he found the right underground black market channels later, those monsters Nexus core could likely be sold to other heroes for a much higher cash value than their standard official conversion rate. There was absolutely no need to rush to sell them.","His thoughts quickly shifted toward another, very practical matter. Beds.","The three girls were still sleeping squished together on the large, combined mattress in the main bedroom. Meanwhile, he himself still slept on a cheap, noisy air bed.","With this new money, he could finally purchase some proper, comfortable furniture for the house. He would buy three separate, soft beds for the girls, and one proper, sturdy bed for himself. It was a simple, comfortable, and normal plan. The thought of giving them a normal life made him smile slightly.","Fire and Lightning","Finally, Dexter turned his attention inward once more. He focused entirely on his powerful new bloodline.","A deep, crimson light flickered brightly within his pupils. He slowly, deliberately raised his left hand into the air.","Whoosh!","A thick, blood-red flame instantly appeared, hovering two inches above his palm. The room temperature immediately skyrocketed. The crimson fire danced silently in the dark shadows of the room, twisting and turning like a living, breathing creature.","This was his innate Flame Will. More accurately, this was the pure Flame Will of the Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline.","After evolving from Origin Grade up into Ancient Grade, the difference in the fire was simply overwhelming. The flames were much denser. Much hotter. And incredibly violent. Dexter estimated that these new flames were at least three times stronger than the weak flames he possessed before his bloodline evolved.","He stared deeply at the crimson fire quietly. Its dark color perfectly resembled liquid blood mixed heavily with boiling molten lava. It was beautiful, but incredibly deadly.","Then, Dexter lowered his left hand and raised his right hand.","Crackle!","Violent, bright blue lightning instantly exploded around his fingertips. Wild electric arcs danced across his open palm as the quiet air filled with the sharp, cracking sound of thunder.","[C-Rank Talent: Thunder Manipulation]","The blue lightning twisted and coiled rapidly around his right arm like a nest of living, glowing snakes. Dexter couldn’t hide the deep fascination shining in his eyes. He slowly pointed his index finger toward the bedroom wall.","Crack!","A thin streak of bright lightning shot forward through the air.","Boom!","A small, loud explosion echoed through the quiet room. A tiny, smoking hole appeared perfectly in the wall, while dark black soot spread in a circle around the impact point.","Dexter nodded his head in deep satisfaction. The destructive piercing power of the lightning was exactly what he had expected. Perhaps it was even greater."]}]);
